
    const ALL_STORIES = [{"chapter": 1, "key": "tortoise_and_hare", "titleEn": "The Tortoise and the Hare", "titleJa": "ウサギとカメ", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_tortoise_and_hare.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A proud hare always laughed at a slow tortoise. \"You walk so slowly! Look at me. I am the fastest animal in the forest,\" the hare said.\n\nThe tortoise smiled and answered, \"Let's have a race today. I can run faster than you think.\"\n\nThe hare laughed loudly. \"That is impossible! But okay, let's run.\"\n\nThe race started. The hare ran very fast. Soon, he was far ahead of the tortoise. He looked back and saw no one. \"The tortoise is too slow. I have a lot of time. I will take a short nap under this big tree,\" said the hare. He sat down and fell asleep.\n\nMeanwhile, the tortoise kept walking. He did not stop. He walked step by step.\n\nWhen the hare woke up, the sun was going down. He ran quickly to the finish line. However, the tortoise was already there!\n\nSlow and steady wins the race.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a proud hare was always boasting about his speed to the other animals. He especially enjoyed making fun of a slow tortoise. \"Nobody can beat me because I am the fastest runner in these woods!\" he cried.\n\nTo his surprise, the quiet tortoise replied calmly, \"I accept your challenge. Let's race to the top of the hill.\"\n\nThe hare laughed out loud, believing that victory was already his. As soon as the signal was given, the hare dashed forward and left the tortoise far behind.\n\nAfter running for a while, the hare stopped to look back. The tortoise was moving so slowly that he was barely visible in the distance. \"I have plenty of time before he catches up,\" thought the hare. \"I think I will rest under this shady tree.\" He lay down on the soft grass and soon fell into a deep sleep.\n\nWhile the hare was sleeping, the tortoise continued to walk steadily without stopping.\n\nWhen the hare finally opened his eyes, he saw that the sun was setting. He sprinted toward the finish line as fast as he could. However, the tortoise had already crossed the line and won the race.\n\nPersistence and hard work will always bring success in the end.", "Grade_Pre2": "An arrogant hare was constantly boasting of his extraordinary speed to all the forest creatures. He took particular pleasure in mocking a slow-moving tortoise. \"I challenge anyone in these woods to a race,\" the hare proclaimed arrogantly. \"No one has ever defeated me, nor will anyone ever succeed!\"\n\nMuch to the hare's astonishment, the quiet tortoise stepped forward and replied with composure, \"I accept your challenge. Let us compete to see who reaches the summit of the hill first.\"\n\nAmused by the proposal, the hare agreed immediately, confident of an easy victory. The moment the competition began, the hare accelerated rapidly, leaving his opponent far behind in a cloud of dust.\n\nUpon reaching the midpoint of the course, the hare glanced back and noticed that the tortoise was barely visible in the remote distance. \"It will take him hours to catch up with me,\" reasoned the hare. \"Therefore, I can comfortably enjoy a refreshing nap beneath the oak tree.\" Feeling thoroughly relaxed, he lay down in the shade and fell into a profound slumber.\n\nMeanwhile, the tortoise maintained a slow but steady pace, advancing continuously without a single moment of hesitation.\n\nBy the time the hare finally awoke, twilight had descended upon the forest. Realizing his grave mistake, he sprinted toward the finish line with all his remaining strength. To his utter dismay, however, the tortoise had already crossed the goal and secured a triumphant victory.\n\nSloth and overconfidence lead to ruin, whereas steady perseverance ultimately triumphs over natural talent.", "Grade_2": "A notoriously boastful hare perpetually ridiculed the sluggish movement of a tortoise, repeatedly asserting his own unexcelled swiftness before the woodland community. \"Regardless of who dares to challenge me,\" declared the hare with supreme arrogance, \"my natural velocity remains entirely insurmountable.\"\n\nUnfazed by the hare's pompous declaration, the tortoise calmly offered a counter-proposal. \"Notwithstanding your remarkable speed, I am prepared to engage in a competitive race to the designated hilltop.\"\n\nDeeming the challenge absurdly amusing, the hare readily accepted, anticipating an inevitable triumph. At the commencement of the race, the hare burst forward with extraordinary acceleration, swiftly establishing a formidable lead that rendered his competitor virtually invisible.\n\nHaving traversed half the distance in mere minutes, the hare paused to assess his progress. Perceiving that the tortoise was lagging far behind, the hare succumbed to complacency. \"Inasmuch as the gap between us is immense,\" he calculated, \"a temporary respite will in no way compromise my impending victory.\" Consequently, he reclined beneath the dense foliage of a venerable oak and lapsed into an unalterable sleep.\n\nIn sharp contrast, the tortoise exhibited unwavering determination. Advancing with relentless continuity, he traversed the rugged terrain without succumbing to fatigue or distraction.\n\nWhen the hare eventually awakened, nightfall was imminently approaching. Panic-stricken upon discovering the tortoise's proximity to the finish line, the hare exerted his maximum capacity in a desperate pursuit. Nevertheless, his delayed effort proved futile; the tortoise had already crossed the boundary, securing an unprecedented triumph.\n\nIndolence and unwarranted self-assurance inevitably culminate in failure, whereas relentless perseverance consistently surpasses raw talent.", "Grade_Pre1": "An ostentatious hare habitually demeaned the sluggish gait of a tortoise, relentlessly proclaiming his own athletic preeminence to the forest fauna. \"Should any creature presume to contest my velocity,\" the hare boasted with pompous disdain, \"such an endeavor is preordained to fail, for my swiftness is fundamentally unassailable.\"\n\nImpervious to the hare's supercilious bravado, the tortoise articulated a measured proposition. \"Notwithstanding your heralded agility, I hereby challenge you to a footrace terminating at the mountain summit.\"\n\nDeriding the proposal as a preposterous delusion, the hare acquiesced with patronizing enthusiasm. Upon the signal, the hare bounded forth with phenomenal momentum, establishing a colossal chasm between himself and his adversary within seconds.\n\nHaving covered half the course, the hare paused to survey the distance. Observing the tortoise far in the rear, the hare succumbed to fatalistic complacency. \"Given the insurmountable magnitude of my lead,\" he rationalized, \"a brief interlude of slumber shall not jeopardize my triumph.\" Whereupon, he sought refuge beneath a canopy of leaves and lapsed into a profound coma.\n\nConversely, the tortoise displayed unyielding tenacity. Maintaining an unhurried yet unrelenting cadence, he negotiated the treacherous incline without a single moment of hesitation.\n\nBy the time the hare emerged from his torpor, twilight had enveloped the horizon. Espying his rival adjacent to the finish line, the hare sprinted with frenecy; nevertheless, his belated surge proved entirely ineffectual. The tortoise had already crossed the threshold, achieving an historic victory.\n\nHaughty indolence and premature triumph subvert inherent superiority, whereas steadfast tenacity inexorably eclipses uncultivated genius.", "Classic_Original": "A Hare was one day making fun of the short feet and slow pace of the Tortoise, who retorted: \"Though you be swift as the wind, I will beat you in a race.\" The Hare, believing her assertion to be simply impossible, agreed to the proposal; and they agreed that the Fox should choose the course and fix the goal. On the day appointed for the race the two started together. The Tortoise never for a moment stopped, but went on with a slow but steady pace straight to the end of the course. The Hare, lying down by the wayside, fell asleep. At last waking up, and moving as fast as he could, he saw the Tortoise had reached the goal, and was comfortably resting after her fatigue.\n\nSlow and steady wins the race.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 2, "key": "boy_who_cried_wolf", "titleEn": "The Boy Who Cried Wolf", "titleJa": "オオカミ少年", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_boy_who_cried_wolf.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A young shepherd boy watched his sheep on a hill near a village. He felt bored every day. One day, he decided to play a trick.\n\nHe ran down to the village and shouted, \"Wolf! Wolf! A wolf is chasing my sheep!\"\n\nThe villagers stopped working and ran up the hill to help him. But when they arrived, there was no wolf. The boy laughed at them. The villagers were angry and returned to their work.\n\nA few days later, the boy shouted \"Wolf!\" again. The villagers ran to help him, but it was another lie.\n\nThen, one evening, a real wolf appeared from the forest. It attacked the sheep. The boy cried loudly, \"Help! A real wolf is here!\"\n\nHowever, no one came to help. The villagers thought, \"He is lying again.\" The wolf killed many sheep.\n\nA liar is not believed even when he tells the truth.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a young shepherd boy was guarding his flock of sheep on a hill outside a small village. Because his job was very quiet, he often felt bored. One afternoon, he decided to play a trick on the villagers to entertain himself.\n\nHe ran toward the village and shouted as loudly as he could, \"Wolf! Wolf! A wolf is attacking my sheep!\"\n\nHearing his cries, the villagers dropped their work and hurried up the hill to protect the sheep. However, when they arrived, they found no wolf at all. The boy laughed heartily at their shocked faces. The villagers were very upset with him and went back to their work.\n\nA few days later, the foolish boy played the same trick again, and once more the villagers came running only to be fooled.\n\nFinally, a real wolf emerged from the dark woods and began to attack the flock. Terrified, the boy screamed, \"Please help! A real wolf is attacking!\"\n\nUnfortunately, nobody responded to his cries because everyone believed that he was lying again. In the end, the wolf destroyed many sheep, and the boy learned a painful lesson.\n\nNobody believes a liar, even when he tells the truth.", "Grade_Pre2": "A bored shepherd boy was tending a flock of sheep on a hillside overlooking a tranquil village. Dissatisfied with his routine responsibilities, he sought a way to create excitement. Consequently, he devised a scheme to deceive the local villagers.\n\nRunning toward the settlement, he shrieked frantically, \"Wolf! A ferocious wolf is attacking the sheep!\"\n\nAlarmed by the distress call, the villagers abandoned their tasks and rushed up the slope to defend the livestock. Upon arriving, however, they discovered no predator. The boy doubled over with laughter at their gullibility. Indignant at his deceit, the villagers scolded him severely before returning to their work.\n\nA few days later, the impudent youth repeated his fake warning, and once again the villagers were tricked into rushing to his aid.\n\nEventually, a ravenous wolf actually emerged from the dark forest and began slaughtering the sheep. Panicked, the boy screamed desperately for assistance.\n\nRegrettably, no one heeded his frantic pleas, assuming it was merely another fabrication. Consequently, the wolf destroyed the entire flock, leaving the boy in deep remorse.\n\nDeceit destroys trust; once credibility is lost, even truth is mistaken for falsehood.", "Grade_2": "A juvenile shepherd tasked with safeguarding a village's livestock was stationed on a solitary hillside adjacent to a dense forest. Growing thoroughly disillusioned with the monotony of his solitary duties, he devised an unethical scheme to alleviate his boredom at the expense of the community.\n\n\"Wolf! A fierce predator is devouring the flock!\" shouted the youth with simulated hysteria.\n\nDistressed by his urgent alarm, the villagers instantaneously suspended their daily labor and ascended the slope, armed with improvised weapons to repel the perceived threat. Upon reaching the pasture, however, they discovered that the crisis was entirely fabricated. The boy stood amidst the grazing sheep, reveling in the success of his deceit. Indignant at his frivolous disregard for their safety, the villagers reprimanded him sternly, warning that civic trust should never be compromised for entertainment.\n\nRegrettably, the boy failed to internalize their caution. Within a week, he fabricated the identical false alarm, causing another unwarranted disruption. Consequently, the villagers' residual trust dissolved entirely into profound skepticism.\n\nSubsequently, a ravenous wolf actually descended from the timberland and launched a violent assault on the herd. Overwhelmed by genuine terror, the youth shouted desperately for assistance. \"I implore you to believe me! A real wolf is slaughtering the livestock!\"\n\nJudging his pleas to be yet another manipulative fabrication, the villagers disregarded his distress signals completely. Deprived of external intervention, the boy watched helplessly as the predator decimated the entire flock.\n\nRepeated dishonesty irreparably erodes personal integrity and public trust; hence, a proven deceiver will be met with skepticism even when uttering the absolute truth.", "Grade_Pre1": "An impetuous young shepherd, commissioned to tend a communal flock on a secluded ridge, succumbed to intense ennui induced by the tedious isolation of his assignment. To break the oppressive monotony, he conceived a malevolent deception, recklessly exploiting the villagers' protective instincts for his own perverse amusement.\n\n\"Wolf! A predatory beast is decimating our livestock!\" he ejaculated with simulated panic.\n\nGalvanized by this alarming outcry, the villagers immediately abandoned their vocations and rushed up the steep terrain, equipped with agricultural implements to neutralize the menace. Upon their arrival, however, the alleged emergency evaporated into a malicious hoax. The youth exulted in his successful manipulation, openly deriding their gullibility. Incensed by his callous breach of communal trust, the elders sternly admonished him, warning that veracity is the indispensable foundation of social cohesion.\n\nNotwithstanding their solemn reproof, the incorrigible youth reiterated the identical subterfuge a fortnight later. This second instance of frivolous duplicity completely eroded whatever vestige of credibility he retained, solidifying a consensus of profound cynicism among the populace.\n\nInevitably, a formidable wolf emerged from the forest and commenced a catastrophic slaughter of the helpless flock. Paralyzed by authentic dread, the youth shrieked frantic appeals for succor. \"I beseech your intervention! This is no fabrication!\"\n\nSurmising his frantic supplications to be merely another manifestation of his inveterate deceit, the villagers maintained absolute indifference. Bereft of succor, the youth witnessed the total annihilation of the flock.\n\nPerpetual deceit irreparably subverts personal veracity and communal solidarity; consequently, even authentic testimony from a confirmed impostor will be rejected with unyielding skepticism.", "Classic_Original": "A Shepherd Boy, who watched a flock of sheep near a village, brought out the villagers three or four times by crying out, \"Wolf! Wolf!\" and when his neighbors came to help him, laughed at them for their pains. The Wolf, however, did truly come at last. The Shepherd-boy, now really alarmed, shouted in an agony of apprehension: \"Pray, come and help me; the Wolf is killing the sheep\"; but no one paid the least heed to his cries, nor rendered any assistance. The Wolf, having no cause of fear, at his leisure lacerated or destroyed the whole flock.\n\nThere is no believing a liar, even when he speaks the truth.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 3, "key": "north_wind_and_sun", "titleEn": "The North Wind and the Sun", "titleJa": "北風と太陽", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_north_wind_and_sun.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "The North Wind and the Sun were arguing about who was stronger. Just then, they saw a traveler walking down the road. He was wearing a warm coat.\n\n\"Look,\" said the Wind. \"Let's see who can take off his coat first.\"\n\nThe Wind blew hard. Cold air rushed across the land. But the harder he blew, the more tightly the man held his coat. Finally, the Wind stopped blowing because he was tired.\n\nNext, it was the Sun's turn. The Sun smiled and began to shine brightly. Soon, the day became very warm. The traveler felt hot, took off his coat, and sat under a tree to rest.\n\nKindness is stronger than anger.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a fierce argument arose between the North Wind and the Sun over which of them was stronger. While they were arguing, they noticed a traveler walking along a country road, wrapped in a heavy cloak.\n\n\"I have an idea,\" proposed the Wind. \"The one who can force that traveler to take off his cloak shall be the winner.\"\n\nThe Wind began to blow as hard as he could. Icy air rushed across the field. However, the harder he blew, the more tightly the traveler wrapped the cloak around his body. In the end, the Wind gave up in despair.\n\nThen, the Sun stepped forward and shone warmly upon the earth. Within a few minutes, the traveler felt so hot that he could no longer bear his heavy cloak. He happily took it off and sat down under a shady tree.\n\nGentleness and warm words can accomplish more than force.", "Grade_Pre2": "A fierce dispute arose between the North Wind and the Sun over which of them possessed greater strength. Unable to resolve the conflict through words alone, they agreed to test their power upon a solitary traveler walking along a country highway, wrapped tightly in a heavy cloak.\n\n\"I propose a test,\" declared the North Wind arrogantly. \"Whichever of us compels that traveler to strip off his cloak shall be recognized as the undisputed victor.\"\n\nAccepting the challenge, the North Wind initiated the contest by unleashing a furious blast of arctic air. However, the more violently he blew, the more tightly the traveler wrapped the cloak around his body to protect himself from the piercing cold. Exhausted from his strenuous efforts, the Wind ultimately yielded in despair.\n\nThen, the Sun took his turn, gently beaming warm solar rays upon the earth. Within a few moments, the temperature rose rapidly, making the traveler feel increasingly uncomfortable in his heavy garment. Unable to tolerate the intense warmth any longer, he willingly removed his cloak and sought refuge under the soothing shade of a tree.\n\nPersuasion and gentleness are vastly more effective than brute force and hostility.", "Grade_2": "A fierce contest for supremacy erupted between the North Wind and the Sun, each asserting absolute dominance over the natural elements. To resolve their intractable conflict, they agreed to abide by an objective trial of strength.\n\nSpotting a solitary traveler traversing a mountain path enveloped in a heavy winter garment, the North Wind proposed a definitive criterion. \"Whichever of us compels that traveler to divest himself of his cloak shall be conceded the title of supreme power.\"\n\nConcurring with the terms, the Sun yielded the initial attempt. Instantly, the North Wind unleashed a ferocious gale, howling across the terrain with violent velocity. Contrary to his expectations, however, the relentless onslaught merely impelled the traveler to grasp his attire with redoubled firmness to shield himself from the tempestuous climate. Despite exerting his maximum capacity, the Wind's aggressive tactics proved entirely counterproductive.\n\nThereupon, the Sun emerged, radiating mild and soothing warmth across the atmosphere. Gradually escalating the solar intensity, he transformed the frigid environment into a pleasant climate. Overwhelmed by the mounting heat, the traveler voluntarily unfastened his heavy garment and discarded it beside the pathway.\n\nCoercion and hostility inevitably breed resistance, whereas gentle persuasion and warmth consistently prevail over brute force.", "Grade_Pre1": "An unyielding hegemony dispute materialized between the North Wind and the Sun, both claiming absolute sovereignty over the atmospheric realm. To adjudicate their intractable rivalry, they pledged to submit to an empirical test of efficacy.\n\nObserving a solitary wayfarer negotiating an exposed ridge wrapped in a heavy mantle, the North Wind stipulated the precise challenge. \"Whichever entity forces that traveler to strip off his garment shall be acknowledged as possessing paramount potency.\"\n\nAssenting to the protocol, the Sun granted priority to his adversary. Instantly, the North Wind generated a tempestuous blizzard, unleashing furious gusts designed to tear the cloak away. Contrary to his calculation, the belligerent assault merely impelled the wayfarer to clutch his garment with desperate tenacity to ward off the hypothermic peril. Notwithstanding his maximum expenditure of force, the Wind's coercive methodology produced an entirely antithetical outcome.\n\nWhereupon, the Sun stepped forth, diffusing benevolent warmth throughout the biosphere. Incrementally augmenting the thermal emission, he ameliorated the hostile atmosphere. Incapable of enduring the mounting solar radiance, the traveler voluntarily shed his burdensome attire and rested in the shade.\n\nBrutal coercion and aggressive hostility inexorably provoke intransigent resistance, whereas subtle benevolence and persuasive warmth invariably vanquish raw force.", "Classic_Original": "The North Wind and the Sun had a contest to decide which was the stronger. To settle the matter, they agreed to test their strength upon a traveler who was walking down the road wrapped in a warm cloak. Whichever of them could make him take his cloak off first was to be accounted the victor.\n\nThe North Wind blew with all his might, but the harder he blew, the more closely did the traveler wrap his cloak around him, till at last the North Wind gave up the attempt in despair.\n\nThen the Sun shone out warmly, and immediately the traveler took off his cloak.\n\nPersuasion is better than force.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 4, "key": "lion_and_mouse", "titleEn": "The Lion and the Mouse", "titleJa": "ライオンとネズミ", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_lion_and_mouse.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A big lion was sleeping under a tree. Suddenly, a little mouse ran over his face. The lion woke up and caught the mouse with his big paw.\n\n\"Please don't eat me!\" squeaked the mouse. \"If you let me go, I will help you someday.\"\n\nThe lion laughed. \"How can a little mouse help a big lion?\" But he was kind and let the mouse go free.\n\nA few weeks later, some hunters caught the lion in a heavy net. The lion roared loudly because he could not move.\n\nThe mouse heard the roar and ran to the lion. He used his sharp teeth to chew the ropes. Soon, the lion was free.\n\n\"Thank you,\" said the lion.\n\nEven a small friend can be a great help.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a mighty lion was sleeping peacefully under a shaded tree. Suddenly, a tiny mouse ran across his nose and woke him up. Furious at being disturbed, the lion caught the creature under his huge paw.\n\n\"Please spare my life!\" begged the mouse. \"If you set me free, I promise to return your kindness in the future.\"\n\nThe lion laughed out loud, wondering how such a tiny creature could ever assist the king of beasts. However, feeling generous, he decided to let the mouse go.\n\nA few weeks later, the lion was caught in a hunter's strong net. Unable to break free, he roared in anger and distress.\n\nHearing the familiar sound, the little mouse rushed to the scene. He quickly began to chew through the thick ropes with his sharp teeth. Before long, the net fell apart, and the lion was rescued.\n\n\"You laughed at me before, but now you see that even a mouse can help a lion,\" smiled the little mouse.\n\nLittle friends may prove to be great friends.", "Grade_Pre2": "A majestic lion was resting quietly in his forest domain when an unsuspecting mouse accidentally ran across his paw. Enraged by the sudden disturbance, the monarch of the jungle seized the tiny intruder, preparing to crush him without hesitation.\n\n\"I implore you to grant me mercy!\" pleaded the mouse trembling with fear. \"Should you spare my life, I assure you that I shall express my gratitude whenever you require assistance.\"\n\nAmused by the absurd notion that a helpless rodent could render aid to a formidable predator, the lion nevertheless displayed magnanimity and released his prisoner unharmed.\n\nShortly thereafter, a group of cunning hunters trapped the lion within a heavy net suspended from a tree. Immobilized and helpless, the lion roared in profound anguish.\n\nRecognizing the distress call, the mouse hastened to the location. Without a moment's delay, he commenced gnawing diligently through the sturdy ropes with his sharp incisors. Consequently, the bindings severed, and the formidable beast regained his freedom.\n\nRecalling his earlier skepticism, the humbled lion expressed sincere gratitude to his tiny savior.\n\nNo act of kindness, no matter how small, is ever wasted, and even the humblest ally may prove indispensable in times of crisis.", "Grade_2": "A formidable lion, the undisputed monarch of the wilderness, was slumbering in a shaded sanctuary. His tranquility was abruptly shattered when a diminutive mouse inadvertently traversed his face. Provoked by the intrusion, the apex predator instantly pinned the fragile creature beneath his massive paw, intending to execute it summarily.\n\n\"I beseech your Majesty to exercise clemency!\" implored the terrified rodent. \"My transgression was purely accidental. Should you grant me amnesty, I pledge to render reciprocal assistance whenever you encounter adversity.\"\n\nSkepticism and amusement swept over the lion at the absurd proposition that an insignificant creature possessed the capacity to aid a sovereign beast. Nonetheless, moved by a rare impulse of magnanimity, he unclasped his paw and granted the rodent its liberty.\n\nSubsequently, while prowling through the woodland, the lion triggered a sophisticated snare constructed by big-game hunters. Bound securely within heavy cordage, his tremendous physical exertion proved futile, leaving him roaring in profound helplessness.\n\nRecognizing the vocalization of distress, the mouse promptly navigated toward the source. Demonstrating remarkable ingenuity and perseverance, the rodent methodically severed the fibrous strands with its sharp incisors, ultimately liberating the trapped monarch.\n\nNo creature is so humble as to be devoid of utility; hence, acts of benevolence frequently yield unforeseen dividends in moments of acute crisis.", "Grade_Pre1": "A colossal lion, the unchallenged sovereign of the veldt, reposed within a secluded copse. This serene repose was rudely disrupted when an infinitesimal rodent inadvertently scurried across the apex predator's countenance. Incensed by this inadvertent sacrilege, the monarch immobilized the helpless organism beneath his formidable claw, poised to exterminate it without compunction.\n\n\"I implore your Sovereign Highness to extend magnanimous clemency!\" supplicated the quaking rodent. \"My inadvertent trespass bore no malice. Were you to accord me amnesty, I solemnize a vow to reciprocate with commensurate assistance in your hour of peril.\"\n\nDerision and incredulity seized the monarch upon contemplating the preposterous thesis that a paltry rodent could ever succor an omnipotent carnivore. Nevertheless, impelled by a transient whim of regal magnanimity, he disengaged his grip and emancipated the captive.\n\nIn the fullness of time, while negotiating a dense thicket, the lion unwittingly activated an insidious trap devised by big-game poachers. Enmeshed within unyielding netting, his frantic physical exertion produced no mitigation, reducing the sovereign to vocalizing impotent fury.\n\nDiscerning the unmistakable reverberation of anguish, the rodent expeditiously gravitated to the site. Exercising astounding tenacity, the diminutive creature meticulously gnawed through the resilient cordage with razor-sharp incisors, thereby restoring the sovereign's autonomy.\n\nNo entity, regardless of its apparent insignificance, is wholly destitute of efficacy; consequently, altruistic benevolence routinely yields incalculable dividends during times of catastrophic vulnerability.", "Classic_Original": "A Lion was awakened from sleep by a Mouse running over his face. Rising up angrily, he caught him and was about to kill him, when the Mouse piteously entreated, saying: \"If you would only spare my life, I would be sure to repay your kindness.\" The Lion laughed and let him go. It happened shortly after this that the Lion was caught by some hunters, who bound him by strong ropes to the ground. The Mouse, recognizing his roar, came and gnawed the rope with his teeth, and set him free, exclaiming: \"You ridiculed the idea of my ever being able to help you, not expecting to receive from me any requital of your favor; now you know that it is possible for even Mice to confer benefits upon Lions.\"\n\nLittle friends may prove great friends.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 5, "key": "ant_and_grasshopper", "titleEn": "The Ant and the Grasshopper", "titleJa": "アリとキリギリス", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_ant_and_grasshopper.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "During the warm summer, a grasshopper sang and danced all day. He saw a hard-working ant carrying heavy corn to her nest.\n\n\"Why do you work so hard?\" asked the grasshopper. \"Summer is fun! Come and sing with me.\"\n\nThe ant replied, \"I am storing food for the cold winter. You should collect food too.\" But the grasshopper laughed and kept dancing.\n\nSoon, winter came. Snow covered the ground, and there was no food anywhere. The grasshopper was very hungry and cold.\n\nHe went to the ant's house and asked, \"Please give me some food.\"\n\nThe ant asked, \"What did you do during the summer?\"\n\nThe grasshopper answered, \"I sang and danced all summer.\"\n\nThe ant said, \"Then you can dance through the winter!\" And she closed her door.\n\nWork today, and you will have food tomorrow.", "Grade_3": "On a bright summer day, a carefree grasshopper was singing and enjoying music in a green field. Nearby, a group of ants was working tirelessly, gathering grain and carrying it to their underground nest.\n\n\"Why waste such a lovely day working so hard?\" asked the grasshopper. \"Come and join me! We should enjoy the summer.\"\n\nThe wise ant replied, \"I am preparing food for the coming winter, and I advise you to do the same.\" However, the grasshopper ignored her advice and continued to play his music.\n\nWhen winter arrived, freezing winds blew across the land, and snow buried the field. Having stored nothing, the grasshopper found himself starving and shivering from the cold.\n\nIn desperation, he knocked on the ant's door and begged for a small piece of corn.\n\n\"What did you do all summer while we were working?\" asked the ant.\n\n\"I was busy singing,\" replied the grasshopper regretfully.\n\n\"If you were foolish enough to sing all summer, you may dance all winter!\" answered the ant firmly.\n\nIt is wise to prepare today for the needs of tomorrow.", "Grade_Pre2": "Throughout a golden summer afternoon, an indolent grasshopper indulged in melodious music, completely unconcerned with future necessity. In stark contrast, a colony of diligent ants labored unceasingly, transporting heavy grains of wheat to fortify their subterranean pantry.\n\n\"Why exhaust yourselves with such arduous labor during this enchanting season?\" mocked the grasshopper. \"You ought to abandon your toil and participate in my festivities!\"\n\nThe prudent ant paused and replied gravely, \"I am accumulating provisions to survive the inevitable harshness of winter, and I strongly recommend that you pursue a similar strategy.\" Nevertheless, the short-sighted grasshopper dismissed the warning with contempt and persisted in his idle amusements.\n\nEventually, winter descended, covering the countryside with a blanket of ice and snow. Deprived of food and shelter, the impoverished grasshopper found himself suffering acutely from starvation and frostbite.\n\nDriven by sheer desperation, he approached the ant's residence and humbly implored her for a meager portion of grain.\n\n\"How did you spend the summer months while we were diligently storing provisions?\" inquired the ant sternly.\n\n\"Alas, I devoted all my time to song and merriment,\" admitted the grasshopper remorsefully.\n\n\"In that case,\" responded the ant dispassionately, \"since you spent the summer in song, you may spend the winter dancing on an empty stomach.\"\n\nPrudence and foresight ensure survival, whereas negligence and immediate gratification lead inevitably to catastrophe.", "Grade_2": "During the abundant summer months, an industrious colony of ants engaged in meticulous labor, transporting provisions to replenish their subterranean reserves in anticipation of winter's austerity. Each ant labored systematically, prioritizing long-term security over immediate gratification.\n\nIn stark contrast, an indolent grasshopper squandered the season in frivolous amusement, playing melodies and indulging in fleeting pleasures. Observing the ants' grueling exertions, the grasshopper derided their foresight. \"Why dedicate these idyllic days to relentless toil?\" he inquired dismissively. \"Present abundance renders such arduous preparation entirely superfluous.\"\n\nA pragmatic ant admonished him gravely, \"We are systematically accumulating reserves to withstand the inevitable scarcity of winter. Prudence dictates that you likewise initiate preparations.\" Unmoved by this pragmatic counsel, the grasshopper persisted in his short-sighted hedonism.\n\nWith the onset of winter, frigid temperatures devastated the flora, shrouding the countryside in impenetrable snow. Lacking any provisions to sustain himself, the destitute grasshopper suffered severe deprivation. In extreme distress, he appealed to the ants' benevolence, supplicating for a fraction of their surplus grain.\n\nThe ant confronted the petitioner dispassionately. \"How did you utilize your time during the season of abundance?\"\n\n\"I devoted myself entirely to music and merriment,\" admitted the humbled grasshopper.\n\n\"Inasmuch as you sang throughout the summer,\" concluded the ant dispassionately, \"it is appropriate that you dance through the winter.\" With that, the portal was decisively closed.\n\nProvident foresight and disciplined perseverance shield against adversity, whereas reckless short-sightedness culminates in destitute vulnerability.", "Grade_Pre1": "Throughout the vernal season of bounty, an extraordinarily industrious ant commune executed systematic labor, stockpiling agrarian commodities to fortify their subterranean granaries against impending winter privations. Each individual operated with unremitting discipline, subordinating immediate sensory pleasure to long-term institutional survival.\n\nConversely, a hedonistic grasshopper dissipated the temperate months in ostentatious frivolity, orchestrating ephemeral harmonies while indulging in unbridled gratification. Surveying the ants' relentless endeavors, the grasshopper disparaged their strategic foresight. \"Wherefore surrender these pristine days to excruciating labor?\" he postulated derisively. \"Existing plenitude obviates the necessity for such paranoid accumulation.\"\n\nA sagacious ant proffered stern counsel: \"We are methodically amassing sustenance to insulate ourselves against the inevitable ecological austerity of winter. Rational prudence mandates that you promptly emulate our methodology.\" Unswayed by this imperative admonition, the grasshopper persisted in his myopic extravagance.\n\nUpon the inevitable arrival of winter, arctic blizzards decimated the vegetation, paralyzing the ecosystem under a blanket of frost. Bereft of reserves, the impoverished grasshopper experienced acute physiological collapse. Reduced to absolute destitution, he petitioned the ants' altruism, imploring a subsistence ration from their bountiful repository.\n\nThe ant scrutinized the mendicant with icy detachment. \"Wherein lay your endeavors while abundance prevailed?\"\n\n\"I consecrated my existence to artistic expression and melody,\" confessed the chastened grasshopper.\n\n\"Inasmuch as your summer was squandered in vocalization,\" decreed the ant with inexorable logic, \"it is fitting that your winter be consumed in choreographic desperation.\" Whereupon, the barrier was immutably sealed.\n\nProvident stewardship and disciplined frugality constitute an inviolable defense against catastrophe, whereas unbridled short-sightedness inevitably precipitates irreversible vulnerability.", "Classic_Original": "In a field one summer's day a Grasshopper was hopping about, chirping and singing to its heart's content. An Ant passed by, bearing along with great toil an ear of corn he was taking to the nest. \"Why not come and chat with me,\" said the Grasshopper, \"instead of toiling and moiling in that way?\" \"I am helping to lay up food for the winter,\" said the Ant, \"and recommend you to do the same.\" \"Why bother about winter?\" said the Grasshopper; \"we have got plenty of food at present.\" But the Ant went on its way and continued its toil. When the winter came the Grasshopper had no food and found itself dying of hunger, while it saw the ants distributing every day corn and grain from the stores they had collected in the summer. Then the Grasshopper knew:\n\nIt is best to prepare for the days of necessity.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 6, "key": "fox_and_grapes", "titleEn": "The Fox and the Grapes", "titleJa": "キツネとブドウ", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_fox_and_grapes.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "One hot summer afternoon, a hungry fox walked through a farm. He saw some beautiful purple grapes hanging high on a tree.\n\n\"I am so thirsty and hungry,\" thought the fox. \"Those grapes look delicious.\"\n\nHe walked back a few steps and jumped high in the air. But he missed the grapes.\n\nHe tried again and again, but the grapes were too high.\n\nFinally, the fox was tired. He stopped jumping and looked at the grapes.\n\n\"I don't need those grapes,\" he said, turning his nose up. \"I am sure they are sour and bad to eat.\"\n\nThen he walked away calmly.\n\nIt is easy to dislike what you cannot get.", "Grade_3": "On a scorching summer afternoon, a hungry fox was wandering through an orchard in search of food. Suddenly, he noticed a bunch of ripe, juicy purple grapes hanging from a high branch.\n\n\"Those grapes look delicious, and they will surely satisfy my thirst,\" said the fox to himself.\n\nHe took a few steps back, ran forward, and leaped as high as he could into the air. However, he missed the grapes by a few inches.\n\nRefusing to give up, the fox tried several times, but the grapes remained far beyond his reach.\n\nExhausted from his repeated efforts, he finally realized that his attempts were useless. Walking away with his nose in the air, he remarked coldly, \"They are probably sour anyway, and I have no interest in eating sour fruit.\"\n\nIt is easy to despise what you cannot obtain.", "Grade_Pre2": "During a sultry midsummer afternoon, a famished fox wandered aimlessly through a sun-drenched vineyard seeking sustenance. Unexpectedly, his gaze fell upon a luscious cluster of dark grapes dangling temptingly from a high trellis.\n\n\"What a magnificent prize!\" exclaimed the fox, his mouth watering in anticipation. \"That sweet nectar will unquestionably alleviate my extreme thirst.\"\n\nStepping back a considerable distance to gain momentum, he sprinted forward and bounded into the air with all his agility. Regrettably, despite his utmost effort, he fell short of the prize by mere centimeters.\n\nUndeterred by his initial failure, the persistent beast repeated the maneuver multiple times, yet the prize remained irrevocably out of reach.\n\nConfronted with physical exhaustion and the futility of his endeavors, the fox eventually abandoned the enterprise. Retreating with an air of deliberate indifference, he declared disdainfully, \"Upon closer inspection, those grapes are manifestly unripened and sour; consequently, they are entirely unworthy of my palate.\"\n\nIt is a common human trait to disparage and belittle whatever rewards lie beyond one's capability to achieve.", "Grade_2": "On an oppressively humid summer afternoon, a famished fox traversed a sun-drenched vineyard in pursuit of sustenance. Suddenly, his gaze was arrested by an exquisite cluster of ripe, succulent grapes suspended from a high trellis. The lustrous purple fruit presented a tantalizing spectacle that immediately stimulated his appetite.\n\n\"That magnificent fruit will undoubtedly alleviate my dehydration,\" the fox reasoned, mesmerized by the prospect of gratification.\n\nGathering momentum, he executed a powerful vertical leap, yet failed to diminish the distance separating him from the reward. Refusing to concede defeat, he retreated a short distance, accelerated rapidly, and launched himself into the air once more. Nevertheless, the grapes remained suspended far beyond his physical reach.\n\nPersisting in his fruitless endeavors, the fox executed numerous frantic attempts, exhausting his physical reserves without achieving the slightest progress. Eventually, recognizing the insurmountable nature of the obstacle, he abandoned his quest with calculated indifference.\n\nAttempting to conceal his humiliation under a facade of disdain, the fox walked away, remarking aloud, \"Upon closer inspection, those grapes are manifestly unpalatable and green. Consuming them would merely induce gastric discomfort.\"\n\nHuman nature frequently resort to psychological rationalization, disparaging unattainable objectives to preserve self-esteem in the face of failure.", "Grade_Pre1": "Amid the torrid intensity of a midsummer afternoon, a ravenous vulpine prowled through an opulent vineyard seeking caloric sustenance. Without warning, his optic focus converged upon an opulent cluster of translucent grapes suspended from an elevated arbor. The luminescent purple spheres presented a tantalizing aesthetic that instantly ignited his carnivorous desire.\n\n\"That celestial nectar shall forthwith extinguish my acute dehydration,\" the vulpine postulated, spellbound by the illusion of imminent satiety.\n\nGenerating kinetic momentum, he executed an athletic leap, yet failed to bridge the spatial interval partitioning him from the prize. Repudiating instantaneous failure, he withdrew several paces, accelerated with maximum velocity, and vaulted skyward anew. Notwithstanding his strenuous exertion, the fruit remained tantalizingly beyond his anatomical reach.\n\nPerspervering in these redundant exertions, the vulpine conducted repeated futile ascents, completely depleting his muscular energy without mitigating the spatial disparity. Ultimately comprehending the absolute impossibility of the endeavor, he relinquished the enterprise with an air of artificial disdain.\n\nEndeavoring to obfuscate his profound humiliation beneath a veneer of aristocratic contempt, the vulpine departed, pronouncing loudly: \"A rigorous scrutiny reveals that those berries are palpably astringent and unripe. Their ingestion would inevitably precipitate severe gastrointestinal distress.\"\n\nConfronted by insurmountable defeat, human cognition compulsively invokes psychological rationalization, denigrating unachievable imperatives to safeguard vulnerable ego-integrity.", "Classic_Original": "One hot summer's day a Fox was strolling through an orchard till he came to a bunch of Grapes just ripening on a vine which had been trained over a lofty branch. \"Just the thing to quench my thirst,\" quoth he. Drawing back a few paces, he took a run and a jump, and just missed the bunch. Turning round again with a One, Two, Three, he jumped up, but with no greater success. Again and again he tried after the tempting morsel, but at last had to give it up, and walked away with his nose in the air, saying: \"I am sure they are sour.\"\n\nIt is easy to despise what you cannot get.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 7, "key": "town_mouse_country_mouse", "titleEn": "The Town Mouse and the Country Mouse", "titleJa": "田舎のネズミと街のネズミ", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_town_mouse_country_mouse.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A country mouse invited his friend, a town mouse, to his home. He served simple corn and bread. The town mouse turned up his nose.\n\n\"Your life is so poor,\" said the town mouse. \"Come to the city with me. I have fine cheese and delicious cake every day.\"\n\nThe country mouse agreed and visited the town mouse's big house. The dining table was full of delicious food.\n\nHowever, just as they began to eat, a big cat burst into the room with a loud noise! The two mice ran quickly and hid in a dark hole. They shook with fear.\n\nWhen the cat left, the country mouse packed his bag.\n\n\"I am going home,\" he said. \"I prefer simple food in peace to rich food in fear.\"\n\nPeace and safety are better than luxury with danger.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a country mouse invited his old friend, a town mouse, to visit his humble home in the fields. The country mouse offered simple meals such as dried beans and wheat. The town mouse tasted a little and complained politely.\n\n\"My friend, your food is so plain and your life is so quiet,\" said the town mouse. \"You must come to the city with me to enjoy luxury and fine dining.\"\n\nCurious, the country mouse accompanied his friend to a grand mansion in the city. The dining room was filled with delicious cakes, fruit, and expensive cheese.\n\nHowever, before they could enjoy their meal, the dining room door suddenly opened, and two fierce barking dogs rushed inside. Terrified, both mice sprinted into a narrow hole in the wall, holding their breath in terror.\n\nAs soon as the danger passed, the country mouse said goodbye to his friend.\n\n\"You may have luxury in the city,\" he said, \"but I prefer my simple life in peace and safety.\"\n\nA humble life in peace is better than a luxurious life in fear.", "Grade_Pre2": "A hospitable country mouse extended an invitation to his urban acquaintance, a town mouse, to experience rustic life in his subterranean burrow. The host served modest fare consisting of wheat stalks, wild roots, and dry acorns. The urban guest sampled the meal reluctantly, unable to conceal his disdain for such unrefined food.\n\n\"My esteemed friend,\" remarked the town mouse patronizingly, \"how can you tolerate such a dreary existence? If you accompany me to the metropolis, you shall partake in lavish banquets every evening.\"\n\nEnticed by the prospect of extravagance, the naive country mouse agreed to the journey. Upon arriving at an opulent urban residence, he was astounded by the banquet table, which groaned under the weight of exquisite pastries, delicate jellies, and imported cheeses.\n\nHowever, just as they prepared to indulge, the double doors flew open violently, and two terrifying hounds burst into the chamber, barking fiercely. Overwhelmed by panic, the mice scrambled frantically into a tight crevice within the woodwork, trembling in mortal fear.\n\nOnce quietude was restored to the room, the country mouse promptly retrieved his travel pouch.\n\n\"You may retain your opulence and sophisticated delicacies,\" he observed wisely, \"for I would far rather enjoy frugal meals in tranquility than feast sumptuously under the constant shadow of mortal peril.\"\n\nSecurity and peace of mind in modest circumstances are vastly preferable to affluence plagued by anxiety and danger.", "Grade_2": "A rural rodent maintained a frugal yet tranquil existence within a secluded agrarian habitat. On one occasion, he extended hospitality to his urban cousin, welcoming him to his unpretentious burrow. The host presented a modest fare comprising rustic roots, wild berries, and unrefined grains.\n\nSampling the coarse sustenance with visible distaste, the urban visitor voiced his disdain. \"My esteemed relative,\" he remarked condescendingly, \"your lifestyle is defined by unnecessary austerity. In the metropolis, I habitually partake of opulent banquets. I urge you to accompany me to the urban center to taste genuine affluence.\"\n\nEnticed by visions of sensory indulgence, the rural rodent acquiesced to the invitation. Upon arriving at an opulent metropolitan mansion under cover of darkness, the host escorted his guest to a dining hall overflowing with gourmet delicacies, including imported cheeses and exquisite confections.\n\nHowever, precisely as the guest prepared to sample the extravagant feast, the sanctuary was abruptly breached. Two menacing hounds stormed the chamber, their ferocious barking echoing off the marble walls. Panic-stricken, the rodents scrambled into a precarious crevice to evade imminent destruction.\n\nOnce tranquility was restored, the rural rodent promptly announced his intention to return to his homeland. \"While your environment offers unparalleled luxury, it is inextricably bound to perpetual jeopardy. I firmly elect a modest existence safeguarded by serenity over perilous opulence.\"\n\nA humble lifestyle accompanied by peace and security is immeasurably superior to luxurious affluence burdened by perpetual anxiety and mortal hazard.", "Grade_Pre1": "A pastoral rodent maintained an austere yet serene existence within a sequestered agricultural sanctuary. On a particular occasion, he proffered hospitality to his cosmopolitan kinsman, receiving him into his unostentatious subterranean domicile. The host proffered a rudimentary repast consisting of uncultivated tubers, indigenous berries, and unprocessed cereals.\n\nPartaking of this primitive nourishment with unabashed aversion, the cosmopolitan guest articulated profound condescension. \"My cherished kinsman,\" he declared patronizingly, \"your existence is characterized by unmitigated deprivation. Within the metropolis, I habitually revel in opulent culinary extravaganzas. I implore you to migrate with me to the urban epicenter to experience authentic prosperity.\"\n\nBeguiled by prospects of hedonistic gratification, the pastoral rodent acceded to the proposition. Under the cloak of nocturnal obscurity, they penetrated a lavish metropolitan estate, where the host conducted his guest to a banqueting hall laden with epicurean delicacies.\n\nNevertheless, at the exact juncture when the visitor prepared to partake of the sumptuous banquet, the domestic sanctuary was violently compromised. Two formidable canine predators invaded the precinct, their guttural growls reverberating throughout the marble rotunda. Terror-stricken, the rodents executed a chaotic retreat into a subterranean fissure to avert impending annihilation.\n\nUpon the restoration of equilibrium, the pastoral rodent unequivocally declared his immediate repatriation. \"Notwithstanding the undeniable grandeur of your urban paradise, it is inextricably tethered to chronic peril. I unhesitatingly prioritize an unpretentious existence anchored in tranquility over a perilous affluence fraught with mortality.\"\n\nAn unpretentious lifestyle fortified by tranquility and physical security is infinitely preferable to ostentatious affluence inextricably encumbered by perpetual trepidation and existential threat.", "Classic_Original": "A Country Mouse invited a Town Mouse to dinner. The Country Mouse produced wheat stalks, roots, and acorns. The Town Mouse refused to eat them, saying: \"I cannot understand, my friend, how you can put up with such poor food as this. Come with me to the city, and you shall enjoy a feast.\" So they set off together. Arriving at the city house late at night, the Town Mouse showed his friend a rich spread of pastries, jellies, and cheese. But just as they began to eat, the door suddenly flew open, and a huge cat bounded in with a roar. Both mice scampered off to a tiny hole in the wall, trembling with fright. As soon as the room was quiet again, the Country Mouse took his leave, saying: \"Good-bye, my friend. You have luxury and rich dainties, but they are accompanied by fear and danger. I prefer my simple food in safety.\"\n\nPoverty with security is better than plenty in the midst of fear and uncertainty.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 8, "key": "crow_and_pitcher", "titleEn": "The Crow and the Pitcher", "titleJa": "カラスと水つぼ", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_crow_and_pitcher.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A thirsty crow flew all over the field looking for water. Finally, he found a tall pitcher with a little water at the bottom.\n\nHe tried to drink, but the neck of the pitcher was too narrow. His beak could not reach the water.\n\n\"I am so thirsty! What should I do?\" thought the crow.\n\nHe looked around and saw many small stones on the ground. Suddenly, he had a good idea.\n\nHe picked up the stones one by one with his beak and dropped them into the pitcher.\n\nSlowly, the water level rose to the top. The crow drank the cool water happily and saved his life.\n\nLittle by little does the trick.", "Grade_3": "During a hot summer drought, a thirsty crow flew across the dry countryside searching for water to drink. At last, he discovered a tall clay pitcher containing a small amount of water at the bottom.\n\nHe eagerly thrust his beak into the pitcher, but the neck was far too narrow. Try as he might, he could not reach the water.\n\nDetermined not to give up, the clever crow thought carefully until he came up with a brilliant plan.\n\nHe began picking up small pebbles from the ground one by one and dropping them into the pitcher. With each pebble he dropped, the water level slowly rose higher.\n\nAfter dropping dozens of pebbles, the water finally reached the top. The crow was able to quench his thirst and save his own life.\n\nWhere there is a will, there is a way.", "Grade_Pre2": "Amidst a prolonged summer drought, a severely dehydrated crow traversed the arid landscape in search of life-sustaining water. Exhausted and near collapse, he eventually spotted a tall ceramic pitcher standing in a deserted courtyard. Upon investigation, he observed a meager reservoir of water residing at the very bottom.\n\nEagerly inserting his beak into the vessel, he discovered to his dismay that the elongated neck rendered the fluid completely inaccessible. Despite numerous desperate attempts to tilt or fracture the vessel, his physical strength proved insufficient.\n\nRefusing to succumb to despair, the resourceful avian paused to analyze the dilemma. Exercising remarkable ingenuity, he formulated a methodical strategy to overcome the obstacle.\n\nObserving a multitude of small pebbles scattered across the surrounding ground, he commenced gathering them individually with his beak and depositing them methodically into the pitcher. Predictably, with each submerged pebble, the water level incrementally elevated.\n\nThrough persistent labor and unwavering patience, the water eventually rose to the rim of the container. Consequently, the triumphant crow quenched his agonizing thirst and successfully preserved his life.\n\nNecessity is the mother of invention, and systematic perseverance overcomes seemingly insurmountable obstacles.", "Grade_2": "Amid an extended period of intense drought, a dehydrated crow traversed the arid landscape in a desperate quest for moisture. Approaching the point of total physical exhaustion, his keen vision identified a tall ceramic pitcher situated upon a desolate courtyard.\n\nImpelled by survival instinct, the avian descended to inspect the container. Upon examining the interior, he confirmed the presence of a small liquid reserve. Nevertheless, his initial relief dissolved into profound dismay when he ascertained that the narrow neck of the vessel rendered the water entirely inaccessible to his bill.\n\nInitially, the crow attempted to tip the container to spill its contents, yet the weight of the vessel defied his physical capacity. Subsequently, he attempted to shatter the durable ceramic structure, but his impact proved wholly ineffective. Confronted by this critical dilemma, he paused to evaluate alternative solutions.\n\nExhibiting extraordinary cognitive problem-solving, the crow observed numerous small pebbles strewn across the surrounding terrain. He conceived a brilliant plan based on the principle of fluid displacement.\n\nExercising meticulous patience, the bird retrieved the stones individually and deposited them into the vessel. Concurrently with the accumulation of pebbles at the base, the liquid level ascended incrementally. Through persistent execution of this methodical process, the water eventually crested the rim, enabling the crow to fully satisfy his physiological need.\n\nIntellectual ingenuity combined with methodical perseverance routinely surmounts obstacles that defy raw physical force.", "Grade_Pre1": "During a protracted epoch of ecological aridity, an imperiled corvid navigated the desiccated terrain in a critical quest for hydration. Nearing complete physiological collapse, his acute ocular acuity registered a tall ceramic vessel resting upon an abandoned courtyard.\n\nMotivated by existential imperative, the corvid alighted to evaluate the reservoir. Peering into the cavity, he verified the existence of a modest aqueous deposit. Howbeit, his momentary gratification evaporated into acute consternation upon discerning that the constricted aperture rendered the fluid hopelessly unapproachable to his beak.\n\nEndeavoring to overturn the vessel, the corvid discovered that its gravitational mass exceeded his physical leverage. Subsequently, he attempted to fracture the resilient ceramic matrix, yet his percussive assault produced no structural compromise. Facing an existential impasse, he suspended physical action to engage in cognitive analysis.\n\nDemonstrating sophisticated problem-solving acumen, the corvid observed countless small pebbles scattered across the adjacent substrate. He formulated a strategic intervention based on hydrodynamic displacement.\n\nManifesting extraordinary perseverance, the avian individually collected the stones and systematically submerged them within the receptacle. Proportionately with the accumulation of solid matter at the base, the fluid column elevated incrementally. Via the relentless execution of this empirical methodology, the water eventually overflowed the aperture, empowering the corvid to fully assuage his physiological crisis.\n\nCognitive ingenuity integrated with systematic tenacity routinely surmounts impediments that prove impervious to brute physical force.", "Classic_Original": "A Crow, half-dead with thirst, came upon a Pitcher which had once been full of water; but when the Crow pushed his beak into the mouth of the Pitcher, he found that only very little water was left in it, and that he could not reach far enough down to get at it. He tried, and he tried, but at last had to give it up, and walked away with his nose in the air, saying: \"I am sure they are sour.\" Then a thought came to him, and he took a pebble and dropped it into the Pitcher; then he took another pebble and dropped it into the Pitcher; then he took another and dropped it into the Pitcher. At last, at last, he saw the water mount up near to the brim, and kneeling down he quenched his thirst.\n\nLittle by little does the trick.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 9, "key": "dog_and_his_shadow", "titleEn": "The Dog and His Shadow", "titleJa": "欲張りな犬", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_dog_and_his_shadow.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A dog stole a big piece of meat from a butcher's shop. He was very happy and ran home to eat it.\n\nOn his way home, he had to cross a small wooden bridge over a clear stream.\n\nAs he looked down into the water, he saw his own reflection. But the greedy dog thought it was another dog carrying another big piece of meat!\n\n\"I want that meat too!\" thought the dog.\n\nHe opened his mouth and barked loudly at the reflection.\n\nThe moment he opened his mouth, his own piece of meat fell into the water and sank to the bottom. The dog was left with nothing.\n\nIf you are greedy and want everything, you will lose what you have.", "Grade_3": "A greedy dog managed to steal a juicy piece of meat from a local butcher's shop. Carrying his prize proudly in his mouth, he hurried toward his home to enjoy his feast.\n\nOn his way, he had to cross a narrow wooden bridge spanning a calm stream.\n\nLooking down into the clear water, he noticed his own reflection. However, assuming it was another dog carrying a piece of meat that appeared even larger than his own, his greed overcame him.\n\n\"If I take his meat as well, I will have twice as much!\" thought the foolish dog.\n\nHe snapped fiercely at the image in the water. But as soon as he opened his mouth, his piece of meat dropped into the river and sank out of sight.\n\nHe who grasps at the shadow loses the substance.", "Grade_Pre2": "A covetous hound successfully purloined a choice cut of meat from a village butcher. Gripping the prized morsel tightly between his jaws, he beat a hasty retreat toward his secluded lair to devour his spoils in solitary satisfaction.\n\nDuring his homeward journey, he traversed a rustic wooden footbridge spanning a tranquil crystal-clear brook.\n\nGlancing downward into the unruffled water, he perceived his own inverted reflection. Misinterpreting the optical illusion, he concluded that another canine was positioned beneath the surface, holding a portion of meat far superior in magnitude to his own. Instantly, insatiable avarice overwhelmed his rational judgment.\n\n\"If I dispossess him of his treasure,\" reasoned the misguided animal, \"I shall double my current wealth!\"\n\nYielding to irresistible greed, he opened his jaws to snap aggressively at his perceived rival. The instant he unclasped his teeth, his authentic prize slipped from his mouth, plunged into the current, and descended irrevocably into the watery depths.\n\nExcessive greed blinds the intellect; those who obsessively pursue illusive phantoms invariably forfeit the tangible blessings they already possess.", "Grade_2": "A fortunate canine was returning home, clutching a choice cut of meat acquired from a local butcher. Elated by his good fortune, he anticipated savoring his prize in solitary comfort.\n\nHis route mandated traversing a narrow wooden bridge spanning a tranquil stream. Pausing mid-crossing, he peered into the transparent water and observed his own optical reflection. Misinterpreting this aquatic image as a formidable competitor carrying an item of superior magnitude, the covetous canine was instantly overcome by insatiable avarice.\n\n\"I shall expropriate that additional prize,\" the canine resolved foolishly, driven by an unbridled impulse to maximize his acquisition.\n\nCompelled by greed to usurp what he perceived as a rival's asset, the canine snapped his jaws aggressively, emitting a loud bark to intimidate the image.\n\nInevitably, the instant his mouth unclasped, his actual prize dislodged and plunged into the current below. The swift waters instantly swept the meat beyond recovery. The canine remained stranded on the structure, contemplating the permanent loss of his tangible asset, confronted only by the mockery of his own hollow reflection.\n\nInsatiable greed for illusory phantoms routinely precipitates the forfeiture of tangible reality.", "Grade_Pre1": "A privileged canine was journeying homeward, carrying a prime portion of meat procured from a purveyor. Transported by euphoric self-congratulation, he envisioned consuming his prize in unmolested solitude.\n\nHis itinerary necessitated negotiating a precarious footbridge bridging a pristine rivulet. Halting midway, his gaze penetrated the crystalline mirror of the water, discerning his own optical manifestation. Confounding this aquatic mirage with an antagonist possessing a prize of far greater dimension, the rapacious canine was compulsively overwhelmed by unappeasable cupidity.\n\n\"I am impelled to appropriate that superior commodity,\" the canine postulated foolishly, capitulating to an irrational obsession with maximum accumulation.\n\nDictated by predatory instincts to usurp what he erroneously designated as a competitor's possession, he unclasped his mandibles to unleash a menacing growl intended to subjugate the phantom.\n\nPredictably, the moment his jaws opened, his authentic treasure disengaged and plummeted into the torrential current beneath. The turbulent waters irrevocably swept the asset into oblivion. The canine lingered upon the structure, mournfully meditating upon the absolute forfeiture of his concrete asset, mocked solely by the empty insubstantiality of his own image.\n\nUnbridled cupidity for intangible mirages inexorably precipitates the total devastation of verifiable substance.", "Classic_Original": "A Dog, crossing a bridge over a stream with a piece of meat in his mouth, saw his own shadow in the water and took it for that of another Dog, with a piece of meat double his own in size. He immediately let go of his own, and fiercely attacked the other Dog to get his larger piece from him. He thus lost both: that which he grasped at in the water, because it was a shadow; and his own, because the stream swept it away.\n\nBeware lest you lose the substance by grasping at the shadow.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 10, "key": "milkmaid_and_her_pail", "titleEn": "The Milkmaid and Her Pail", "titleJa": "ミルク搾りの娘", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_milkmaid_and_her_pail.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "Patty, a milkmaid, carried a pail of fresh milk on her head. She was walking to the market to sell the milk.\n\nAs she walked, she began to calculate her future.\n\n\"I will sell this milk for money,\" she thought. \"With the money, I will buy eggs. The eggs will hatch into fine chickens. Then I will sell the chickens and buy a beautiful new dress.\"\n\nShe felt so happy and proud. \"I will wear the dress to the party. All the young men will want to dance with me. But I will toss my head and say no!\"\n\nAs she said this, she tossed her head back.\n\nDown fell the pail of milk! The milk spilled all over the ground, and all her dreams vanished in a moment.\n\nDo not count your chickens before they are hatched.", "Grade_3": "Patty, a young milkmaid, was walking to the market, balancing a pail of fresh milk carefully on top of her head. As she strolled along the country path, she began daydreaming about what she would do with her earnings.\n\n\"When I sell this delicious milk, I will use the money to purchase a hundred eggs,\" she thought excitedly. \"Most of the eggs will hatch into healthy chickens. I will raise them and sell them for a good price.\"\n\nContinuing her calculations, she smiled to herself. \"With that money, I will buy a splendid dress to wear to the festival. All the young men will ask me to dance, but I will proudly toss my head and refuse them all!\"\n\nForgetting the heavy pail on her head, she tossed her head back to demonstrate her pride.\n\nInstantly, the pail fell to the ground, and the milk was spilled everywhere. Tears filled her eyes as she realized that all her grand plans had disappeared in a second.\n\nDo not count your chickens before they are hatched.", "Grade_Pre2": "Patty, an ambitious young milkmaid, was journeying toward the market square, skilfully balancing a container of freshly drawn milk upon her head. As she ambled along the peaceful rural thoroughfare, her mind became absorbed in speculative calculations regarding the financial proceeds of her commodity.\n\n\"Upon liquidating this milk for substantial currency,\" she soliloquized enthusiastically, \"I shall reinvest the capital to acquire several dozen eggs. In due course, these eggs will incubate and hatch into robust poultry. Subsequently, I shall market the chickens at a premium valuation.\"\n\nExtrapolating her commercial success, her vanity swelled. \"With the accrued profits, I will purchase an extravagant gown to adorn myself for the upcoming harvest gala. Innumerable suitors will solicit my hand in marriage, yet I shall scornfully toss my head and reject every proposal!\"\n\nIntoxicated by her grandiose fantasies, she dramatically jerked her head backward to emulate her envisioned disdain.\n\nPrecipitously, the vessel slipped from her crown and shattered upon the cobblestones, inundating the soil with her white treasure. Overwhelmed by grief, she stood paralyzed as her prospective fortune evaporated instantaneously.\n\nDo not count your chickens before they are hatched; premature reliance upon unearned gains inevitably precipitates bitter disappointment.", "Grade_2": "A young dairy maid was returning from the pasture, balancing a vessel filled to capacity with fresh milk atop her head. As she traversed the rural pathway, she succumbed to grandiose financial projections, mentally reinvesting the anticipated proceeds of her commodity.\n\n\"Disposing of this milk at the regional market will generate substantial capital,\" she reasoned strategically. \"I shall allocate those funds toward the acquisition of hundreds of eggs. Allowing for natural mortality, the venture will yield a formidable flock of poultry.\"\n\nHer speculative calculations rapidly expanded. \"Once these birds reach maturity, I shall liquidate them during peak demand, securing a lucrative return. This capital will enable the purchase of exquisite attire suitable for the forthcoming municipal gala.\"\n\nImmersed in her vision of social elevation, she imagined herself as the centerpiece of admiration. \"Every suitor will vie for my favor, yet I shall haughtily reject their advances with a disdainful gesture of my head.\"\n\nEnraptured by this imaginary scenario, she impulsively executed the physical movement in reality. Consequently, the vessel lost its equilibrium, plunging to the earth and saturating the soil with her entire liquid asset.\n\nDistraught by the sudden calamity, she wept for her evaporated wealth, recognizing that her elaborate scheme had dissolved into nothingness.\n\nPremature speculation on unverified outcomes frequently precipitates catastrophic disillusionment; never count your chickens before they hatch.", "Grade_Pre1": "An ambitious agrarian maiden was navigating a rural thoroughfare, bearing a receptacle filled to the brim with unpasteurized milk upon her crown. During her solitary transit, she succumbed to extravagant financial extrapolations, pre-emptively allocating the hypothetical revenue generated by her agricultural asset.\n\n\"Monetizing this dairy volume at the central emporium will yield significant liquid capital,\" she calculated meticulously. \"I propose to invest these funds in the procurement of avian ova. Factorizing expected attrition, the enterprise will materialize in a substantial avian flock.\"\n\nHer speculative projections proliferated exponentially. \"Subsequent to their maturation, I shall liquidate the livestock during a period of peak market demand, capturing a exorbitant dividend. This capital shall facilitate the acquisition of haute couture for the upcoming aristocratic assembly.\"\n\nObsessed with this mirage of socio-economic ascendance, she pictured herself the cynosure of all eyes. \"Numrous suitors will vie for my patronage, yet I shall contemptuously spurn their overtures with a supercilious toss of my head.\"\n\nEngulfed by this vivid hallucination, she unwittingly mimicked the physical motion in actuality. Whereupon, the receptacle forfeited its equilibrium, descending precipitously to saturate the terrain with her entire liquid capital.\n\nProfoundly traumatized by this instantaneous debacle, she lamented the annihilation of her illusory fortune, acknowledging that her elaborate construct had collapsed into absolute nullity.\n\nPremature speculation predicated upon unverified hypotheses inevitably induces catastrophic disillusionment; never count your chickens prior to their incubation.", "Classic_Original": "Patty the Milkmaid was going to market carrying her milk in a Pail on her head. As she went along, she began calculating what she would do with the money she would get for the milk. \"I'll buy some eggs from Farmer Brown,\" said she, \"and they will hatch into chickens. I'll sell the chickens, and buy a new gown to wear to the fair. All the young fellows will propose to me, but I'll toss my head and say No.\" As she spoke, she tossed her head back, the Pail fell off, and all the milk was spilled! She had to go home and tell her mother what had occurred. \"Ah, my child,\" said the mother:\n\nDo not count your chickens before they are hatched.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 11, "key": "honest_woodcutter", "titleEn": "The Honest Woodcutter", "titleJa": "金の斧と銀の斧", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_honest_woodcutter.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A poor woodcutter was chopping wood near a deep river. Suddenly, his axe slipped from his hand and fell into the water. He lost his only tool, so he sat by the river and cried.\n\nSuddenly, Hermes, the god of the forest, appeared. \"Why are you crying?\" Hermes asked. \n\nThe woodcutter answered, \"I lost my axe in the river. Now I cannot work.\"\n\nHermes dived into the water and brought up a gold axe. \"Is this your axe?\" he asked.\n\n\"No, that is not mine,\" the honest man said.\n\nHermes dived again and brought up a silver axe. \"Is this yours?\"\n\n\"No, that is not mine either,\" the man replied.\n\nFinally, Hermes brought up the old iron axe. \"Yes! That is my axe!\" the woodcutter shouted happily.\n\nHermes smiled and said, \"You are very honest. I will give you all three axes as a gift.\"\n\nLater, a greedy man heard this story. He went to the river and dropped his axe on purpose. When Hermes showed him the gold axe, the greedy man lied, \"Yes! That is mine!\" \n\nHermes was angry at his lie. He disappeared with the gold axe and did not return the old axe. The greedy man lost everything.\n\nHonesty is the best policy.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, an honest woodcutter was working near a deep river. By accident, his axe slipped out of his hands and sank to the bottom of the water. Since he was too poor to buy a new one, he sat on the riverbank and wept bitterly.\n\nSuddenly, Hermes, a divine messenger, appeared before him. Learning about the woodcutter's trouble, Hermes decided to help. He dived into the cold river and returned with a brilliant golden axe. \"Is this the axe that you lost?\" Hermes inquired.\n\n\"No, that is not mine,\" the woodcutter replied truthfully.\n\nHermes dived a second time and brought up a silver axe. Again, the honest woodcutter shook his head and said, \"No, my axe is much older than that.\"\n\nFinally, Hermes dived a third time and pulled out the old iron axe. The woodcutter cried out with joy, \"That is indeed my axe! Thank you so much!\"\n\nImpressed by his honesty, Hermes rewarded the man by giving him all three axes.\n\nWhen a greedy neighbor heard about this fortunate event, he decided to trick the god. He rushed to the river and threw his own axe into the water on purpose. When Hermes appeared with a golden axe, the greedy man shouted eagerly, \"Yes, that belongs to me!\"\n\nDisgusted by his deception, Hermes vanished instantly, leaving the greedy man with neither the golden axe nor his own.\n\nGreed will bring you nothing, but honesty is always rewarded in the end.", "Grade_Pre2": "An impoverished yet virtuous woodcutter was diligently laboring on the banks of a swift mountain river. While he was chopping timber, the axe head suddenly detached from its handle, plunging into the deep, turbulent current. Deprived of his sole means of livelihood, the grief-stricken laborer collapsed upon the riverbank and wept uncontrollably.\n\nMoved by the man's genuine distress, Hermes, the divine protector of travelers, materialized before him. Upon discovering the cause of his sorrow, Hermes plunged into the depths of the river and re-emerged with a magnificent axe crafted entirely of pure gold. Presenting the radiant object, the deity inquired whether it was the tool he had misplaced. Without hesitation, the woodcutter declined, stating with humble conviction that such a costly instrument did not belong to him.\n\nHermes descended beneath the surface once more, this time retrieving an exquisite axe of polished silver. Nevertheless, the woodcutter maintained his integrity, firmly denying ownership. Descending for a third time, Hermes brought forth the humble iron axe. Overwhelmed with profound relief and gratitude, the woodcutter acknowledged it immediately. Immensely impressed by such rare uprightness, Hermes bestowed all three axes upon him as a token of divine favor.\n\nSubsequently, when an envious neighbor learned of this remarkable fortune, he resolved to duplicate the miracle through deliberate deceit. Hurrying to the identical spot, he intentionally hurled his axe into the river and staged a dramatic show of grief. When Hermes appeared and displayed the golden axe, the avaricious impostor reached forward eagerly, falsely claiming ownership.\n\nInfuriated by this blatant dishonesty, Hermes vanished into thin air, utterly refusing to recover either the golden treasure or the man's discarded tool. Consequently, the deceitful laborer was left empty-handed, suffering the harsh penalty of his unbridled cupidity.\n\nIntegrity is an enduring virtue that commands universal respect, whereas deceit and shameless greed inevitably precipitate complete ruin.", "Grade_2": "In a secluded mountain district, an indigent yet conscientious lumberjack derived his modest subsistence from felling timber alongside a torrential alpine river. While executing his arduous labor with customary diligence, a structural failure of his implement precipitated an immediate crisis: the iron axe head separated from its shaft, descending into the fathomless and swirling depths of the torrent. Bereft of his primary productive capital and lacking the financial resources to procure an adequate replacement, the desolate artisan slumped along the precipitous embankment, lamenting his abrupt misfortune.\n\nPrompted by profound empathy for human anguish, Hermes, the patron deity of commerce and travel, materialized beside the despairing mortal. Ascertaining the etiology of the craftsman's lamentation, the celestial entity plunged beneath the turbulent surface, presently re-emerging with an opulent implement fashioned exclusively of solid gold. Interrogating the woodcutter regarding its provenance, the deity offered him the precious artifact. Incorruptible in his ethical rectitude, the impoverished laborer unequivocally repudiated ownership, professing that an instrument of such excessive value bore no relation to his mundane occupation.\n\nUndeterred, Hermes executed a secondary descent, surfacing with an elaborately burnished silver axe. Manifesting unwavering fidelity to moral truth, the artisan rejected this specimen with equal composure. Only upon the deity's tertiary emergence bearing the weathered iron implement did the woodcutter articulate exuberant recognition, profusely expressing gratitude for the restoration of his authentic property. Utterly captivated by an exhibition of ethical probity so rarely observed among mortals, Hermes conferred all three implements upon the upright laborer as a tangible testament to the supremacy of moral rectitude.\n\nThe news of this miraculous acquisition ignited intense cupidity in the psyche of a degenerate peer. Calculating that divine benevolence could be systematically exploited through manipulative simulations, the impostor hastened to the identical riparian location, intentionally casting his implement into the current and simulating theatrical hysteria. Upon the deity's reappearance displaying the golden commodity, the charlatan enthusiastically asserted a fraudulent claim, proclaiming it to be his authentic possession.\n\nRevolted by this audacious display of deceit, the divinity instantaneously dissolved into nothingness, withholding not merely the celestial artifact but permanently abandoning the submerged mundane tool to the subterranean currents.\n\nMoral rectitude constitutes an intrinsic virtue whose authentic practice yields unanticipated dividends, whereas fraudulent machinations motivated by unconstrained avarice inevitably result in catastrophic deprivation.", "Grade_Pre1": "In an austere montane wilderness, an impoverished yet scrupulously principled woodman eked out a precarious livelihood harvesting timber along the periphery of a ferocious alpine torrent. During the execution of his daily toil, an unforeseen mechanical failure abruptly jeopardized his economic survival: the iron blade detached from its wooden haft, plunging irrevocably into the chasm of swirling, turbid rapids. Deprived instantaneously of his sole productive asset and lacking the fiscal liquidity to commission a surrogate implement, the devastated laborer collapsed upon the riparian verge, surrendering to unrestrained desolation.\n\nGalvanized by compassionate resonance with mortal suffering, Hermes, the psychopomp and divine patron of terrestrial wayfarers, materialized in radiant glory beside the despondent artisan. Diagnosing the etiology of the craftsman’s bereavement, the immortal voyager dived into the subterranean depths of the aqueous vortex, presently resurfacing with an ornate implement wrought entirely of unblemished gold. Interrogating the woodman regarding the artifact's provenance, the deity proffered the dazzling treasure. Unflinching in his moral incorruptibility, the indigent artisan repudiated the proffer without ambivalence, affirming with modest gravitas that an instrument of such exorbitant opulence bore zero correspondence to his austere station in life.\n\nUnperturbed, Hermes executed a second immersion, retrieving a splendid axe sculpted from lustrous sterling silver. Demonstrating impenetrable fidelity to objective verity, the laborer declined this secondary treasure with identical equanimity. Only when the divinity emerged for a third time bearing the corroded, utilitarian iron blade did the artisan articulate ecstatic affirmation, effusively voicing veneration and gratitude for the restitution of his authentic chattel. Profoundly edified by an exhibition of ethical probity so vanishingly anomalous among terrestrial beings, Hermes bestowed all three implements upon the righteous woodsman as an enduring testament to the supreme sovereignty of integrity over material cupidity.\n\nWhen intelligence of this miraculous windfall permeated the adjacent settlement, it catalyzed pathological avarice within a morally bankrupt acquaintance. Hypothesizing that divine benevolence represented an exploitable cognitive heuristic susceptible to theatrical manipulation, the disingenuous charlatan hastened to the identical littoral coordinates. Deliberately consigning his functional implement to the abyss, he staged an exaggerated pantomime of hysterical despair. Upon Hermes’s epiphanic emergence wielding the golden prize, the avaricious interloper audaciously vocalized a mendacious claim, asserting proprietary rights over the celestial treasure.\n\nUtterly repulsed by such blatant moral decrepitude and transparent duplicity, the deity dematerialized into the ether, withholding not merely the transcendent golden treasure but consigning the fraudster's discarded instrument to permanent oblivion within the fluvial silt.\n\nAuthentic integrity transcends utilitarian calculus and commands transcendent reward, whereas disingenuous simulations of virtue animated by naked cupidity inexorably precipitate total disinheritance.", "Classic_Original": "A Woodman was felling a tree on the bank of a river, and by chance his axe slipped from his hand and dropped into the water. Deeply troubled, he sat down by the river and began to weep. Hermes appeared and, learning the reason for his grief, dived into the river. He brought up a golden axe and asked if it was the one he had lost. The woodman replied that it was not. Hermes dived a second time and brought up a silver axe. Again the woodman denied that it was his. Hermes dived a third time and brought up the wooden axe which had been lost. The woodman recognized it with joy. Hermes, delighted by his honesty, gave him all three axes. The woodman told his friends what had happened. One of them went to the river, dropped his axe on purpose, and sat weeping. Hermes appeared, dived, brought up a golden axe, and asked if it was his. The greedy man cried out with joy, \"Yes, that is mine!\" Hermes was disgusted by his dishonesty and not only kept the golden axe, but refused to retrieve the wooden one.\n\nHonesty is the best policy.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 12, "key": "goose_golden_eggs", "titleEn": "The Goose that Laid the Golden Eggs", "titleJa": "金の卵を産むガチョウ", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_goose_golden_eggs.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A poor farmer and his wife owned a wonderful goose. Every morning, the goose laid a shiny golden egg.\n\nThe farmer sold the golden egg at the market every day. Soon, they became rich and lived comfortably.\n\nHowever, the farmer became greedy. \"One egg a day is too slow,\" he thought. \"The goose must have a lot of gold inside her belly. If I open her, I can get all the gold at once!\"\n\nHe told his wife about his plan, and she agreed. They killed the goose and opened her belly.\n\nTo their surprise, there was no gold inside at all! She was just like any other ordinary goose.\n\nNow, they had no golden eggs and no goose. They wept because their greed destroyed everything.\n\nDo not be greedy, or you will lose what you have.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a humble farmer and his wife were fortunate enough to possess a rare goose. To their delight, every single morning the goose laid a solid golden egg.\n\nBy selling these precious eggs at the market, the couple gradually accumulated wealth and enjoyed a comfortable life. \n\nHowever, as time passed, the farmer grew impatient and greedy. He thought to himself, \"It takes too long to get just one egg a day. If the goose produces gold, her inside must be filled with a vast treasure! If we cut her open, we can acquire all the gold at once.\"\n\nHoping to become millionaires overnight, the foolish couple decided to carry out the plan. They killed the goose immediately and examined her inside. \n\nMuch to their disappointment, they discovered that the bird was no different from any normal goose. There was not a single piece of gold inside.\n\nRealizing their terrible mistake, the couple cried in despair. By seeking to gain everything too quickly, they had lost their steady source of wealth forever.\n\nThose who are overly greedy will end up losing even what they already possess.", "Grade_Pre2": "A modest agrarian couple lived in humble circumstances until fortune smiled upon them through an extraordinary goose. Remarkably, this singular bird produced a solid gold egg at dawn every single day. By regularly converting these precious items into currency, the peasants rapidly elevated their standard of living and accumulated substantial savings without enduring excessive labor.\n\nNotwithstanding this miraculous source of consistent prosperity, the farmer became increasingly dissatisfied with the daily pace of enrichment. Consumed by an insatiable lust for rapid wealth, he began to speculate about the bird's internal anatomy. \"Surely,\" he reasoned impatiently to his spouse, \"the creature's interior must contain a massive reservoir of molten gold. If we extract the entirety of the treasure simultaneously, we will instantly achieve unimaginable prosperity.\"\n\nPersuaded by this seductive fallacy, the couple resolved to slaughter the goose in order to seize the concealed riches. Without pausing to reflect on the potential consequences, they terminated the creature's life and dissected its body.\n\nMuch to their utter horror and mortification, however, they discovered that the goose's anatomy differed in no respect from that of any common waterfowl. Not a single particle of precious metal lay hidden within.\n\nConfronted with the irreversible tragedy of their own making, the couple succumbed to bitter remorse. In their rash attempt to obtain instantaneous abundance, they had extinguished the very source of their daily sustenance.\n\nUnchecked avarice blinds judgment and inevitably destroys the sustainable foundations of genuine well-being.", "Grade_2": "In an impoverished rural enclave, an agrarian household eked out a precarious existence until an unprecedented stroke of biological anomaly altered their financial trajectory. One of their domestic fowl, an outwardly unexceptional goose, began depositing an egg of immaculate, solid gold at each successive dawn. By methodically liquidating these daily windfalls at municipal markets, the proprietors systematically dismantled their generational poverty, transitioning from marginal subsistence to an enviable degree of socio-economic security.\n\nHowever, the psychological dynamics of sudden wealth rarely promote enduring temperance. Rather than remaining content with a reliable, compounding income stream, the patriarch grew increasingly intolerant of chronological constraints. Corrupted by cognitive distortions that conflated biological productivity with infinite inorganic reserves, he formulated a catastrophic financial conjecture. He postulated that the waterfowl's anatomical core must house an immense subterranean matrix of consolidated bullion. Proceeding from this delusional premise, he rationalized that preemptively liquidating the entire capital reserve through immediate surgical intervention would compress decades of wealth accumulation into a single instant.\n\nSwayed by this disastrous economic calculus and prioritizing immediate gratification over sustainable returns, the couple executed the terminal vivisection of their singular asset. Stripping away the creature's organic layers with feverish anticipation, they subjected the visceral cavity to meticulous scrutiny.\n\nTo their paralyzed stupefaction and profound disillusionment, empirical reality asserted itself with brutal finality: the bird's internal physiological composition was entirely indistinguishable from that of any mundane avian specimen. Not the slightest trace of precious auriferous substance existed within the biological carcass.\n\nThe realization of their catastrophic miscalculation precipitated profound despair. Through a reckless obsession with maximizing immediate liquidity, they had irrevocably obliterated the self-renewing capital engine that had underwritten their prosperity.\n\nUnregulated cupidity and shortsighted impatience inevitably subvert sustainable prosperity, demonstrating that the destruction of generative capital in pursuit of immediate gratification yields total insolvency.", "Grade_Pre1": "Within a marginalized rural periphery, an agrarian household endured chronic economic deprivation until an unprecedented physiological mutation radically reconstructed their socio-economic standing. One of their domesticated waterfowl, a phenotypically unremarkable goose, commenced depositing an ovum of unalloyed, solid gold at each successive diurnal threshold. By methodically monetizing these perpetual windfalls within regional bullion exchanges, the previously indigent peasants eliminated their generational liabilities, establishing a degree of financial independence that defied their historic socio-economic stratification.\n\nNevertheless, behavioral economics repeatedly illustrates that unearned, sudden liquidity frequently erodes rational prudence, cultivating acute cognitive myopia. Rather than acknowledging the miraculous virtue of a compounding, self-perpetuating yield, the patriarch succumbed to pathologically inflated expectations. Debilitated by the cognitive fallacy of temporal discounting and erroneously conceptualizing organic metabolism as a static repository of inorganic mineral reserves, he synthesized an absurd financial hypothesis. He postulated that the waterfowl’s visceral interior housed an inexhaustible lode of consolidated bullion, foolishly concluding that preemptively liquidating this hypothetical endowment via terminal anatomical dissection would instantaneously collapse multi-decade wealth accumulation into a single lucrative event.\n\nSubordinating sustainable long-term yields to an unquenchable obsession with immediate gratification, the infatuated couple executed the vivisection of their sole generative asset. Driven by feverish avarice, they dissected the abdominal cavity with forensic desperation, frantically probing the internal viscera for the anticipated golden matrix.\n\nWhereupon, unyielding biological reality asserted its immutable laws with catastrophic finality: the specimen’s internal physiology exhibited absolute uniformity with the baseline anatomy of common domestic poultry. Devoid of the faintest trace of precious auriferous sedimentation, the eviscerated carcass lay inert upon the abattoir table—a grim monument to cognitive hubris.\n\nThe catastrophic comprehension of their irreversible miscalculation precipitated an agonizing psychological collapse. In their predatory quest to artificially accelerate capital extraction, they had permanently obliterated the biological engine that had underwritten their economic emancipation, voluntarily relegating their household to irreversible destitution.\n\nUnconstrained cupidity predicated on the myopic prioritization of immediate liquidity inevitably annihilates sustainable prosperity; the sacrificial destruction of generative capital upon the altar of instantaneous gratification guarantees ultimate insolvency.", "Classic_Original": "A Cottager and his wife had a Hen which laid a golden egg every day. They supposed that the Hen must contain a great lump of gold in its inside, and in order to get the gold, they killed it. Having done so, they found to their surprise that the Hen differed in no respect from their other hens. The foolish pair, hoping to become rich all at once, thus deprived themselves of the gain of which they were assured day by day.\n\nThinking to get at once all the gold, they lost even the little they had.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 13, "key": "wolf_in_sheeps_clothing", "titleEn": "The Wolf in Sheep's Clothing", "titleJa": "羊の皮をかぶった狼", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_wolf_in_sheeps_clothing.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A hungry wolf wanted to eat sheep. However, a watchman and his strong dogs protected the sheep every day. The wolf could not go near the flock.\n\nOne day, the wolf found an old sheep skin on the ground. He had a clever idea. \"I will wear this skin. Then I can look like a sheep!\" he thought.\n\nThe wolf put on the sheep skin and walked into the field. The sheep did not know he was a wolf. A young lamb even walked behind him. The wolf quietly led the lamb away and ate it.\n\nFor many days, the wolf tricked the sheep and ate well.\n\nOne night, the shepherd came to the farm. He wanted to catch a sheep for dinner. In the dark, he saw the wolf wearing the sheep skin. The shepherd thought it was a big sheep, so he caught it and killed it.\n\nThe wolf was caught in his own trick.\n\nAppearances can be deceiving.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a sly wolf was desperately searching for a way to attack a flock of sheep. However, because the shepherd and his fierce dogs kept a close watch, the wolf failed every time he tried to approach them.\n\nOne afternoon, the wolf discovered the fleece of a sheep that had been thrown away in the pasture. A wicked plan entered his mind. \"If I disguise myself in this wool,\" he reasoned, \"the shepherd will mistake me for one of his own animals.\"\n\nAfter putting on the sheep's skin, the wolf strolled calmly among the flock. As he had expected, neither the shepherd nor the guard dogs noticed his true identity. A innocent lamb even followed him closely. Taking advantage of the opportunity, the wolf led the lamb into the forest and devoured it.\n\nFor a while, the wolf succeeded in deceiving everyone and enjoyed effortless feasts every night.\n\nHowever, justice came unexpectedly. One evening, the shepherd entered the fold in the dark, intending to slaughter a sheep for his family's meal. Mistaking the disguised wolf for a fat sheep, the shepherd seized him instantly and put an end to his life.\n\nThose who try to deceive others through fake appearances will eventually suffer the consequences.", "Grade_Pre2": "A predatory wolf had long coveted a thriving flock of sheep grazing peacefully on a verdant hillside. Nevertheless, penetrating their defenses proved virtually insurmountable due to the unceasing vigilance maintained by a diligent shepherd and his formidable hounds. Frustrated by numerous thwarted incursions, the carnivore resolved to substitute cunning strategy for brute force.\n\nWhile prowling along the perimeter of the pasture, the wolf stumbled upon the discarded fleece of a slaughtered sheep. Instantly recognizing the tactical utility of the pelt, he enveloped his lean frame within the woolly disguise. His objective was to fabricate an illusion of harmless docility, thereby circumventing the herdsman's suspicion.\n\nThus camouflaged, the intruder infiltrated the flock without exciting the slightest apprehension among the animals. Deceived by the superficial exterior, even a vulnerable lamb unhesitatingly trotted alongside the disguised carnivore, accepting him as its maternal guardian. Exploiting this misplaced trust, the wolf gently coaxed the juvenile creature into a secluded thicket and promptly devoured it. Emboldened by this effortless triumph, the predator repeated the heinous subterfuge for several consecutive days, feasting on unsuspecting livestock without detection.\n\nNevertheless, retribution manifested itself in an ironic and fatal manner. Late one evening, seeking provisions for the forthcoming holiday banquet, the shepherd quietly ventured into the enclosed fold armed with a carving knife. Impaired by the nocturnal gloom, the herdsman instinctively singled out the largest silhouette, erroneously presuming it to be a choice ram. Before the disguised monster could react or shed his false attire, the shepherd seized him firmly and dispatched him on the spot.\n\nHypocritical pretension and deceptive facades cannot indefinitely shield the wicked; those who exploit innocence under the cloak of virtue will inevitably perish by their own deceit.", "Grade_2": "A cunning predatory carnivore had perpetually fixated its lethal ambitions upon an idyllic pastoral community, where an expansive flock of domesticated ruminants grazed under the rigorous surveillance of a vigilant shepherd and his seasoned canine sentinels. Every direct assault initiated by the predator had been systematically repelled by the perimeter security apparatus, rendering conventional physical confrontation strategically non-viable. Confronted by this defensive deadlock, the predator opted to abandon overt aggression in favor of sophisticated psychological subversion.\n\nTraversing the periphery of the enclosure, the beast discovered the flayed fleece of a slaughtered sheep, which had been carelessly discarded adjacent to the shearing shed. Discerning the immense deceptive potential of this biological vestment, the wolf draped the tactile woolen exterior over his own lethal anatomy. By masquerading as an embodiment of pastoral harmlessness, he effectively neutralized the perceptual vigilance of both the human guardian and the herd's collective instincts.\n\nIntegrated into the pastoral population, the camouflaged infiltrator exploited cognitive shortcuts inherent in social herd dynamics. Mammals instinctively associate familiar visual and olfactory markers with safety; consequently, an impressionable juvenile lamb gravitated toward the disguised menace, accepting the impostor as a legitimate matriarch. Manipulating this misplaced filial allegiance, the predator surreptitiously guided the naive creature into an isolated ravine, where he liquidated his victim with absolute impunity. For weeks, this parasitic masquerade persisted, sustained by the target population's systemic inability to interrogate superficial appearances.\n\nHowever, dialectical irony precipitated a swift and catastrophic termination to this predatory deception. One midnight, motivated by an urgent requirement to secure fresh meat for an imminent festival, the herdsman entered the darkened sheepcote. Lacking visual acuity amid the dense obscurity, the shepherd relied on tactile perception, systematically appraising the livestock to designate a specimen possessing optimal mass. Encountering the oversized silhouette of the shrouded wolf, the herdsman erroneously categorized the beast as an exceptionally plump prime ram. Mobilizing professional efficiency, he clamped an iron grip around the animal's throat and executed a lethal incision before the masquerading impostor could articulate defense or shed his borrowed pelt.\n\nVisual subterfuge constitutes an inherently fragile defense mechanism; those who weaponize fraudulent innocence to victimize the vulnerable will ultimately be consumed by the catastrophic repercussions of their own manufactured identities.", "Grade_Pre1": "In the harsh ecology of competitive survival, an apex canine predator harbored an unyielding predatory fixation upon a thriving pastoral flock. However, penetrating the livestock’s fortified sanctuary proved impervious to physical force, continually thwarted by the multi-layered defensive apparatus orchestrated by an indefatigable shepherd and his seasoned mastiffs. Recognizing the structural obsolescence of frontal assault, the carnivore executed an epistemological pivot: where kinetic violence proved impotent, he would deploy asymmetric socio-biological espionage.\n\nScouring the periphery of the pastoral settlement, the predator encountered the intact fleece of a flayed sheep, which had been abandoned adjacent to an abattoir enclosure. Discerning the covert utility of this biological masquerade, the wolf encased his muscular anatomy within the tactile woolen shroud. By counterfeiting the morphology of benign docility, the infiltrator aimed to exploit evolutionary heuristics that prime herd animals to prioritize superficial phenotypic markers over behavioral scrutiny.\n\nInfiltrating the pastoral fold under cover of dusk, the impostor capitalized upon the social compliance inherent in mammalian herd behavior. Evolutionary psychology dictates that ungulates uncritically defer to familiar olfactory and aesthetic signifiers; accordingly, a juvenile lamb gravitated toward the predator, intuitively interpreting the borrowed pelt as a maternal nexus. Exploiting this tragic cognitive shortfall, the infiltrator coaxed the naive progeny into a secluded ravine, expeditiously liquidating the organism with absolute impunity. Emboldened by this triumphal deception, the carnivore instituted a systemic regime of parasitic extraction, harvesting vulnerable livestock without provoking alarm.\n\nNevertheless, retributive justice intervened through a supreme act of poetic irony. Late one evening, responding to an urgent imperative to procure provisions for a ceremonial feast, the shepherd quietly entered the nocturnal gloom of the fold armed with a slaughtering blade. Impaired by sensory deprivation, the herdsman eschewed visual discrimination in favor of tactile palpation, evaluating the livestock solely by volumetric density. Stumbling upon the disguised predator’s substantial mass, the herdsman instinctively classified the creature as a prime specimen of exceptional girth. Before the interloper could mobilize defensive resistance, decipher the mortal hazard, or shed his deceptive vestment, the herdsman administered a lethal laceration to the throat, terminating the predator's life in an instant.\n\nSuperficial masquerade constitutes an intrinsically volatile survival strategy; those who weaponize false innocence to exploit the defenseless inevitably construct the precise operational mechanisms of their own catastrophic immolation.", "Classic_Original": "A Wolf found great difficulty in getting at the sheep owing to the vigilance of the shepherd and his dogs. But one day it found the skin of a sheep that had been flayed and thrown aside, so it put it on over its own pelt and strolled down among the sheep. The lamb that belonged to the sheep whose skin the Wolf was wearing began to follow the Wolf; so leading the lamb a little away, he soon made a meal off her, and for some time he succeeded in deceiving the sheep, and enjoying hearty meals.\n\nAppearances are deceptive.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 14, "key": "fox_and_stork", "titleEn": "The Fox and the Stork", "titleJa": "キツネとツル", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_fox_and_stork.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A mischievous fox invited a stork to dinner. The fox wanted to play a trick on her.\n\nWhen the stork arrived, the fox served delicious soup in a very shallow plate. The fox lapped up the soup easily with his tongue. However, the stork had a very long beak, so she could not drink any soup at all. \n\n\"I am sorry,\" the fox laughed. \"Is the soup not good?\"\n\nThe stork smiled and said, \"Thank you for dinner. Please come to my house tomorrow.\"\n\nThe next day, the fox went to the stork's home. The stork served dinner in a tall jar with a narrow neck. The stork put her long beak into the jar and enjoyed the food. But the fox could only lick the outside of the jar.\n\nThe fox went home very hungry. He realized his mistake.\n\nTreat others as you want them to treat you.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a sly fox decided to play a trick on his neighbor, a stork. He invited her to his house for dinner, promising a delicious meal.\n\nWhen the stork arrived, the fox served some hot soup, but he poured it into very shallow dishes. While the fox lapped up the soup effortlessly with his broad tongue, the poor stork could only touch the liquid with the tip of her long beak. As a result, she was unable to eat anything and remained hungry throughout the evening.\n\n\"I am afraid that you do not like my soup,\" the fox said with a mischievous grin.\n\n\"On the contrary, it smells wonderful,\" replied the stork politely. \"To show my gratitude, please accept an invitation to dine at my home tomorrow night.\"\n\nThe following evening, the fox visited the stork's residence. To his surprise, the stork served the meal in a tall, narrow jar with a slender neck. The stork easily inserted her long beak into the container and enjoyed her food. However, the fox's snout was far too wide to fit inside, so he could do nothing but lick the outer rim of the jar.\n\nFeeling embarrassed and hungry, the fox returned home, understanding that he had received a fitting punishment for his previous rudeness.\n\nOne good turn deserves another, but bad treatment will return to you just the same.", "Grade_Pre2": "A cunning fox and a dignified stork maintained an outward display of cordial friendship, although the fox harbored a petty desire to humiliate his avian companion. Under the pretense of hospitable generosity, the fox extended an invitation to the stork for an evening banquet at his den.\n\nUpon her arrival, the host presented a fragrant broth served exclusively in remarkably flat, shallow earthenware dishes. While the fox's broad tongue enabled him to consume the liquid with consummate ease, the stork's elongated beak proved entirely unsuited for such wide tableware. Despite repeated attempts, she could merely dip the tip of her bill into the broth, remaining completely famished. Amused by her obvious distress, the fox feigned polite concern, insincerely lamenting her apparent lack of appetite.\n\nMasking her resentment behind impeccable courtesy, the stork gracefully endured the humiliating ordeal. Before departing, she cordially reciprocated the hospitality, extending an invitation for the fox to join her for dinner on the ensuing evening.\n\nPromptly the following sunset, the expectant fox arrived at the stork's dwelling, anticipating a complimentary feast. To his profound chagrin, the meal was presented inside towering, slender flacons characterized by extremely narrow apertures. The stork effortlessly inserted her long bill into the elongated neck, extracting succulent morsels of food with complete satisfaction. Conversely, the fox found it physically impossible to introduce even his snout into the vessel, reducing him to fruitlessly licking the exterior glaze.\n\nHumiliated and famished, the defeated prankster slunk away into the shadows, forced to acknowledge that his malicious scheme had been ingeniously turned against him.\n\nTrue mutual respect requires considering the unique circumstances of others, whereas those who deliberately subject their peers to embarrassment must expect equivalent retribution.", "Grade_2": "In the realm of animal diplomacy, a notoriously manipulative fox engaged in a superficial alliance with an austere stork, preserving a facade of social harmony that concealed deep-seated psychological antagonism. Seeking to assert intellectual superiority through interpersonal humiliation, the vulpine host orchestrated a banquet at his subterranean domicile, framing the event as a celebration of mutual rapport.\n\nUpon the guest's punctual arrival, the host unveiled an aromatic gastronomic concoction decanted exclusively across broad, low-rimmed ceramic salvers. This deliberate aesthetic configuration was calibrated to exploit anatomical divergence: while the host's expansive oral anatomy facilitated effortless ingestion, the stork's rigid, elongated rostrum proved structurally incompatible with horizontal liquid planes. Repeated attempts to harvest the broth merely wetted the avian bill, leaving the visitor in a state of acute caloric deprivation. Masking sadistic amusement behind disingenuous hospitality, the fox articulated mock sympathy, attributing her involuntary abstinence to culinary fastidiousness.\n\nRepressing instinctive indignation in favor of strategic retaliation, the stork preserved an attitude of unblemished equanimity. Prior to concluding the visitation, she formally reciprocated the gesture, extending an invitation for an evening banquet at her arboreal residence on the subsequent evening.\n\nDrawn by the prospect of unearned indulgence, the expectant fox arrived at the designated hour, anticipating lavish culinary hospitality. To his acute discomfiture, the meal had been decanted into towering, narrow-necked amphorae characterized by constricted apertures. With elegant mechanical precision, the avian hostess introduced her slender beak deep into the vessel's vertical interior, extracting succulent provisions with total autonomy. In stark contrast, the fox's cranial anatomy presented an insurmountable geometric impediment; unable to penetrate the aperture, the guest was reduced to licking microscopic residue from the external ceramic perimeter.\n\nThoroughly discomfited and physically depleted, the schemer executed a humiliating retreat, compelled to recognize that his pedagogical humiliation had been reciprocated with mathematical symmetry.\n\nAuthentic interpersonal ethics necessitate empathetic accommodation of diverse physiological and contextual realities, whereas institutionalizing malicious exclusion invites retaliatory retribution of identical proportion.", "Grade_Pre1": "In the realm of interspecies social interaction, an inveterately devious vulpine maintained a hollow diplomatic entente with a dignified wading bird. Concealing profound intellectual hubris behind an exterior of ceremonial civility, the fox orchestrated a banquet at his burrow, conceiving the gathering not as an authentic communion of hospitality, but as a calculated staging ground for subtle psychological subjugation.\n\nUpon the guest's arrival, the host presented a delicately infused broth decanted exclusively across flat, horizontal earthenware platters. This deliberate presentation was maliciously engineered to leverage anatomical disparity: whereas the fox's wide oral cavity facilitated rapid, uninhibited consumption via lateral lingual motion, the stork's elongated, narrow rostrum proved structurally unsuited for shallow, planar surfaces. Every effort to harvest the liquid resulted in futile clicks of her beak against the ceramic surface, condemning the dignitary to involuntary starvation. Masking malevolent satisfaction behind a facade of solicitous etiquette, the vulpine host lamented her apparent lack of appetite, disingenuously attributing her abstinence to overrefined culinary fastidiousness.\n\nSubordinating spontaneous resentment to strategic forbearance, the stork exhibited impenetrable composure. Before concluding the diplomatic protocol, she reciprocated the engagement, formally inviting the fox to an evening repast at her lakeside sanctuary the following day.\n\nSeduced by the anticipation of gratuitous culinary pleasure, the fox presented himself with punctual self-satisfaction. To his profound chagrin, the meal was served within towering, cylindrical vessels possessing constricted apertures and elongated necks. With effortless mechanical precision, the avian hostess lowered her slender bill into the vertical conduit, savoring the rich sustenance contained within. Conversely, the fox's broader facial anatomy encountered an impenetrable physical barrier; incapable of inserting even his snout beyond the aperture, the famished schemer was relegated to licking minuscule traces of condensation from the external glaze.\n\nPhysically depleted and socially humiliated, the defeated prankster slunk away into the shadows, forced to acknowledge that his calculated exclusion had been neutralized and reflected back upon him with rigorous mathematical symmetry.\n\nAuthentic ethical reciprocity demands an empathetic accommodation of divergent perspectives and physical constraints; those who deliberately engineer mechanisms of discriminatory humiliation will inevitably find themselves ensnared by the precise structural barriers they pioneered.", "Classic_Original": "At one time the Fox and the Stork seemed to be on very good terms and invited each other to dinner. First the Fox invited the Stork, and served nothing but soup in a very shallow dish. The Fox lapped it up with ease, but the Stork could only wet the end of her long bill in it, and left the meal as hungry as when she came. \"I am sorry,\" said the Fox, \"that the soup is not to your liking.\" The Stork thanked him and invited him to dine with her in return. When the Fox arrived, the Stork served the meal in a tall jar with a narrow neck. The Stork easily inserted her long bill and enjoyed the food, while the Fox could only lick the outside of the jar.\n\nOne bad turn deserves another.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 15, "key": "frog_and_ox", "titleEn": "The Frog and the Ox", "titleJa": "カエルと牛", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_frog_and_ox.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "An old mother frog lived near a pond with her little frogs. One day, a huge ox came to drink water at the pond.\n\nWhen the ox walked away, the little frogs ran to their mother. \"Mother! We saw a terrible monster today! It was as big as a mountain!\" they cried.\n\nThe mother frog was very proud. She did not believe them. \"I can make myself very big, too,\" she said. \n\nShe took a deep breath and puffed herself up. \"Was the monster as big as this?\" she asked.\n\n\"Oh, no! It was much bigger than that!\" the children answered.\n\nThe mother frog took another big breath and puffed herself up even more. \"Was it as big as this?\"\n\n\"No, no! You cannot become as big as the ox!\" the little frogs said.\n\nThe proud mother frog tried once more. She blew herself up harder and harder—POP! She burst into pieces.\n\nDo not try to be bigger than you really are.", "Grade_3": "An old mother frog, who was famous for her pride, lived near a quiet meadow with her young children. One morning, an enormous ox stepped into the pond to quench his thirst.\n\nAfter the ox departed, the terrified young frogs hurried back to their mother. \"Mother! We just saw the largest creature in the world!\" they exclaimed. \"His body was truly massive!\"\n\nUnwilling to admit that any creature could be far grander than herself, the mother frog replied haughtily, \"Nonsense! I can easily make myself just as big as that beast.\"\n\nShe took a deep breath and expanded her body as much as possible. \"Was he as large as this?\" she inquired.\n\n\"No, Mother! He was vastly larger than that!\" the children insisted.\n\nAnnoyed by their response, the mother frog inhaled even more air, puffing herself out to double her original size. \"How about now? Am I not equal to him?\"\n\n\"If you try to compare yourself to the ox, you will only hurt yourself!\" warned her children.\n\nIgnoring their sensible advice, the foolish mother frog inhaled with all her remaining strength. She puffed and stretched until—BOOM! Her skin tore apart, and she burst completely.\n\nFoolish vanity will eventually lead to self-destruction.", "Grade_Pre2": "A venerable matriarch of a frog colony resided alongside a tranquil marsh, notorious among her peers for an inflated sense of self-importance. One sultry afternoon, a colossal ox strolled down to the water's edge to drink, inadvertently crushing several small plants and shaking the surrounding soil with his ponderous steps.\n\nWitnessing this display of sheer magnitude, the juvenile frogs fled in terror to their mother. \"Mother, we have just encountered an incomprehensible behemoth!\" they cried in trembling tones. \"His limbs were as stout as oak trunks, and his stature rivaled a small mountain!\"\n\nIncapable of tolerating the notion that any entity could overshadow her own prestige, the conceited amphibian dismissed their description with contemptuous disdain. \"You are merely exaggerating,\" she scoffed. \"With a modest exertion of willpower, I can readily distend my physique to match that ungainly quadrupeds.\"\n\nTaking a profound inhalation, she stretched her elastic hide, puffing her torso into an awkward sphere. \"Behold!\" she proclaimed proudly. \"Does the intruder surpass this magnitude?\"\n\n\"By an immense margin, Mother!\" her offspring exclaimed candidly. \"Your present dimension is negligible in comparison to that monster!\"\n\nInfuriated by their contradiction, the obstinate mother redoubled her efforts. Drawing vast quantities of atmosphere into her lungs, she expanded her membranes to a perilous degree, straining her abdominal tissues beyond their natural elasticity. \"Surely, I have now achieved parity!\" she wheezed through clenched jaws.\n\n\"Cease this madness, Mother!\" pleaded her terrified offspring. \"Even if you were to rupture your own flesh, you could never equal the ox!\"\n\nDeaf to their desperate supplications and dominated entirely by irrational narcissism, the delusional creature drew one final, violent breath. Incapable of withstanding the immense internal pressure, her fragile body abruptly exploded with a sickening snap.\n\nPretentious vanity that refuses to acknowledge natural limitations will inevitably culminate in catastrophic self-annihilation.", "Grade_2": "Within a riparian wetland ecosystem, a matriarchal amphibian exercised informal dominance over her cohort, driven by an acute manifestation of megalomania and unyielding narcissistic entitlement. Her psychological stability was fundamentally contingent upon maintaining an unchallenged monopoly on local admiration. Consequently, when an immense herbivorous bovine—an ox of gigantic proportions—lumbered to the littoral margin to quench his metabolic thirst, the seismic impact of his physical mass destabilized her carefully cultivated regime of prestige.\n\nTerrified by this visual encounter with biological magnitude, the juvenile offspring sought sanctuary beside their parent, breathlessly recounting the phenomenon. They depicted an organism of titanic physical dimensions whose mass displaced the marshland waters and whose hooves pulverized geological formations. Incapable of reconciling this objective reality with her pathological self-concept, the matriarch immediately exhibited cognitive dissonance, rationalizing that perceived biological disparities could be surmounted through sheer mechanical inflation.\n\nIn an absurd attempt to fabricate biometric parity, she initiated forced pulmonary expansion, distending her dermis and subcutaneous tissues through hyperventilation. \"Observe my volumetric adaptation,\" she demanded imperiously. \"Does this synthetic expansion approximate the dimensions of the intruder?\"\n\n\"Your current volume represents a statistically negligible fraction of that organism,\" the progeny responded with unvarnished empirical candor. \"Any attempt to bridge this evolutionary chasm through volumetric inflation is biologically delusional.\"\n\nProvoked to paroxysms of narcissistic rage by this factual contradiction, the creature accelerated her hyper-inflationary regimen. Inhaling atmospheric gases with desperate vigor, she pressurized her coelomic cavity to critical structural thresholds, inducing severe micro-tearing across her vascularized membrane. Her circulatory and respiratory apparatuses bordered on catastrophic structural failure, yet her compulsive fixation upon simulated equality precluded rational self-preservation. \"Behold!\" she gasped through severely distorted vocal cords. \"I have definitively eradicated the disparity!\"\n\n\"Desist immediately, Mother!\" the juvenile observers shrieked in horror. \"Biological constraints are immutable; structural compromise is imminent!\"\n\nSubordinating somatic survival to the desperate preservation of an untenable illusion, the delusional organism forced a culminating volume of compressed atmosphere into her compromised anatomy. Surpassing the tensile strength of her biological tissues, the hydrostatic pressure triggered explosive structural decompression. In an instant, the organism disintegrated into visceral fragments, leaving her stunned offspring amidst the silent marsh.\n\nUnfettered megalomania that rejects biological reality inevitably precipitates catastrophic structural collapse; attempting to simulate parity with the insurmountable terminates in complete self-annihilation.", "Grade_Pre1": "In the micro-ecological stratification of a secluded marshland, an aged amphibian matriarch held despotic sway over her lacustrine domain, driven by a pathological manifestation of unchecked grandiosity. Her cognitive equilibrium was inextricably tethered to an unassailable conviction of her own supreme distinction. This fragile psychosocial superstructure was profoundly destabilized, however, when a massive ungulate—a bull of colossal anatomical proportions—lumbered to the shoreline to sate its thirst. The sheer kinetic displacement of its physical presence sent seismic tremors through the marshland, abruptly reducing the amphibian colony to absolute insignificance.\n\nParalyzed by the manifestation of such sheer physical scale, her juvenile offspring retreated frantically to their maternal guardian, breathless with terror. In stammering tones, they depicted an organism of incomprehensible magnitude whose massive limbs rivaled ancient trees and whose stride shook the marshy terrain. Incapable of assimilating empirical data that threatened her entrenched delusions of absolute distinction, the matriarch succumbed to catastrophic cognitive distortion. Rather than accepting the insurmountable biological chasm separating her species from the mammalian leviathan, she rationalized that physical parity could be simulated via forced volumetric expansion.\n\nExecuting a grotesque physiological experiment, she inhaled deeply, stretching her elastic dermis to grotesque structural tolerances. \"Behold this anatomical adaptation,\" she proclaimed with haughty arrogance. \"Does this synthetic expansion rival the dimensions of the intruder?\"\n\n\"By an insurmountable margin, Mother!\" the progeny responded with terrifying candor. \"Your current dimension constitutes an infinitesimal fraction of that creature's bulk. Attempting to bridge this evolutionary disparity through somatic inflation represents an exercise in pure delirium.\"\n\nEnraged by this factual contradiction and incapable of tolerating the puncture of her psychological vanity, the obstinate creature redoubled her hyper-inflationary exertion. Drawing massive volumes of atmosphere into her pulmonary apparatus, she expanded her vascularized membrane to perilous structural limits, the pressure stretching her epidermal tissues to the threshold of rupture. \"Witness my triumphant parity!\" she hissed through compressed jaws.\n\n\"Desist, we implore you, Mother!\" her terrified brood wailed in unison. \"Natural boundaries cannot be abrogated by vanity; physical rupture is imminent!\"\n\nDeaf to their desperate supplications and dominated by an irrepressible narcissistic drive, the obstinate organism executed a final, catastrophic inhalation. Exceeding the absolute tensile limits of her biological architecture, internal atmospheric pressure ruptured her organic boundaries. In a split second of violent decompression, the organism literally disintegrated into visceral fragments, leaving her traumatized progeny amidst the tranquil marshland.\n\nUnbridled vanity that refuses to defer to biological or circumstantial boundaries culminates inexorably in catastrophic self-immolation; the compulsive urge to simulate parity with the transcendent invariably precipitates complete annihilation.", "Classic_Original": "An Ox, drinking at a pool, stepped on a family of young frogs and crushed one of them to death. When the mother frog came home, she asked where her little one was. \"A huge beast came by,\" said one of the brothers, \"and crushed him under his big foot.\" \"How big was he?\" asked the mother frog, puffing herself out. \"Was he as big as this?\" \"Oh, much bigger than that!\" replied the young frog. The mother puffed herself out more and more, asking, \"Was he this big?\" \"Cease your puffing, mother,\" said the son, \"for if you burst yourself, you will never equal the beast.\" But the foolish frog tried once more, blew herself up even bigger, and burst!\n\nSelf-conceit may lead to self-destruction.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 16, "key": "bat_birds_beasts", "titleEn": "The Bat, Birds, and Beasts", "titleJa": "コウモリと鳥と獣", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_bat_birds_beasts.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "Long ago, a big war started between the birds and the beasts. A bat did not want to join the war. He decided to wait and see who would win.\n\nAt first, the birds were winning the battle. The bat flew to the birds and said, \"Look at my wings! I have wings, so I am a bird!\" The birds welcomed him.\n\nLater, the beasts became stronger and started to win. The bat quickly left the birds and ran to the beasts. \"Look at my teeth and fur! I have no feathers, so I am a beast!\" he said. The beasts welcomed him, too.\n\nFinally, the war ended, and both sides became friends again. They made peace.\n\nHowever, both the birds and the beasts discovered the bat's trick. \"You are not a true friend to anyone,\" they said angrily.\n\nBoth sides rejected the bat. From that day on, the bat could not show his face in the daytime. He had to hide in dark caves and fly only at night.\n\nHe who tries to please everyone pleases no one.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a fierce conflict broke out between the birds of the air and the beasts of the field. Being timid and selfish, a bat decided to remain neutral until he was certain which side would emerge victorious.\n\nIn the beginning, the birds seemed to have the advantage. Seeing their success, the bat flew over to the birds and declared, \"I am clearly one of you! Look at my broad wings.\" The birds accepted him as a comrade.\n\nHowever, as the war continued, the beasts gained the upper hand. The sly bat immediately changed his loyalty and joined the beasts. \"I am definitely a beast,\" he claimed. \"Look at my sharp teeth and fur! Birds do not have teeth.\" The beasts welcomed him into their army.\n\nWhen the long conflict finally came to an end, the birds and beasts signed a peace treaty. As they shared their experiences, they soon uncovered the bat's deceitful behavior.\n\nDisgusted by his dishonesty, both groups rejected the bat completely and banished him from their territories.\n\nEver since, the bat has been forced to live in dark caves, flying silently only after nightfall to avoid being seen.\n\nThose who try to stand on both sides will eventually find themselves isolated from everyone.", "Grade_Pre2": "A devastating warfare erupted between the feathered avian populations of the skies and the terrestrial quadrupeds inhabiting the forests. Motivated exclusively by cowardly self-preservation, an opportunistic bat resolved to adopt a stance of ambiguous neutrality, adamantly refusing to commit his allegiance until the final outcome of the hostilities became unmistakable.\n\nDuring the initial skirmishes, the aerial forces inflicted substantial casualties upon their ground-based adversaries. Observing that the birds had secured a commanding tactical advantage, the bat descended among their ranks, triumphantly exhibiting his membranous pinions. \"Behold my magnificent wings!\" he proclaimed enthusiastically. \"Undoubtedly, my biological lineage aligns me with the feathered kingdom.\" Welcoming this seemingly loyal recruit, the flock embraced him without skepticism.\n\nNevertheless, the fortunes of war shifted dramatically when the beasts consolidated their legions and mounted a ferocious counteroffensive. Recognizing that the terrestrial forces were rapidly gaining the upper hand, the unprincipled opportunist defected without the slightest hesitation. Presenting himself before the commanding beasts, he ostentatiously displayed his razor-sharp dentition and furry hide. \"Do not be misled by my appendages,\" he insisted persuasively. \"True birds possess neither teeth nor mammalian fur; therefore, I am an unequivocal beast.\" Readily convinced by his cunning rationalization, the beasts admitted him into their confederation.\n\nEventually, both factions negotiated a diplomatic reconciliation, signing a comprehensive peace treaty to terminate the protracted hostilities. During the subsequent festivities, delegates from both realms compared intelligence, promptly exposing the bat's duplicitous maneuvers.\n\nRevolted by such shameless perfidy, both communities formally condemned the traitor and permanently stripped him of citizenship within their sovereign borders. Ostracized by all living creatures, the disowned outcast was driven into subterranean caverns, condemned to nocturnal obscurity and eternal solitude.\n\nUnprincipled opportunism may yield temporary advantages, but chronic disloyalty inevitably results in total alienation and universal contempt.", "Grade_2": "Geopolitical polarization between the sovereign avian confederacy and the terrestrial mammalian coalition degenerated into total, unmitigated warfare across the biome. Confronted by this systemic existential clash, an amphibious chiropteran—a bat occupying an ambiguous phylogenetic niche—rejected ideological commitment, electing instead to operationalize calculated, cynical non-alignment. His strategic calculus was predicated entirely upon minimizing personal vulnerability while positioning himself to extract geopolitical patronage from the eventual victor.\n\nDuring the opening campaign, air superiority doctrine enabled the avian armadas to decimate ground formations through devastating aerial bombardment. Perceiving that the strategic initiative had shifted decisively in favor of the winged coalition, the bat executed an immediate diplomatic pivot. Presenting himself before the avian council, he rhetorically emphasized his aerodynamic morphology, waving his elongated interdigital membranes as conclusive proof of phylogenetic solidarity. \"My functional adaptation for atmospheric flight definitively confirms my sovereign allegiance to the avian collective,\" he asserted with manipulative eloquence. Swayed by confirmation bias and eager to augment their ranks, the avian leadership accredited his credentials without rigorous background vetting.\n\nHowever, the dynamics of protracted warfare rarely conform to linear projections. Regrouping their armored divisions, the terrestrial beasts launched a catastrophic counteroffensive, neutralizing aerial dominance and encircling key strongholds. Discerning the imminent collapse of avian hegemony, the unprincipled diplomat perpetrated an immediate ideological apostasy. Defecting across battle lines, he petitioned the mammalian high command, strategically shifting his taxonomy from flight mechanics to morphological dentition and maternal nursing traits. \"Observe my canine teeth and pelage,\" he argued persuasively. \"Aviation constitutes merely a superficial locomotion mechanism; fundamentally, my biological essence resides within the mammalian hierarchy.\" Satisfied by this expedient rationalization, the beasts integrated him into their operational cadre.\n\nUpon the formal cessation of hostilities, the belligerents convened a peace congress to negotiate demilitarization and post-war territorial demarcation. During bilateral intelligence exchanges, security officials uncovered irreconcilable discrepancies in the chiropteran's historical record, thoroughly exposing his cynical duplicity.\n\nThe collective response of both sovereign bodies was immediate and uncompromising. Formally designating him a persona non grata, the unified coalition revoked his legal status, subjecting him to unconditional banishment from the planetary surface. Stripped of diplomatic immunity and universally abhorred as the quintessential embodiment of moral vacuity, the disenfranchised outcast was relegated to subterranean caverns, permanently consigned to nocturnal isolation and systemic ostracism.\n\nPragmatic opportunism devoid of moral conviction may facilitate transient survival, but calculated duplicity ultimately precipitates total disenfranchisement and universal execration.", "Grade_Pre1": "In the geopolitical arena of an ancient ecosystem, systemic ideological polarization between the aerial avian confederation and the terrestrial mammalian hegemony precipitated total war. Confronted by this catastrophic geopolitical conflagration, an ambivalent chiropteran organism—a bat occupying an ambiguous evolutionary interstice—eschewed moral commitment, adopting instead a posture of calculated diplomatic fence-sitting. His strategic calculus was governed exclusively by an ethos of unprincipled self-preservation, deliberately calibrated to exploit whatever geopolitical equilibrium emerged from the conflagration.\n\nDuring the opening phase of hostilities, aerial blitzkrieg doctrines enabled the winged forces to inflict asymmetrical attrition upon ground divisions. Ascertaining that the momentum had swung decisively toward the avian alliance, the bat executed a seamless opportunistic rapprochement. Infiltrating the avian plenary council, he brandished his elongated dactylopatagium—the aerodynamic flight membrane—as irrefutable proof of shared biological heritage. \"My anatomical adaptation for sustained flight represents an inviolable biological mandate binding my allegiance to the aerial realm,\" he declared with consummate demagoguery. Captivated by confirmation bias and desperate to bolster their depleted ranks, the avian hierarchy accredited his bona fides without rigorous forensic vetting.\n\nHowever, the trajectory of existential conflict is fundamentally non-linear. Consolidating their mechanized ground units, the mammalian legions mounted a devastating counteroffensive, decimating the avian flight wings and besieging their mountain redoubts. Recognizing the imminent evaporation of avian hegemony, the unprincipled opportunist executed a brazen act of geopolitical turncoatism. Traversing sovereign lines under cover of twilight, he presented a petition to the mammalian high command, abruptly reclassifying his taxonomic morphology. \"Disregard my functional flight apparatus,\" he urged with cynical sophistry. \"Aerodynamic propulsion is merely a phenotypic anomaly; my prominent dentition, mammalian pelage, and viviparous heritage firmly anchor my allegiance within the mammalian fraternity.\" Seduced by his rhetorical agility, the mammalian commanders integrated him into their tactical vanguard.\n\nFollowing the armistice, the belligerent sovereigns convened a multilateral peace congress to establish a new regional security architecture. During bilateral intelligence deconfliction, historical reconnaissance archives cross-referenced his duplicitous maneuvers, exposing his systemic ideological prostitution.\n\nThe collective verdict rendered by both sovereign entities was swift, draconian, and irreversible. Unanimously declaring him an outlaw stripped of diplomatic immunity, the joint tribunal condemned the opportunist to total juridical and physical banishment from the biosphere. Ostracized as the archetypal manifestation of unmitigated perfidy and ethical nullity, the wretched pariah was driven into subterranean chasms, condemned to eternal nocturnal obscurity and universal revulsion.\n\nPragmatic equivocation unmoored from ethical conviction may secure ephemeral immunity from conflict, but chronic duplicity inexorably precipitates complete geopolitical disenfranchisement and universal obloquy.", "Classic_Original": "A great battle was about to be fought between the Birds and the Beasts. The Bat, fearing the result, stayed away and waited to see which side would win. When the Birds were winning, the Bat flew among them, claiming to be a bird because he had wings. Later, when the Beasts gained the upper hand, the Bat went over to them, claiming to be a beast because he had teeth and fur. But when peace was declared, both sides recognized his deceit. Ashamed and rejected by all, the Bat was forced to hide in dark caves, flying only at night.\n\nHe that is friend to all is friend to none.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 17, "key": "belling_the_cat", "titleEn": "Belling the Cat", "titleJa": "ネズミの会議", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_belling_the_cat.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "The mice in a big house had a serious problem. A cruel cat lived in the same house. The cat walked very quietly and caught a mouse every day. The mice were terrified.\n\nOne night, the mice held a meeting to discuss a plan. \"We must find a way to know when the cat is coming,\" said one mouse.\n\nMany mice spoke, but no one had a good idea. \n\nAt last, a young mouse stood up proudly. \"I have a wonderful idea!\" he said. \"Let's tie a small bell around the cat's neck. When the cat walks, the bell will ring! Then we can hear it and run away easily.\"\n\nAll the mice cheered and clapped their hands. \"What a great idea!\" they shouted.\n\nThen, a wise old mouse stood up slowly. He looked around the room and asked quietly, \"That is indeed a smart plan. But tell me—who will put the bell on the cat?\"\n\nThe room became completely quiet. No mouse volunteered.\n\nTalking is easy, but doing is difficult.", "Grade_3": "The mice living in a large estate were suffering from a severe crisis. A fierce cat was constantly hunting them, creeping so silently that no one could predict her approach. As a result, the mice lived in constant fear and were afraid to leave their holes.\n\nTo solve this life-threatening problem, the mice summoned a general council to brainstorm a strategy. \n\nAfter several useless proposals had been made, a young mouse stepped forward with great confidence. \"I have devised an excellent solution,\" he announced. \"We should attach a small silver bell to a ribbon and fasten it around the cat's neck. Whenever she moves, the bell will jingle, giving us ample warning to escape safely!\"\n\nHearing this clever proposal, the assembly erupted in applause, praising the young mouse for his brilliant mind.\n\nHowever, an experienced old mouse, who had remained silent until then, stood up slowly. He smiled faintly and said, \"The proposal is certainly ingenious. However, I have one simple question: Which one of us is brave enough to bell the cat?\"\n\nUpon hearing this question, the cheering stopped instantly. The mice looked at each other in silence, realizing that not a single member was willing to execute the dangerous plan.\n\nIt is easy to propose grand ideas, but carrying them out in reality is far more difficult.", "Grade_Pre2": "The rodent community inhabiting an ancient manor house was confronted with an existential catastrophe. A relentless feline predator terrorized their domain, stalking her quarry with such noiseless precision that her deadly assaults were virtually undetectable until it was too late. Paralyzed by perpetual dread, the mice suffered severe deprivation, restricted to their subterranean crevices and unable to forage for basic sustenance.\n\nRecognizing that collective inaction would inevitably culminate in total extermination, the elder rodents convened an emergency assembly to deliberate upon defensive countermeasures. Numerous proposals were submitted, yet each was sequentially dismissed as impractical or inadequate.\n\nAt length, an articulate young mouse ascended the podium, radiating self-assurance. \"Distinguished peers,\" he proclaimed with theatrical eloquence, \"I have formulated an infallible remedy for our collective affliction. Let us affix a miniature brass bell to a collar and attach it securely around the neck of our nemesis. The acoustic reverberation generated by her movements will provide infallible advance notice, enabling us to seek refuge long before she enters striking range!\"\n\nElectrified by this ostensibly flawless innovation, the assembly erupted in unanimous acclaim. The delegates vociferously lauded the orator, hailing the stratagem as an epoch-making triumph of intellect over brute strength.\n\nAmid the euphoria, however, an aged mouse renowned for prudence rose deliberately to his feet. Raising his paw to solicit silence, he addressed the assembly with measured sobriety. \"The conceptual brilliance of this scheme is undeniable,\" he remarked dryly. \"Nevertheless, its practical efficacy hinges upon one critical operational detail: Who among us is prepared to volunteer to attach the bell?\"\n\nIn an instant, the exuberant jubilation dissipated into an oppressive hush. Glancing anxiously at one another, the mice stood paralyzed by mutual cowardice, painfully forced to acknowledge that an idealistic hypothesis devoid of practical execution remains entirely worthless.\n\nFormulating grand theoretical solutions is deceptively simple, whereas personal willingness to undertake perilous implementation is exceedingly scarce.", "Grade_2": "Within the domestic ecosystem of a rural manor, the indigenous rodent population experienced an existential governance crisis triggered by asymmetric feline predation. The apex carnivore operated with acoustic stealth and tactical lethality, inflicting unsustainable attrition upon the colony. Because traditional sensory mechanisms were incapable of detecting the predator's pre-attack maneuvers, the rodent collective succumbed to functional paralysis, enduring acute nutritional deprivation while confined to sub-floor crevices.\n\nTo mitigate this systemic catastrophe, the administrative council summoned an extraordinary plenary session, mandating the formulation of comprehensive mitigation strategies. The deliberative process, however, was initially paralyzed by cognitive gridlock, as senior delegates iteratively proposed and subsequently invalidated an array of rudimentary evasion tactics.\n\nBreaking the procedural impasse, an ambitious junior delegate commandeered the rostrum, exuding charismatic authority. \"Esteemed colleagues,\" he declaimed with polished rhetorical sophistry, \"the resolution to our strategic vulnerability lies not in passive retreat, but in early-warning sensor deployment. I propose installing an acoustic signaling transducer—specifically, an oscillating bronze chime—affixed directly to the feline cervical perimeter. The kinetic energy generated during predatory locomotion will systematically trigger sound waves, generating early acoustic telemetry that will permit preemptive dispersion before the predator achieves lethal proximity!\"\n\nSeduced by the theoretical coherence of this algorithmic paradigm, the assembly descended into uncritical euphoria. The delegates overwhelmingly ratified the initiative, hailing the presenter as a visionary strategist whose intellectual synthesis had rendered physical asymmetry obsolete.\n\nHowever, the dialectical gap between theoretical architecture and field execution was abruptly illuminated by a veteran technocrat. Rising with solemn gravity, the senior statesman punctured the celebratory delirium with unsparing forensic realism. \"The intellectual elegance of this schematic is beyond dispute,\" he observed with chilling detachment. \"Nevertheless, empirical feasibility is fundamentally contingent upon a single operational prerequisite: Which specific individual among this deliberative body possesses the operational readiness to execute the cervical attachment?\"\n\nThe impact of this interrogation was devastating. The triumphalist rhetoric evaporated instantaneously, replaced by an immobilizing psychological chill. Subdued by collective cowardice, each delegate averted his gaze, confronted with the sobering institutional reality that an immaculate theoretical framework completely disconnected from operational feasibility represents an exercise in cognitive futility.\n\nDesigning sophisticated theoretical paradigms is intellectually trivial; executing dangerous operational mandates constitutes the singular metric of authentic viability.", "Grade_Pre1": "In the micro-political architecture of an aristocratic manor, the subterranean rodent polity confronted an existential governance crisis precipitated by asymmetric feline predation. Operating with auditory stealth and lethal efficiency, the feline predator inflicted catastrophic demographic attrition upon the community. Because the organism’s predatory locomotion circumvented traditional sensory detection, the polity collapsed into administrative and behavioral paralysis, resulting in severe resource starvation as the populace remained restricted to sub-floor cavities.\n\nTo remediate this existential vulnerability, the governing senate convened an extraordinary assembly, mandating the formulation of a defensive security doctrine. The deliberative body, however, rapidly devolved into cognitive paralysis, as senior representatives proposed and sequentially dismissed an array of palliative evasion stratagems.\n\nSensing an opportunity for institutional ascendance, a precocious orator seized the rostrum, exuding charismatic demagoguery. \"Distinguished senators,\" he declaimed with mesmerizing rhetorical panache, \"our systemic vulnerability is not inevitable; rather, it is a technical failure of early-warning intelligence. I propose fabricating a kinetic acoustic beacon—an oscillating brass bell—and securing it around the cervical perimeter of our nemesis. The kinetic friction generated by the predator’s locomotion will emit continuous acoustic telemetry, alerting our sentinels and enabling preemptive evacuation long before the carnivore achieves lethal proximity!\"\n\nSeduced by the conceptual elegance of this theoretical schematic, the assembly succumbed to uncritical institutional euphoria. The legislators vociferously ratified the initiative by acclamation, canonizing the orator as a visionary tactician whose intellectual synthesis had neutralized physical asymmetry.\n\nHowever, the profound chasm separating theoretical modeling from perilous tactical execution was ruthlessly interrogated by an elder statesman. Rising with austere gravitas, the veteran legislator pierced the atmospheric delirium with forensic skepticism. \"The intellectual symmetry of this proposal is undeniably seductive,\" he noted with razor-sharp lucidity. \"Nonetheless, empirical viability is inexorably contingent upon a singular operational bottleneck: Who among this deliberative assembly possesses the physical fortitude and moral temerity to affix the bell to the feline throat?\"\n\nThe rhetorical inquiry delivered an instantaneous psychological shockwave. The triumphalist euphoria dissipated immediately, replaced by an immobilizing, sepulchral silence. Paralyzed by mutual cowardice and an instinctive awareness of mortal vulnerability, the delegates averted their eyes, compelled to confront the sobering reality that an immaculate theoretical framework divorced from operational execution constitutes an exercise in intellectual vanity.\n\nSynthesizing grand theoretical policy is rhetorically effortless; the willingness to hazard mortal peril in its physical implementation constitutes the sole immutable crucible of authentic leadership.", "Classic_Original": "The Mice held a general council to consider what measures they could take to outwit their common enemy, the Cat. Many plans were discussed, but none was thought practical. At last a young Mouse got up and proposed that a bell should be hung around the neck of the Cat. \"Then,\" said he, \"we shall always have notice when she is coming, and can easily escape.\" This proposal was received with applause, until an old Mouse got up and said, \"That is all very well, but who is to bell the Cat?\"\n\nIt is easy to propose, but hard to execute.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 18, "key": "bear_and_two_travelers", "titleEn": "The Bear and the Travelers", "titleJa": "旅人とクマ", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_bear_and_two_travelers.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "Two good friends were walking together on a quiet mountain road. They promised to help each other if any danger came.\n\nSuddenly, a huge bear came out of the forest!\n\nOne traveler quickly ran away, climbed a tall tree, and hid in the leaves. He did not help his friend at all.\n\nThe other traveler could not run fast. He knew that bears do not touch dead bodies. So he dropped to the ground and held his breath. He lay completely still like a dead man.\n\nThe bear walked up to him and smelled his ears, nose, and mouth. The bear thought he was dead, so it walked back into the forest.\n\nWhen the bear was gone, the man in the tree came down. He laughed and asked, \"What did the bear whisper in your ear?\"\n\nThe other man answered quietly, \"The bear gave me good advice. He said: 'Never travel with a friend who leaves you in danger.'\"\n\nA friend in need is a friend indeed.", "Grade_3": "Two companions were traveling together along a lonely forest path. Before setting out, they had made a solemn promise to stand by each other in times of trouble.\n\nSuddenly, a giant bear emerged unexpectedly from the thick bushes, letting out a terrifying roar.\n\nPanicked by the sight, one of the travelers immediately abandoned his friend, sprinted toward a nearby tree, and concealed himself among the high branches.\n\nLeft alone on the path, the other traveler realized he had no chance of escaping or fighting the beast. Remembering that bears rarely attack dead creatures, he collapsed onto the ground, closed his eyes, and held his breath, pretending to be deceased.\n\nThe bear approached the motionless man, sniffing around his ears, nose, and chest. Believing that the man was already dead, the bear lost interest and quietly ambled back into the woods.\n\nOnce the danger had passed, the traveler in the tree climbed down and asked jokingly, \"My friend, I noticed the bear put his snout right next to your ear! What secret did he whisper to you?\"\n\nThe other traveler looked at him coldly and replied, \"He offered me a piece of valuable advice. He warned me never to trust a companion who deserts his friend in a crisis.\"\n\nTrue friends prove their loyalty when danger arrives.", "Grade_Pre2": "Two sworn companions were traversing an isolated wilderness trail, having previously pledged mutual loyalty and sworn to defend one another should adversity arise. However, true character remains untested during times of tranquility, revealing its authenticity only under extreme duress.\n\nWithout prior warning, an immense brown bear burst through the dense underbrush, blocking their forward progress with menacing fury. Overcome by primal terror and disregarding his solemn oath, the first traveler instantly deserted his associate. With desperate agility, he scaled a robust oak tree, securely concealing himself within the dense foliage where the predator could not reach him.\n\nBereft of assistance and recognizing the absolute futility of flight, the abandoned traveler evaluated his precarious dilemma with astonishing composure. Recalling the biological curiosity that bears exhibit an instinctive aversion to lifeless corpses, he deliberately cast himself face-downward upon the earth. Suppressing every reflexive impulse, he arrested his respiration and remained utterly rigid, convincingly feigning mortality.\n\nThe massive beast lumbered toward the prone figure, nudging his limp limbs with its snout and inspecting his ears and nostrils for signs of breath. Finding neither warmth nor heartbeat, the predator concluded that the creature was devoid of life and subsequently retreated into the wilderness.\n\nWhen the imminent peril had fully subsided, the coward descended from his arboreal sanctuary, attempting to mask his treachery with jovial familiarity. \"My good fellow,\" he chuckled deceitfully, \"I observed that the beast placed its mouth directly against your ear. What confidential counsel did it impart to you?\"\n\nGazing at his companion with unyielding severity, the survivor retorted, \"The animal bestowed a profound moral truth upon me: Henceforth, avoid venturing into perilous journeys alongside an associate who abandons you the moment misfortune strikes.\"\n\nAdversity is the ultimate crucible that distinguishes authentic camaraderie from hollow pretense.", "Grade_2": "While navigating a remote and hazardous mountainous expanse, two civilian travelers entered into an explicit reciprocal security covenant, pledging mutual defense against exogenous environmental perils. Sociological observation, however, consistently indicates that rhetorical commitments formulated under benign conditions possess negligible predictive validity when agents are suddenly subjected to severe survival pressure.\n\nThis theoretical axiom was abruptly verified when a predatory ursine monstrosity—a grizzly of immense proportions—breached the perimeter vegetation, obstructing their vector of transit with unmitigated hostility. Paralyzed by primal survival heuristics, the first companion instantly abrogated his contractual obligations. Prioritizing unilateral self-preservation, he leveraged his superior kinetic velocity to ascend an adjacent arboreal structure, embedding himself within the high canopy to achieve complete physical invulnerability.\n\nSimultaneously abandoned and deprived of tactical retreat options, the second traveler was compelled to negotiate an immediate asymmetric existential threat. Recognizing that muscular engagement or terrestrial flight would precipitate immediate fatal interception, he implemented a high-risk behavioral deception based on the predator's scavenger psychology. Leveraging the known ethological phenomenon that predatory ursines exhibit pronounced olfactory aversion to necrotic tissue, he collapsed prone onto the terrain. Systematically repressing autonomic physiological indicators, he induced absolute immobility, arrested pulmonary respiration, and simulated post-mortem rigidity.\n\nThe carnivore approached the inert organism, conducting a rigorous sensory audit. It subjected the subject's cephalic perimeter, auditory canals, and respiratory apertures to intrusive tactile and olfactory probing. Deciphering neither thermal emission nor rhythmic biological vibrations, the predator categorized the biological mass as inert carrion and consequently evacuated the immediate sector.\n\nFollowing the definitive dissipation of the existential hazard, the opportunistic deserter descended from his arboreal redoubt, attempting to rehabilitate his compromised social standing through superficial levity. \"Comrade,\" he inquired with calculated disingenuousness, \"I noted the carnivore delivering an extended acoustic communication into your ear. What classified revelation did it disclose?\"\n\nFixing his gaze upon his erstwhile partner with forensic disdain, the survivor articulated an uncompromising ethical verdict: \"The beast imparted an invaluable piece of tactical counsel: Sever strategic partnerships with any associate whose professed solidarity disintegrates the precise instant existential peril materializes.\"\n\nAdversity serves as an infallible diagnostic mechanism, ruthlessly segregating authentic ethical fidelity from opportunistic social posturing.", "Grade_Pre1": "While traversing an inhospitable alpine wilderness, two itinerant companions entered into a mutual security concordat, solemnly pledging unconditional solidarity should mortal peril manifest. Sociological inquiry reveals, however, that verbal compacts formulated under benign, peacetime conditions possess zero empirical validity when moral agents are abruptly subjected to extreme existential duress.\n\nThis axiom received immediate empirical verification when an apex ursine predator—an enormous brown bear—erupted from the undergrowth, obstructing their path with terrifying ferocity. Paralyzed by autonomic panic and renouncing his ethical obligations, the first traveler unilaterally abrogated the alliance. Exploiting his athletic agility, he scaled a robust oak tree, securing an elevated vantage point in the canopy that guaranteed complete physical immunity while consigning his companion to certain death.\n\nMarooned in the open and recognizing that terrestrial flight was mathematically non-viable, the abandoned traveler confronted immediate annihilation. With remarkable cognitive lucidity, he executed a high-stakes countermeasure predicated upon the predator’s innate ethology. Aware that bears instinctively display profound olfactory aversion to necrotic biological matter, the traveler cast himself face-down into the detritus. Subduing his terrified nervous system, he suspended pulmonary respiration, suppressed the blink reflex, and induced absolute muscular flaccidity to simulate biological decease.\n\nThe massive beast approached the prostrate organism, conducting an intrusive sensory reconnaissance. It prodded his limp anatomy with its snout, inspecting his nostrils and acoustic cavities for the subtlest respiratory emission or cardiac vibration. Registering neither thermal dissipation nor kinetic motion, the predator classified the biomass as inert carrion and presently ambled back into the primordial forest.\n\nOnce the imminent threat had receded, the cowardly defector scrambled down from his arboreal sanctuary, attempting to sanitize his treason through patronizing facetiousness. \"My intrepid comrade,\" he smirked with transparent disingenuousness, \"I observed the beast whispering into your ear. What esoteric wisdom did the oracle impart?\"\n\nFixing his gaze upon his former associate with icy contempt, the survivor delivered an unsparing moral indictment: \"The creature conferred an indispensable behavioral axiom: Terminate all collaboration with any partner whose professed fidelity evaporates the precise moment adversity demands genuine sacrifice.\"\n\nAdversity acts as an infallible crucible; it ruthlessly strips away rhetorical pretense, permanently bifurcating authentic moral fidelity from the hollow posturing of self-interested opportunism.", "Classic_Original": "Two friends were traveling on the same road together when a Bear suddenly appeared out of the forest. One of them quickly climbed up into a tree and hid himself among the branches. The other, seeing that he had no chance alone against the Bear, fell flat upon the ground and held his breath, pretending to be a corpse. The Bear came up, smelled his ears and nose, and believing him to be a corpse, walked away. When the danger was past, the friend in the tree came down and asked jokingly, \"What did the Bear whisper in your ear?\" The other replied, \"He gave me this advice: Never travel with a friend who deserts you in the face of danger.\"\n\nMisfortune tests the sincerity of friends.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 19, "key": "lions_share", "titleEn": "The Lion's Share", "titleJa": "獅子の分け前", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_lions_share.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A lion, a fox, a jackal, and a wolf went hunting together. They promised to share all the food equally.\n\nAfter a long chase, they caught a big deer. The wolf divided the deer into four equal parts.\n\nBefore anyone could eat, the lion stood up and roared. \"Wait!\" he said. \"I will take the first part because I am the king of the forest.\"\n\nThe lion continued, \"I will also take the second part because I am the strongest hunter.\"\n\n\"And I will take the third part,\" the lion added, \"because I fought harder than any of you.\"\n\nThen, the lion looked fiercely at the three animals. \"Now, if anyone wants the fourth part, you must fight me for it!\"\n\nThe fox, the jackal, and the wolf said nothing. They walked away hungry, leaving all the food to the powerful lion.\n\nMight makes right.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, a mighty lion formed an alliance with three smaller beasts—a fox, a jackal, and a wolf. They agreed to hunt together and share their prey into four equal portions.\n\nAfter working hard all day, they successfully captured a large stag. The wolf carefully divided the meat into four equal shares so that each partner would receive a fair amount.\n\nHowever, just as they were about to enjoy their meal, the lion stepped forward arrogantly and raised his paw. \"Hold on!\" he commanded. \"I am claiming the first share because I am the supreme ruler of these woods.\"\n\nHe then gestured to the next piece. \"The second share belongs to me as well, because I contributed the most strength during the hunt.\"\n\nWithout pausing, the lion took the third share. \"I am taking this portion too, because my bravery was far superior to yours.\"\n\nFinally, the lion glared menacingly at his terrified partners. \"As for the fourth and final share,\" he growled, \"anyone who dares to touch it will have to challenge me to a fight to the death!\"\n\nRealizing that it was impossible to argue with such a tyrant, the three animals silently surrendered their shares and retreated into the forest, leaving the lion to enjoy the entire prize alone.\n\nPartnerships with the powerful are rarely fair or equal.", "Grade_Pre2": "A formidable lion entered into a hunting coalition with three subordinate carnivores: a fox, a jackal, and a wolf. Recognizing that their combined capabilities would significantly enhance their hunting efficiency, the quadruple partnership solemnly ratified a covenant stipulating that all captured quarry would be partitioned into four strictly equivalent dividends.\n\nFollowing an exhaustive pursuit across rugged terrain, the allied predators succeeded in bringing down an enormous stag. In accordance with their prior accord, the conscientious wolf meticulously dissected the carcass into four identical allotments, ensuring complete parity among the participants.\n\nHowever, just as the lesser carnivores prepared to claim their legitimate shares, the apex predator intervened with imperial arrogance. Planting his massive paw upon the first portion, the monarch declared authoritatively, \"This primary dividend is rightfully mine by virtue of royal prerogative, for I am the undisputed sovereign of this realm.\"\n\nWithout waiting for dissent, the lion laid claim to the subsequent partition. \"The second allotment likewise reverts to me, acknowledging my decisive physical superiority during the final struggle.\"\n\nContinuing his systematic expropriation, the tyrant confiscated the third section. \"This portion is similarly non-negotiable, serving as just compensation for my peerless courage, which manifestly eclipsed your modest contributions.\"\n\nFinally, casting an intimidating glare over his trembling cohorts, the despot issued an explicit ultimatum regarding the remaining fragment: \"Whoever among you harbors the audacious temerity to touch this final share must be prepared to contend with my lethal fury in mortal combat!\"\n\nAcknowledging the utter futility of appealing to abstract principles of justice against overwhelming physical supremacy, the subdued partners forfeited their entitlements without uttering a single complaint. Withdrawing into the forest with empty stomachs, they learned that entering an ostensibly equitable partnership with a powerful autocrat is merely a perilous illusion.\n\nIn relationships dominated by radical power imbalances, formal agreements provide no meaningful protection against tyrannical coercion.", "Grade_2": "In the harsh jurisprudence of the wilderness, a hegemonic apex predator—a majestic male lion—negotiated a multilateral hunting syndicate comprising three peripheral meso-predators: a vulpine, a jackal, and a wolf. Seeking to optimize thermodynamic efficiency in resource acquisition, the consortium formally established an ostensibly egalitarian contractual framework. The foundational charter explicitly codified that any biomass procured through collaborative labor would be apportioned into four mathematically indistinguishable quotas, guaranteeing equitable distributive justice.\n\nDeploying coordinated pack-hunting tactics, the predatory syndicate successfully cornered and neutralized a mature, high-yield cervid stag. Discharging his administrative obligation with scrupulous fidelity, the wolf executed the anatomical division of the carcass, arranging four perfectly symmetrical allotments of organic sustenance to facilitate impartial liquidation.\n\nHowever, the transition from collective production to resource distribution invariably exposes structural power asymmetries. Before the secondary participants could formalize their claims, the hegemonic sovereign intervened, establishing a physical blockade over the commodity. Restating the distribution protocols through a unilateral reinterpretation of sovereignty, the monarch asserted: \"The initial quadrant is allocated to my estate under the doctrine of sovereign prerogative, reflecting my uncontested ontological status as absolute ruler.\"\n\nPreempting procedural objection, the tyrant annexed the second quota through an appeal to marginal productivity: \"The subsequent allotment naturally accedes to my jurisdiction as requisite compensation for superior kinetic contribution, given that the terminal takedown was achieved solely through my muscular supremacy.\"\n\nExtending his predatory expropriation, the despot claimed the tertiary dividend: \"This section is similarly non-distributable, constituting an entitlement derived from disproportionate risk assumption and unparalleled martial fortitude, which objectively eclipsed the marginal labor of ancillary subordinates.\"\n\nHaving systematically monopolized seventy-five percent of the shared asset under pseudo-legal pretexts, the autocrat discarded dialectical rationalization and weaponized raw physical intimidation regarding the residual quarter. Glaring at his demoralized confederates with lethal malice, the apex predator issued a non-negotiable decree: \"Any entity harboring the reckless insolence to contest this terminal parcel must be prepared to litigate the dispute through unmitigated physical combat against my absolute monopoly on violence!\"\n\nConfronted with the stark reality that legalistic appeals to distributive justice are structurally impotent against monopolistic force, the disenfranchised meso-predators conceded their contractual entitlements without vocal resistance. Retreating into the scrubland to endure enforced starvation, the dispossessed partners absorbed a fundamental axiom of realpolitik: entering ostensibly multilateral compacts with autocratic monopolies yields nothing beyond institutionalized exploitation.\n\nWhen contractual frameworks lack independent enforcement mechanisms, formal covenants merely provide ideological camouflage for coercive expropriation by dominant power centers.", "Grade_Pre1": "In the unsparing realpolitik of the primeval biosphere, a hegemonic apex carnivore—an adult male lion possessing absolute physical supremacy—orchestrated a predatory cartel with three peripheral scavengers: a fox, a jackal, and a wolf. Driven by an imperative to optimize energetic efficiency during foraging operations, the alliance ratified an ostensibly egalitarian treaty. This charter explicitly mandated that any caloric windfall procured through collaborative labor would be partitioned into four mathematically identical dividends, guaranteeing symmetrical distributive equity.\n\nExecuting coordinated pursuit tactics, the coalition cornered and dispatched an immense, prime-condition stag. Fulfilling his administrative obligations with punctilious fidelity, the wolf dissected the carcass into four geometrically symmetrical quotas, methodically preparing the haul for equitable liquidation.\n\nHowever, the sociological transition from collective capital generation to surplus allocation invariably unmasks structural hegemony. Before the subordinate partners could stake their legitimate claims, the sovereign intervened, establishing martial control over the shared commodity. Reconstructing the distribution protocols through a cynical manipulation of executive prerogative, the despot proclaimed: \"The initial quadrant reverts to my sovereign jurisdiction under the unassailable doctrine of royal prerogative, acknowledging my supreme ontological status as absolute ruler.\"\n\nPrecluding procedural grievance, the tyrant annexed the second quota through an appeal to marginal productivity: \"The secondary allotment naturally falls under my exclusive entitlement as compensation for superior kinetic labor, given that the terminal takedown was executed solely through my formidable muscular apparatus.\"\n\nAccelerating his predatory expropriation, the autocrat claimed the tertiary segment: \"This portion is similarly non-negotiable, constituting a mandatory entitlement derived from disproportionate risk assumption and unparalleled martial fortitude, which rendered your auxiliary contributions completely inconsequential.\"\n\nHaving systematically confiscated seventy-five percent of the collaborative asset through pseudo-legal sophistry, the despot abandoned procedural pretense regarding the residual quadrant, brandishing raw, unadulterated coercion. Glaring at his demoralized partners with lethal menace, the apex predator issued an absolute ultimatum: \"Whoever among you harbors the reckless insolence to contest this terminal parcel must be prepared to litigate the adjudication in mortal hand-to-hand combat against my unmitigated monopoly on physical violence!\"\n\nRecognizing that legalistic appeals to distributive equity are functionally impotent when confronted by hegemonic violence, the disenfranchised meso-predators surrendered their contractual entitlements without voicing protest. Retreating into the shadows of the wilderness to endure enforced starvation, the dispossessed partners absorbed a foundational axiom of political realism: multilateral compacts entered into alongside autocratic monopolies serve merely as institutional facades designed to legitimize despotic extortion.\n\nAbsent external enforcement mechanisms, formal contractual agreements provide zero institutional safeguard against despotic predation; egalitarian treaties negotiated in the shadow of radical power asymmetries inevitably degenerate into instruments of unilateral expropriation.", "Classic_Original": "A Lion, a Fox, a Jackal, and a Wolf went hunting together in the forest and caught a fine stag. They agreed to divide the prey into four equal parts. The Lion stepped forward and declared, \"I take the first portion because I am the King of beasts. I take the second portion because I am the strongest partner. I take the third portion because I fought hardest.\" Then he glared at the others and added, \"As for the fourth portion, if any of you touches it, he will have to fight me!\" The three animals silently walked away, leaving the entire stag to the Lion.\n\nMight makes right.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 20, "key": "frog_and_mouse", "titleEn": "The Frog and the Mouse", "titleJa": "ネズミとカエル", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_frog_and_mouse.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A mouse and a frog became friends. However, the frog was wicked and wanted to trick the mouse.\n\nOne day, the frog tied the mouse's leg to his own leg with a string. \"Come with me to my home in the pond!\" the frog said. \n\nThe mouse was afraid of water, but he could not escape. The frog swam into the deep water and dived under. The mouse drowned and died.\n\nWhile the dead mouse floated on the water, a big hawk flew in the sky. The hawk saw the floating mouse and swooped down. He grabbed the mouse with his sharp claws and carried him into the air.\n\nBecause the frog was still tied to the mouse, the hawk carried the frog, too! The hawk ate both the mouse and the frog for lunch.\n\nIf you try to hurt others, you will hurt yourself.", "Grade_3": "Once upon a time, an innocent mouse befriended a deceitful frog. Although the mouse trusted him completely, the frog harbored a cruel plan to harm his companion.\n\nOne morning, the frog tied one of the mouse's feet to his own with a strong string. \"Let us travel together across the pond so that I can show you my wonderful aquatic kingdom,\" the frog suggested.\n\nAlthough the mouse was hesitant because he could not swim, he was forced to follow. As soon as they reached the middle of the pond, the frog dived beneath the surface, dragging the helpless mouse under the water. The poor mouse struggled desperately, but he soon drowned.\n\nAs the mouse's body floated on the surface, a hungry hawk flying high above spotted the easy prey. The hawk swooped down instantly and seized the dead mouse in its sharp talons.\n\nSince the frog was still firmly attached to the mouse by the string, he was pulled out of the water as well! The hawk flew to a high branch and devoured both animals together.\n\nThose who set traps for others will eventually fall into their own destruction.", "Grade_Pre2": "A trusting terrestrial mouse established an amicable relationship with an amphibious frog, completely oblivious to the malevolent malice festering within his associate's mind. Harboring a perverse hostility toward creatures inhabiting dry land, the treacherous amphibian conceived a premeditated plot to assassinate his companion.\n\nUnder the fraudulent pretext of introducing the mouse to the wonders of aquatic life, the frog proposed a joint excursion across a tranquil lagoon. To ensure that they remained united during their journey, the conniving instigator bound one of the mouse's hind limbs securely to his own with a robust reed fiber. Intimidated by the unfamiliar aquatic environment yet reluctant to doubt his friend's sincerity, the apprehensive mouse reluctantly acquiesced to the arrangement.\n\nInitially, the frog swam gently across the surface, disarming any lingering reservations. However, upon reaching the deepest section of the pool, the traitor executed his heinous design. With sudden violence, he submerged abruptly, relentlessly dragging the non-swimming rodent beneath the dark water. Despite thrashing desperately in a futile bid for survival, the suffocated mammal rapidly succumbed to asphyxiation, his lifeless corpse subsequently bobbing to the surface.\n\nGleeful over the successful consummation of his treachery, the amphibian floated beneath the corpse, savoring his cruelty. However, retributive justice struck from the heavens with terrifying velocity. A soaring kite scanning the water for carrion intercepted the conspicuous silhouette. Plunging like an arrow, the raptor clamped its formidable talons onto the floating carcass and ascended rapidly into the stratosphere.\n\nBecause the submerged traitor remained inextricably linked to his victim by the indestructible cord, the frog was involuntarily hauled into the atmosphere alongside the deceased rodent. Realizing his inescapable doom, the shrieking amphibian was carried away to a desolate precipice, where the raptor expeditiously devoured both conspirator and victim in a single feast.\n\nPerfidious cruelty contains the seeds of its own destruction, ensuring that those who orchestrate the annihilation of the innocent inevitably bind themselves to identical ruin.", "Grade_2": "In an ecological interface bridging aquatic and terrestrial habitats, a naive terrestrial rodent initiated an interspecies association with an amphibious anuran. Psychologically predisposed to goodwill, the mammalian partner remained entirely oblivious to the sociopathic malice harbored by his counterpart. Resenting terrestrial sovereignty and harboring a morbid compulsion to demonstrate aquatic supremacy, the duplicitous frog formulated a premeditated conspiracy designed to liquidate his associate under the guise of pastoral camaraderie.\n\nTo operationalize his homicidal design, the amphibian fabricated an enticing narrative of botanical tourism, inviting the unsuspecting rodent to inspect submerged benthic ecosystems. Overcoming the mammal's instinctive hydrophobia, the instigator proposed a binding ligature—a durable botanical cord fashioned from fibrous reeds—affixed securely between their respective limbs, disingenuously framing the apparatus as a precautionary safety tether. Paralyzed by the dread of appearing ungrateful and subverting his rational anxieties to social compliance, the gullible rodent capitulated to the lethal entanglement.\n\nUpon navigating beyond the littoral shallows into pelagic depths, the conspirator initiated the terminal phase of his scheme. Abruptly diving toward the benthic sediment, the frog mobilized his specialized propulsion to drag the buoyant, non-adapted mammal beneath the water line. The rodent's desperate physiological convulsions proved utterly futile against fluid dynamics; within minutes, acute hypoxia induced respiratory collapse, resulting in terminal drowning. As cellular respiration ceased, the buoyant corpse bobbed inertly upon the liquid surface, anchored invisibly to the lurking perpetrator beneath.\n\nWhile the perfidious anuran lingered beneath the floating cadaver, indulging in premature self-congratulation, apex aerial surveillance altered the trajectory of the encounter. An opportunistic raptor—a red kite surveying the lagoon for biomass—detected the conspicuous horizontal displacement of the buoyant mammal. Executing a steep parabolic dive, the bird of prey embedded its razor-sharp talons into the floating mammalian flesh, immediately initiating high-velocity vertical ascension.\n\nCrucially, the physical ligature that had functioned as an instrument of deliberate murder now transformed into an inescapable conduit of retributive doom. Inextricably anchored to the ascending carcass, the submerged amphibian was violently yanked across the surface tension and catapulted into the atmosphere. Incapable of severing the synthetic bond, the screaming anuran was transported to a precipitous cliffside redoubt, where the raptor systematically dismembered and devoured both the innocent casualty and the treacherous architect of the catastrophe.\n\nMalicious conspiracies engineered against the vulnerable contain an intrinsic boomerang dynamic; those who bind others to unjustified destruction inadvertently construct the precise mechanisms that guarantee their own catastrophic demise.", "Grade_Pre1": "In the liminal ecological boundary separating terrestrial scrubland from a lacustrine marsh, an unsuspecting terrestrial rodent entered into a perilous interspecies entente with an amphibious anuran. Governed by a psychological disposition toward uncritical sociability, the naive mammal was fundamentally incapable of deciphering the sociopathic malice festering within his companion’s psyche. Animated by a profound, pathological resentment of terrestrial creatures and harboring a perverse compulsion to demonstrate aquatic hegemony, the duplicitous amphibian synthesized a premeditated conspiracy designed to liquidate his companion under the disingenuous guise of recreational tourism.\n\nTo execute this homicidal stratagem, the amphibian fabricated an enticing narrative of botanical tourism, inviting the impressionable rodent to inspect subterranean aquatic wonders. Countering the mammal’s instinctive, evolutionarily justified hydrophobia, the instigator engineered a synthetic ligature—a tensile cord woven from fibrous marsh reed—affixed securely between their adjacent hind limbs. He duplicitously framed this fatal mechanism as an indispensable safety harness designed to guarantee mutual security during the aquatic voyage. Overcome by normative social pressure and dreading the social stigma of seeming discourteous, the gullible victim subordinated rational self-preservation, capitulating unconditionally to the lethal constraint.\n\nUpon transitioning from the littoral perimeter into the abyssal depths of the marsh, the conspirator executed the terminal phase of his betrayal. Diving with calculated, sudden violence, the amphibian deployed his specialized hydrodynamic propulsion to plunge his buoyant, non-swimming associate beneath the surface. The rodent’s frantic muscular convulsions proved pathetically inconsequential against fluid dynamic resistance; within moments, acute pulmonary asphyxiation induced catastrophic systemic collapse, resulting in biological cessation. As vital signs extinguished, the buoyant carcass floated upon the surface film, bound invisibly to the perfidious conspirator lurking in the depths.\n\nWhile the anuran lingered beneath the floating corpse, indulging in euphoric self-congratulation, apex aerial surveillance irrevocably reconfigured the outcome. A soaring raptor—a predatory kite conducting systematic reconnaissance for carrion—intercepted the distinctive visual signature of the floating mammalian carcass. Executing a steep parabolic dive, the raptor embedded its talons into the cadaver with concussive velocity, immediately commencing high-speed vertical ascension.\n\nWhereupon, the synthetic tether that had functioned as an instrument of premeditated murder converted inexorably into a conduit of poetic retribution. Bound irrevocably to the ascending carcass, the submerged conspirator was violently wrenched through the surface tension, catapulted upward into the open sky. Incapable of severing the ligature, the shrieking amphibian was borne aloft to a desolate cliffside precipice, where the raptor systematically dismembered and devoured both the innocent casualty and the perfidious architect of the catastrophe.\n\nConspiracies engineered to victimize the defenseless possess an immutable, self-cannibalizing momentum; those who bind others to unjust doom inadvertently fashion the precise operational instruments of their own catastrophic immolation.", "Classic_Original": "A Mouse became friends with a Frog, but the Frog harbored wicked intentions. One day, the Frog tied the Mouse's leg to his own with a strong thread, promising to show him the sights of the pond. The Frog swam into the middle of the pond and dived beneath the surface, dragging the helpless Mouse down until he drowned. While the Mouse's body floated on the water, a Hawk flying overhead spotted it. The Hawk swooped down, seized the dead Mouse, and carried him away. Because the Frog was still tied to the Mouse, the Hawk devoured both of them together.\n\nHarm set, harm get.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 21, "key": "androcles_and_lion", "titleEn": "Androcles and the Lion", "titleJa": "アンドロクレスとライオン", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_androcles_and_lion.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "Once, a poor slave named Androcles ran away from his cruel master. He hid in a dark cave in the forest.\n\nSoon, a big lion entered the cave. Androcles was terrified, but the lion did not attack him. The lion was crying in pain because a sharp thorn was stuck in his paw. \n\nAndrocles approached the lion bravely and pulled out the thorn. The lion felt relieved and licked the man's hand like a dog. They lived together in the cave as friends.\n\nA few months later, soldiers found Androcles and took him back to the city. The king decided to feed him to a hungry lion in a large stadium.\n\nMany people came to watch. When the cage opened, a ferocious lion rushed toward Androcles. But when the lion reached him, it stopped. It recognized its old friend and began to rub its head against his legs affectionately.\n\nThe king was amazed by this wonderful sight. After he heard their story, the king freed both Androcles and the faithful lion.\n\nKindness is never forgotten.", "Grade_3": "A slave named Androcles once escaped from a harsh master who treated him poorly. While wandering through a vast forest, he discovered a quiet cave where he could hide safely.\n\nSuddenly, a huge lion appeared at the entrance, groaning in agony. Although Androcles was trembling with fear, he noticed that the beast was limping. The lion held up its swollen paw, which had a large, painful thorn deeply embedded in it. Overcoming his fear, Androcles carefully extracted the thorn and cleaned the wound. Deeply grateful, the gentle lion purred and became his loyal companion.\n\nHowever, soldiers eventually captured Androcles and condemned him to be thrown to the wild beasts in the royal arena. On the day of punishment, an enormous crowd gathered to witness the execution. A ferocious lion, which had been starved for days, was released into the ring. It roared fiercely and charged straight at Androcles.\n\nYet, as soon as the beast recognized the young man, it immediately knelt down and purred softly, licking his hands with affection. The emperor, who was astonished by this miraculous scene, called Androcles to explain. Moved by their touching bond, the emperor pardoned Androcles and granted total freedom to both the man and his loyal beast.\n\nTrue gratitude knows no boundaries, and mercy is always rewarded.", "Grade_Pre2": "Subjected to intolerable tyranny under an oppressive Roman patrician, an enslaved youth named Androcles orchestrated a desperate escape into the remote wilderness. Wandering aimlessly through dense woodlands in search of sanctuary, he sought refuge within a secluded subterranean cavern.\n\nHis uneasy solitude was shattered when an immense lion entered the cavern, uttering deep groans of distress. Paralyzed with terror, Androcles anticipated immediate slaughter. However, upon closer observation, he discerned that the majestic carnivore was incapacitated by severe agony. The beast timidly extended its inflamed forepaw, in which a formidable thorn was deeply lodged. Recognizing an opportunity for mutual survival, the fugitive suppressed his dread and meticulously extracted the foreign object, subsequently cleansing the festering puncture. Profoundly indebted to his benefactor, the noble creature exhibited gentle affection, sharing its cavern and provisions with Androcles for several months.\n\nTragically, imperial legionaries eventually apprehended the fugitive, transporting him to the capital where he was sentenced to suffer public execution by combat with famished carnivores in the Circus Maximus. On the fateful afternoon, an immense assembly of spectators cheered ruthlessly as Androcles was abandoned unarmed in the amphitheater. A ravenous lion, deliberately starved to amplify its ferocity, was unleashed from its subterranean cage.\n\nThe beast bounded furiously across the arena; nevertheless, upon identifying the defenseless captive, its predatory aggression instantly evaporated. Subdued by affectionate recognition, the magnificent predator bowed reverently and caressed Androcles's limbs. Bewildered by this extraordinary phenomenon, the Roman emperor interrogated the slave regarding the miracle. Thoroughly captivated by the narrative of cross-species compassion and reciprocal loyalty, the sovereign granted full imperial pardon to Androcles and restored the noble lion to its native habitat.\n\nGenuine benevolence transcends the boundaries of species, proving that compassionate deeds inevitably yield unexpected salvation.", "Grade_2": "Under the institutionalized brutality of imperial Roman servitude, an enslaved domestic subordinate named Androcles endured systematic dehumanization beneath a patrician master whose despotism bordered on psychopathy. Recognizing that continued subservience guaranteed physical and spiritual attrition, the desperate youth executed a clandestine evasion into the arid hinterlands of North Africa, ultimately seeking provisional asylum within the recesses of a subterranean limestone grotto.\n\nThis precarious equilibrium was shattered when an apex mammalian carnivore—an immense male Barbary lion—staggered into the sanctuary, emitting guttural lamentations indicative of physiological distress. Paralyzed by mortal dread, the fugitive prepared for instantaneous evisceration; nevertheless, acute empirical observation revealed that the colossal predator was rendered non-lethal by acute physical disability. Trembling with trepidation yet recognizing a moral imperativeness, Androcles approached the recumbent beast, discerning a calcified acacia spine deeply embedded within the suppurating tissue of its right forepaw. Mobilizing rudimentary surgical dexterity, the fugitive extracted the invasive obstruction and meticulously debrided the infected wound. What commenced as an alliance of desperation rapidly evolved into an interspecies symbiosis; bound by reciprocal fidelity, the carnivore routinely provisioned the grotto with fresh game, sustaining their subterranean cohabitation for over three continuous years.\n\nInevitably, Roman military patrols combing the frontier apprehended the fugitive, repatriating him to the metropolis where judicial authorities condemned him to damnatio ad bestias—execution by exposure to ravenous beasts in the imperial amphitheater. On the day of spectacle, before tens of thousands of bloodthirsty plebeians, Androcles was deposited defenseless in the sand, while a famished feline predator, starved for consecutive days to optimize lethal aggression, was propelled from the subterranean hypogeum.\n\nWith thunderous roars reverberating throughout the colosseum, the beast charged; miraculously, the trajectory of homicidal momentum terminated abruptly at the captive's feet. Rather than dismembering the condemned youth, the predator experienced an instantaneous cognitive reconnection, bowing with submissive reverence and affectionately caressing the man's trembling extremities. Confronted with this unprecedented suspension of predatory instinct, the Roman sovereign halted the spectacle, demanding an immediate judicial deposition. Deeply moved by this profound manifestation of cross-species fidelity and acknowledging the transcendence of primal compassion over institutionalized cruelty, the emperor commuted Androcles's capital sentence, conferring unconditional emancipation upon the man and returning the majestic carnivore to its sovereign wilderness.\n\nAltruistic intervention operates as an indestructible currency within the moral architecture of the universe, demonstrating that compassionate deeds performatively dismantle the mechanisms of lethal tyranny.", "Grade_Pre1": "Entrenched within the coercive apparatus of Roman chattel slavery, an alienated subordinate designated Androcles endured systemic psychological degradation and corporal torment under the capricious despotism of a provincial proconsul. Realizing that continued subservience inexorably culminated in physical annihilation, the desperate bondsman initiated a clandestine trans-frontier migration, seeking precarious asylum within the inhospitable geological fissures of the Numidian desert. Penetrating a subterranean cavern of calcified limestone, he established a precarious sanctuary, subsisting upon wild vegetation and stagnant rainwater.\n\nThis fragile pastoral seclusion was irrevocably compromised by the sudden ingress of an apex carnivore—a colossal Barbary lion whose guttural vocalizations resonated with unbearable somatic distress. Immobilized by visceral terror, the fugitive initially anticipated instantaneous anatomical dismemberment; however, rigorous empirical observation illuminated a profound biological anomaly: the formidable predator was rendered functionally incapacitated by severe acute trauma. Suppressing his autonomic panic response, Androcles approached the recumbent feline, perceiving an inflamed, suppurating puncture wound within its swollen dexter paw, wherein a hardened acacia spine remained deeply embedded. Exercising delicate mechanical precision, the runaway slave carefully extracted the calcified foreign body, subsequently debriding the necrotic margins and applying soothing herbal compresses. What commenced as a tentative détente born of shared vulnerability rapidly crystallized into an unprecedented interspecies symbiosis. Bound by an immutable ethos of reciprocal benevolence, the magnificent carnivore systematically provisioned the subterranean redoubt with fresh game, sustaining their harmonious cohabitation across multiple seasonal cycles.\n\nInevitably, an imperial cohort conducting systematic counter-insurgency sweeps apprehended the fugitive, consigning him to the capital where administrative magistrates condemned the recidivist runaway to damnatio ad bestias—public execution via consumption by famished wild beasts within the Flavian Amphitheater. On the designated afternoon of execution, before an amphitheater overflowing with bloodthirsty patricians and plebeians, Androcles was abandoned weaponless upon the sand. From the subterranean hypogeum was unleashed an immense carnivore, deliberately subjected to prolonged caloric deprivation to heighten its predatory ferocity.\n\nEmitting thunderous acoustic vibrations that shook the arena’s foundations, the feline launched a ferocious ballistic charge; yet, at the precise threshold of lethal collision, the beast's predatory momentum underwent an instantaneous physiological and cognitive cessation. Recognizing its subterranean benefactor, the sovereign predator abandoned all predatory impulses, prostrating itself in veneration and affectionately licking the captive's paralyzed extremities. Paralyzed by cognitive dissonance at this miraculous suspension of instinctive carnivory, the assembled spectators erupted in bewildered uproar, prompting the Roman emperor to summon the bondsman for an immediate judicial inquiry. Profoundly moved by this sublime chronicle of cross-species solidarity, and acknowledging that reciprocal fidelity had nullified the arbitrary jurisdiction of imperial law, the sovereign conferred absolute legal emancipation upon the slave and decreed the unconditional repatriation of the noble beast to its sovereign ecosystem.\n\nAltruistic benevolence constitutes an indestructible transcendent dialectic within the moral cosmos, proving that radical acts of empathy possess the inherent potency to neutralize the lethal violence of totalitarian oppression.", "Classic_Original": "A slave named Androcles once escaped from his master and fled into the forest. As he was wandering about there, he came upon a Lion lying down, groaning and moaning. At first he turned to flee, but finding that the Lion did not pursue him, he turned back and went up to him. As he came near, the Lion put out his paw, which was all swollen and bleeding, and Androcles found that a huge thorn had got into it, and was causing all the pain. He pulled out the thorn and bound up the paw of the Lion, who was soon able to rise and lick the hand of Androcles like a dog. Then the Lion took Androcles to his cave, and every day used to bring him meat from which the two lived. \n\nBut shortly afterwards both Androcles and the Lion were captured, and the slave was sentenced to be thrown to the Lion, after the latter had been kept without food for several days. The Emperor and all his Court came to look on at the spectacle, and Androcles was led out into the middle of the arena. Soon the Lion was let loose from his den, and rushed bounding and roaring towards his victim. But as soon as he came near to Androcles he recognised his friend, and fawned upon him, and licked his hands like a friendly dog. The Emperor was astonished at this strange spectacle and summoned Androcles to him. Androcles told the Emperor all that had happened, and was at once pardoned and set free, while the Lion was also loosed into his native forest.\n\nGratitude is the sign of noble souls.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 22, "key": "fox_and_crow", "titleEn": "The Fox and the Crow", "titleJa": "キツネとカラス", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_fox_and_crow.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "One morning, a black crow found a delicious piece of cheese. She flew to a high branch of a tall tree to eat it quietly.\n\nA sly fox was walking through the woods. He was very hungry, and he smelled the cheese. He looked up and saw the crow on the branch.\n\nThe fox wanted the cheese, so he decided to trick her. He walked to the tree and said politely, \"Good morning, beautiful bird! Your black feathers are so shiny and wonderful! You look like the queen of birds.\"\n\nThe crow was very pleased to hear this praise. \n\nThen the fox said, \"I am sure your voice is as sweet as your feathers. Please sing a song for me!\"\n\nThe crow wanted to show her lovely voice. She opened her beak and cried loudly, \"Caw! Caw!\" \n\nAt that moment, the cheese fell from her mouth. The fox caught it quickly and ate it all. \n\n\"Thank you for the cheese,\" laughed the fox. \"You have a voice, but you have no brains!\"\n\nDo not trust people who flatter you.", "Grade_3": "A proud crow had successfully stolen a large piece of cheese from an open cottage window. Feeling thoroughly pleased with herself, she flew up to the safety of a high tree branch, intending to savor her prize.\n\nA crafty fox, which had been prowling in search of a meal, caught the rich aroma of the cheese. He crept silently toward the base of the tree and gazed up at the bird. Knowing that he could not climb the tree, he realized that he had to use flattery to accomplish his goal.\n\n\"Greetings, magnificent creature!\" the fox called out in a smooth, gentle tone. \"How extraordinarily glossy your feathers look in the morning sunshine! Surely, a bird of such rare beauty must possess a voice that is equally enchanting. If only I could hear your melodious song, I would certainly bow to you as the true queen of all birds.\"\n\nFlattered by these sweet compliments, the foolish crow completely lost her common sense. Eager to prove that she possessed a magnificent voice, she lifted her head, opened her beak wide, and let out a loud screech.\n\nThe instant her beak opened, the precious cheese dropped directly to the ground. The fox snapped it up immediately and swallowed it with delight. Looking up at the crestfallen bird, he chuckled, \"Your singing is loud enough, my dear, but you sorely lack good judgment.\"\n\nNever trust those who shower you with empty flattery.", "Grade_Pre2": "Having successfully purloined an exquisite wedge of savory cheese from a farmhouse windowsill, a conceited crow perched upon a prominent bough within an ancient grove. Convinced of her unassailable superiority and immune to immediate hazards, the avian thief prepared to indulge leisurely in her illicit prize.\n\nHowever, the pungent fragrance permeated the forest air, rapidly attracting the attention of a famished fox prowling beneath the canopy. Recognizing that the coveted morsel was suspended entirely out of physical reach, the predator perceived that physical aggression would prove futile; consequently, he resolved to exploit psychological manipulation to achieve his objective.\n\nApproaching the trunk with calculated deference, the cunning tactician commenced a barrage of extravagant adulation. \"Hail, sovereign empress of the feathered realm!\" the fox proclaimed with simulated awe. \"The lustrous sheen of your immaculate plumage outshines the rarest silk, reflecting the dawn with incomparable dignity. Undeniably, if your acoustic gifts correspond to such visual perfection, no terrestrial monarch could challenge your undisputed supremacy over the animal kingdom.\"\n\nIntoxicated by this calculated flattery, the gullible corvid experienced a catastrophic collapse of critical judgment. Desperate to validate the deceiver's exaggerated accolades and demonstrate the melodious quality of her vocal capabilities, she reflexively parted her mandibles to deliver a resonant call.\n\nIn doing so, she inevitably relinquished her grasp upon the culinary treasure. Gravitational pull swiftly conveyed the cheese downward, where the opportunistic fox intercepted the prize before it contacted the turf. Consuming the nourishment expeditiously, the triumphant manipulator offered a sarcastic parting evaluation: \"Your auditory performance was adequately robust, madam, yet your intellectual discernment remains lamentably deficient.\"\n\nThose who succumb to excessive vanity inevitably render themselves vulnerable to exploitation by dishonest flatterers.", "Grade_2": "Having successfully executed the theft of an artisanal wedge of aged dairy product from an agrarian residence, an arrogant corvid established an elevated vantage point upon an arboreal bough within an ancient deciduous forest. Enveloped in the intoxicating delusion of invulnerability, the avian pilferer contemplated the leisurely consumption of her illicitly acquired spoils, completely detached from the terrestrial hazards operating beneath the woodland canopy.\n\nHowever, atmospheric currents dispersed the pungent olfactory markers of the delicacy across the forest floor, alerting a prowling vulpine carnivore driven by caloric deficit. Assessing the spatial geometry of the encounter, the fox observed that the coveted prize was suspended beyond the parameters of terrestrial predation; direct physical confrontation being rendered structurally unviable, the tactical predator recognized that psychological subversion represented the singular pathway toward confiscation.\n\nAdopting an posture of ceremonial subservience at the base of the trunk, the Machiavellian strategist launched a sophisticated campaign of hyperbolic adulation. \"Greetings, supreme monarch of the avian stratosphere!\" the fox intoned with theatrical reverence. \"The iridescent brilliance of your ebony plumage reflects the celestial luminescence with a majesty that eclipses all earthly royalties. Reason compels one to deduce that an organism possessing such sublime visual aesthetics must inevitably command an acoustic repertoire of equivalent melodious virtuosity. Could I merely be privileged to experience your sovereign vocalization, I would unequivocally consecrate your absolute hegemony over the natural dominion.\"\n\nTargeted with surgical precision at the corvid's latent narcissistic vulnerabilities, this rhetorical onslaught induced an instantaneous cognitive distortion. Overwhelmed by the desperate psychological impulse to substantiate this fabricated aesthetic appraisal and establish her acoustic supremacy, the bird discarded all residual survival skepticism. In an uninhibited gesture of exhibitionism, she expanded her wings, tilted her head skyward, and forcefully parted her bill to emit a harsh auditory screech.\n\nThe physical consequence was immediate and catastrophic: the cessation of mandibular pressure instantly dissociated the dairy sustenance from her anatomical control. Accelerating under gravitational descent, the nutritional mass plummeted directly toward the forest floor, where the agile predator executed an effortless spatial interception. Ingesting the prize with predatory efficiency, the triumphant fox delivered an incisive pedagogical verdict: \"Your acoustic volume proved entirely sufficient, madam; regrettably, your analytical discernment remains lamentably deficient in proportion to your pride.\"\n\nUncritical susceptibility to flattery constitutes a profound intellectual vulnerability, allowing parasitic manipulators to exploit egoistic vanity as a lever for material dispossession.", "Grade_Pre1": "Having consummated the clandestine expropriation of a cured wheel of artisan dairy nourishment from a pastoral homestead, a vainglorious corvid established an unassailable arboreal redoubt upon the elevated branch of an ancient oak. Cocooned within an intoxicating cognitive bubble of narcissistic invulnerability, the avian thief prepared to indulge in the protracted consumption of her illicit contraband, utterly oblivious to the subtle predatory calculations fermenting upon the forest floor beneath her perch.\n\nInevitably, ambient thermal currents disseminated the pungent olfactory profile of the lipid-dense nourishment, alerting a wandering vulpine tactician suffering from chronic caloric deprivation. Executing a rapid topographical assessment, the terrestrial carnivore recognized that the coveted sustenance was suspended entirely beyond the mechanical perimeter of direct physical assault. Structural inaccessibility precluding brute force, the Machiavellian predator deduced that psychological sabotage and rhetorical manipulation constituted the sole viable mechanism for engineering asset transfer.\n\nStationing himself at the root flare with choreographed humility, the fox orchestrated a devastating barrage of baroque encomiums, weaponizing the target's latent aesthetic vanity. \"Hail, unrivaled empress of the avian firmament!\" the deceiver intoned in cadences of counterfeit veneration. \"The obsidian luster of your magnificent plumage captures the morning light with an iridescent majesty that reduces all terrestrial diadems to vulgar insignificance. Logic unequivocally dictates that an organism endowed with such peerless morphological beauty must simultaneously command an auditory apparatus of transcendental melodious virtuosity. Might I merely be permitted the sublime benediction of hearing your sovereign aria, I should unhesitatingly proclaim your undisputed hegemony over the entirety of the animal commonwealth.\"\n\nEngineered with psychological precision to paralyze the victim’s critical faculties, this verbal sedative triggered an acute cognitive collapse. The desperate craving to validate this extravagant exterior appraisal overwhelmed the corvid's innate evolutionary skepticism. Subordinating rudimentary survival heuristics to an uncontrollable impulse of exhibitionistic pride, the gullible bird tilted her cranium, extended her pinions, and convulsively severed the mandibular pressure holding her prize in order to unleash a raucous vocalization.\n\nAt that fatal instant, the gravitational constant executed its inexorable decree. Deprived of anatomical retention, the nutritional prize dissociated from the corvid's beak and executed an uninhibited vertical plunge through the foliage. Positioning himself beneath the descending vector with surgical spatial anticipation, the agile predator intercepted the falling morsel prior to its contact with the forest floor. Having swallowed the bounty with clinical expedition, the triumphant manipulator delivered an unsparing philosophical critique: \"Your decibel capacity, madam, was undeniably formidable; nevertheless, the acute deficiency of your analytical discernment demonstrates that unmitigated conceit operates as the primary solvent of intellectual equilibrium.\"\n\nPathological vulnerability to disingenuous adulation constitutes a fatal psychological deficit, whereby parasitic manipulators weaponize the victim's own egoistic self-deception as the precise instrument of their material and existential dispossession.", "Classic_Original": "A Crow had snatched a piece of cheese and flew up into a high tree with it to eat it at her leisure. A Fox, seeing this, resolved to possess himself of the cheese, and coming up to the foot of the tree, began to flatter the Crow. \n\n\"What a noble bird I see before me!\" he said. \"Her beauty is without equal, the hue of her plumage exquisite. If only her voice were as sweet as her looks are fair, she ought without doubt to be the Queen of the Birds.\"\n\nThe Crow, hugely flattered by this speech, and wishing to show the Fox that she could sing, opened her mouth and gave a loud caw. The cheese fell, and the Fox, snatching it up, said, \"My good Crow, your voice is right enough, but your wit is wanting.\"\n\nDo not trust flatterers.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 23, "key": "old_man_and_death", "titleEn": "The Old Man and Death", "titleJa": "木こりと死神", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_old_man_and_death.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "An old woodcutter was carrying a heavy bundle of wood on his back. He had to walk a long way under the hot sun.\n\nHe was very tired, and his back hurt terribly. Finally, he could not walk anymore. He threw the heavy wood on the ground and sat down.\n\nIn despair, he cried, \"My life is too hard! I cannot bear this suffering. Death, please come and take me away!\"\n\nSuddenly, the dark figure of Death appeared in front of him. \"You called me,\" Death said in a cold voice. \"What do you want from me?\"\n\nThe old man was terrified. He began to tremble with fear. He did not want to die at all.\n\nQuickly, the old man replied, \"Oh, please sir! I only wanted someone to help me lift this heavy bundle of wood back onto my shoulders!\"\n\nWe often complain about life, but life is always precious.", "Grade_3": "An elderly woodcutter was trudging along a rugged mountain path, carrying an immense bundle of firewood on his aching shoulders. Having labored since dawn without any rest, he felt completely exhausted and overwhelmed by the weight of his burden.\n\nUnable to endure the severe strain any longer, he cast the heavy load to the ground and collapsed beside the trail. Overcome with deep grief, he groaned bitterly, \"My existence is nothing but continuous toil and misery! I have lost all reason to live. Death, come quickly and release me from this endless torment!\"\n\nTo his horror, the grim figure of Death materialized immediately before his eyes. \"You summoned me, mortal,\" Death whispered in a chilling tone. \"Why did you call for my arrival?\"\n\nConfronted with the terrifying reality of mortality, the old man's despair instantly turned into pure panic. Realizing how deeply he cherished his own life, he quickly composed himself and answered with a nervous smile, \"I only requested your kind assistance, noble spirit, to help me lift this bundle back onto my back so that I can return home.\"\n\nPeople frequently complain about life's hardships, yet when death actually approaches, life remains infinitely precious.", "Grade_Pre2": "Weakened by decades of relentless physical exertion, an impoverished woodcutter navigated a steep, perilous alpine trail while supporting a colossal mass of felled timber upon his fractured frame. Having toiled incessantly from the earliest glimmer of dawn without sustenance, the aging laborer reached the absolute threshold of physiological endurance.\n\nOverpowered by agonizing fatigue and spinal pain, he violently discarded the oppressive load onto the dusty terrain and sank down in profound dejection. Swept away by transient despair, he cursed his cruel destiny and vocalized an irrational plea: \"My terrestrial existence offers nothing but unceasing degradation and agonizing fatigue! Bereft of hope or solace, I implore the Grim Reaper to terminate my wretched breath and transport my soul into oblivion!\"\n\nTo his instantaneous terror, the spectral manifestation of Death solidified amidst the surrounding shadows. Brandishing his ominous scythe, the ethereal sovereign inquired in a sepulchral whisper: \"In accordance with your solemn invocation, frail mortal, I have manifested in your presence. Specify what final commission you require of my ultimate authority.\"\n\nParalyzed by the tangible presence of the inescapable abyss, the laborer experienced an instantaneous resurgence of the primal will to survive. His previous lamentations evaporated, supplanted by sheer desperation to preserve his mortal existence. Demonstrating remarkable presence of mind despite his trembling limbs, the peasant managed a strained smile and stammered: \"Benevolent guardian, perceiving that this cumbersome parcel of timber had slipped from my shoulders, I merely solicited your extraordinary fortitude to assist me in hoisting the load back onto my spine.\"\n\nHuman beings frequently utter frivolous complaints regarding the tribulations of existence; nevertheless, when confronted by absolute annihilation, the instinct for self-preservation overwhelmingly reasserts the supreme value of life.", "Grade_2": "Exhausted by continuous decades of agrarian hardship, a destitute woodcutter was laboriously negotiating a steep mountainous incline under the relentless thermal radiation of the midday sun, staggering beneath an immense load of harvested timber that compromised his skeletal equilibrium. Bereft of nutritional sustenance and having surpassed the absolute boundaries of neuromuscular stamina, the senescent laborer experienced acute physiological decompensation.\n\nIncapacitated by excruciating spinal strain, the laborer precipitated his cargo onto the gravel and collapsed into the trailside dust, overwhelmed by acute psychological dejection. Yielding to an impulsive surge of nihilistic despair, the demoralized individual verbalized an explicit invocation directed toward the metaphysical void: \"This mortal existence constitutes nothing more than an unbroken sequence of economic deprivation and biological torment! Having exhausted all emotional justification for prolonging this misery, I formally summon the entity of Death to extinguish my consciousness and consign my physical vessel to the grave.\"\n\nTo his profound psychological shock, the ontological barrier between abstract metaphor and objective reality instantaneously disintegrated. From the encroaching gloom materialized the anthropomorphic manifestation of mortality—the Grim Reaper, wielding his harvest scythe and radiating an aura of subterranean chill. \"Pursuant to your categorical petition, mortal petitioner, I have breached the threshold of eternity to accommodate your departure,\" the apparition intoned in a chilling baritone. \"Declare the execution of your ultimate mandate.\"\n\nConfronted with the immediate, visceral reality of his own terminal extinguishment, the woodcutter's theoretical death wish underwent an instantaneous psychological inversion. The existential lamentations that had characterized his despair vanished, completely eclipsed by the deep-seated neurological impulse of self-preservation. Mobilizing extraordinary presence of mind amidst intense somatic tremor, the aging laborer dissembled his panic, feigned deferential composure, and fabricated a spontaneous rationalization: \"Most venerable sovereign, observing that this unwieldy parcel of timber had inadvertently decoupled from my frame, I merely solicited your immense strength to assist me in re-hoisting the burden onto my shoulders so that I might resume my domestic transit.\"\n\nWhen subjected to acute socioeconomic stress, human beings are prone to vocalizing superficial flirtations with mortality; nevertheless, when confronted by the actual abyss of non-existence, the biological imperative for self-preservation unequivocally supersedes all theoretical grievances.", "Grade_Pre1": "Emaciated by a lifetime of merciless agrarian exploitation, an impoverished woodcutter navigated a treacherous alpine trajectory beneath the oppressive thermal onslaught of the summer solstice, bearing an immense payload of harvested timber that severely distorted his musculoskeletal architecture. Bereft of physiological nourishment and having long exceeded the adaptive boundaries of cellular homeostasis, the senescent laborer experienced a catastrophic neuromuscular collapse, his staggering gait terminating in a sudden, involuntary kinetic failure.\n\nOverpowered by excruciating spinal trauma and systemic exhaustion, the laborer violently dislodged his burdensome cargo onto the calcified scree and sank into the dust, completely unmoored by existential dejection. Succumbing to an impulsive paroxysm of theoretical nihilism, the desperate mortal verbalized an irrevocable invocation directed at the metaphysical cosmos: \"This corporeal existence represents an intolerable continuum of penury, degradation, and inescapable suffering! Having liquidated all biological justification for perpetuating this agonizing somatic tenancy, I explicitly summon Thanatos—the absolute sovereign of the terminal threshold—to extinguish my vital spark and dissolve my consciousness into eternal nothingness!\"\n\nIn terrifying refutation of the assumption that metaphysical cries remain unanswered, the veil separating linguistic abstraction from ontological reality instantaneously disintegrated. Coalescing from the shifting twilight materialized the chilling, anthropomorphic avatar of absolute mortality—the Grim Reaper, wielding his archaic harvesting scythe and radiating an atmospheric temperature approaching absolute zero. \"In strict adherence to your categorical summons, ephemeral mortal, I have manifested within your spatio-temporal coordinates,\" the apparition resonated with subterranean resonance. \"Enunciate your final commission, that I may execute the terminal severing of your mortal coil.\"\n\nConfronted with the unmediated, visceral horror of his imminent biological annihilation, the woodcutter’s romanticized flirtation with mortality suffered an instantaneous ontological rupture. The theatrical melancholy that had animated his theatrical plea vanished without a trace, entirely subordinated to the primal, non-negotiable neurological mandate of self-preservation. Mobilizing an astounding reserve of cognitive equilibrium amidst violent somatic tremors, the terrified peasant masked his psychological disintegration, manufactured an attitude of deferential obsequiousness, and improvised a brilliant tactical rationalization: \"Sublime sovereign of the abyss, perceiving that this cumbersome parcel of cordwood had inadvertently decoupled from my spine, I merely solicited your omnipotent musculature to assist me in elevating the burden back onto my shoulders, that I might complete my homeward transit.\"\n\nUnder conditions of transient socioeconomic despair, human beings routinely indulge in rhetorical posturing regarding the desirability of non-existence; nevertheless, when confronted by the actual, yawning precipice of finality, the primordial imperative of biological survival unequivocally dismantles all philosophical affectations of world-weariness.", "Classic_Original": "An Old Man that had travelled a long way with a huge bundle of sticks, found himself so weary that he cast it down, and called upon Death to deliver him from his troubles. \n\nDeath appeared immediately in answer to his summons, and asked him what he wanted with him. \n\nThe Old Man, terrified, replied: \"Only that you would please to lift that load of sticks upon my shoulders again.\"\n\nWe would often die when our troubles are heavy, but when Death draws near, we cling to life.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 24, "key": "eagle_and_jackdaw", "titleEn": "The Eagle and the Jackdaw", "titleJa": "鷲とカラス", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_eagle_and_jackdaw.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A mighty eagle swooped down from a high rock. He grabbed a small lamb with his sharp claws and carried it into the air easily.\n\nA jackdaw was watching this from a tree. He thought, \"I am as strong and brave as that eagle! I can catch a sheep, too.\"\n\nThe foolish bird flew high and dived down toward a big ram. He landed on the ram's back and dug his claws into the thick wool.\n\nHowever, the ram was much too heavy for him to lift. When the jackdaw tried to fly away, his claws were tangled in the fleece. He could not escape.\n\nA shepherd saw the bird fluttering on the sheep. He walked over, captured the jackdaw, and clipped his wings.\n\nThat evening, he gave the bird to his children. \"What kind of bird is this?\" the children asked.\n\nThe shepherd laughed, \"He thinks he is an eagle, but he is only a jackdaw.\"\n\nKnow your own limits.", "Grade_3": "An eagle swooped down from a high cliff with incredible speed and seized a small lamb in its powerful talons, carrying it effortlessly toward its nest.\n\nA foolish jackdaw, which had been observing the magnificent feat from a nearby branch, was filled with foolish envy. Convinced that he possessed equal strength and skill, he resolved to imitate the king of birds.\n\nCircling high above the pasture, the jackdaw selected the largest and heaviest ram in the flock. He plunged down recklessly and landed upon the beast's back. However, when he attempted to lift the enormous animal into the air, he discovered that he lacked the strength to move it even an inch.\n\nTo make matters worse, his sharp claws became hopelessly entangled in the thick, curly fleece. Despite his frantic flapping, he could not free himself.\n\nThe shepherd, who had witnessed the entire scene, walked over and captured the struggling bird without difficulty. After clipping the jackdaw's wings, the shepherd brought him home as a plaything for his children.\n\n\"What kind of creature is this?\" the curious children inquired.\n\n\"If you ask him,\" the shepherd chuckled, \"he claims to be an eagle; but if you judge him by his actions, he is merely a foolish jackdaw.\"\n\nImitating the powerful without possessing their strength will inevitably lead to humiliation and disaster.", "Grade_Pre2": "Descending precipitously from an inaccessible alpine precipice, an apex eagle captured an unblemished lamb with breathtaking precision, hoisting the livestock airborne through sheer muscular potency. Witnessing this awe-inspiring demonstration of aerial supremacy, a vainglorious jackdaw experienced an overwhelming surge of irrational ambition. Deluded by superficial observation into believing that physical stature was negligible in the execution of predatory feats, the diminutive corvid resolved to duplicate the raptor's triumph.\n\nSurveying the pastoral meadow beneath, the ambitious pretender targeted the most colossal and formidable ram in the flock, erroneously presuming that greater quarry would yield greater renown. Accelerating into a steep dive with a noisy flurry of feathers, he descended violently upon the beast's woolly spine, sinking his curved talons deeply into the matted fleece.\n\nHowever, the profound disparity between his grandiose aspiration and physiological capacity instantly manifested itself. When the jackdaw strained frantically to elevate the massive quadruped into the atmosphere, the unyielding ram barely acknowledged the disturbance, continuing to graze placidly. Furthermore, the bird's slender claws became inextricably entwined within the dense, convoluted fibers of the wool. Entrapped by his own miscalculated assault, his hysterical fluttering merely tightened the knots.\n\nHaving observed the ludicrous spectacle with amused detachment, the attentive shepherd approached and effortlessly apprehended the immobilised bird. Subjecting the captive to humiliating wing-clipping to prevent escape, the herdsman presented the prisoner as a curious novelty for his household.\n\nWhen his children inquired regarding the species of this bizarre pet, the shepherd delivered a pointed verdict: \"In accordance with his inflated delusions, he masquerades as an imperial eagle; nevertheless, judged by the reality of his limited competence, he remains an utterly insignificant jackdaw.\"\n\nBlindly emulating the accomplishments of superior beings without assessing one's innate limitations inevitably invites catastrophic humiliation.", "Grade_2": "Executing a high-velocity ballistic descent from a jagged alpine cliff, an apex golden eagle intercepted a juvenile ovine specimen with flawless aerodynamic precision, utilizing phenomenal pectoral musculature to hoist the struggling prey aloft toward its montane eyrie. Observing this exhibition of aerial dominance from a neighboring vantage point, an egocentric corvid—a diminutive jackdaw—succumbed to a profound cognitive bias: erroneously conceptualizing the raptor's triumph not as the culmination of evolutionary specialization, but as an easily replicable mechanical stunt.\n\nImpelled by reckless vanity, the bird formulated an irrational intention to duplicate the feat on an amplified scale. Surveying the pastoral landscape beneath, he deliberately bypassed modest prey, electing instead to target the dominant patriarch of the flock—a massive, fully matured ram possessing formidable mass and curled horns. Initiating a dive accompanied by an undignified squawk, the jackdaw slammed precipitously onto the quadruped's spinal column, vigorously embedding his slender talons into the dense, crimped matrix of the fleece.\n\nThe instantaneous outcome constituted an absolute refutation of his delusions. When the bird mobilized his full wing stroke to achieve vertical propulsion, the structural immensity of the unyielding herbivore absorbed the kinetic energy without displacement; the ram merely twitched its ear and continued grazing. Compounding this operational failure, the bird's recurved claws became hopelessly ensnared within the interlocking keratinous fibers of the fleece. Every frantic, uncoordinated flap served only to tighten the fibrous entanglement, rendering autonomous extrication physically impossible.\n\nObserving this farcical sequence of events with cynical amusement, the attending pastoralist strode across the turf and apprehended the immobilized corvid without resistance. Subjecting the creature to bilateral pinioning—surgically severing the primary flight feathers to eradicate aerodynamic capability—the herdsman transported the humiliated specimen to his domestic quarters to function as an educational plaything for his offspring.\n\nWhen the children interrogated their father concerning the biological taxonomy of this peculiar captive, the shepherd provided an incisive socio-behavioral critique: \"Measured against the metric of his subjective vanity, this creature presumes to occupy the ecological niche of an imperial eagle; evaluated, however, through the objective lens of his performance, he stands revealed as a preposterous jackdaw.\"\n\nUncritical emulation of extraordinary achievements in the absence of corresponding competence inevitably converts ambitious aspirations into public spectacles of catastrophic ridicule.", "Grade_Pre1": "Launching an explosive gravitational plunge from the stratospheric precipice of a montane crag, an apex raptor—a mature golden eagle—intercepted a grazing lamb with mathematical ballistic trajectory, deploying phenomenal pectoral torque to wrench the livestock from the earth and ascend effortlessly toward its inaccessible eyrie. Observing this sublime manifestation of biomechanical sovereignty from an adjacent scrub oak, a vainglorious corvid succumbed to a catastrophic episode of cognitive dissonance: misconstruing a triumph of millions of years of evolutionary specialization as a superficial behavioral protocol that could be duplicated through mere theatrical imitation.\n\nIntoxicated by an uncalibrated delusion of physiological equivalence, the diminutive jackdaw resolved to orchestrate an identical predation event on a grandiose scale. Scrutinizing the pastoral basin beneath, the pretender deliberately dismissed vulnerable quarry, electing instead to target the undisputed patriarch of the ovine flock—a colossal, horned ram whose biological mass exceeded the bird’s own physiological threshold by several orders of magnitude. Executing an uncoordinated, flapping descent, the deluded corvid plummeted onto the quadruped’s dorsal ridge, frantically burying his gracile talons into the impenetrable, lanolin-saturated matrix of the curly fleece.\n\nThe physical denouement constituted an immediate and absolute ontological humiliation. Mobilizing his total aerobic capacity in an agonized attempt to generate aerodynamic lift, the jackdaw produced zero vertical displacement against the ram’s immense skeletal inertia; the unperturbed herbivore merely flicked its ear and resumed ruminating. To compound this kinetic catastrophe, the bird’s curved talons became irrevocably entwined within the microscopic crimp of the interlocking wool fibers. Every frantic, uncoordinated stroke of his wings functioned not as an instrument of escape, but as an inexorable ratcheting mechanism that anchored his appendages ever more securely within the biological trap.\n\nHaving observed this preposterous exhibition of hubris with dry pastoral amusement, the attending shepherd leisurely traversed the pasture and apprehended the hopelessly entangled captive without deploying physical force. Deciding to transform the incompetent usurper into an object lesson on the perils of overreaching ambition, the herdsman executed unilateral pinioning—excising the primary flight feathers to eliminate aerodynamic functionality—and presented the immobilized specimen to his children as a curious household distraction.\n\nWhen his offspring interrogated the master regarding the specific biological taxonomy of this peculiar organism, the shepherd delivered a devastating philosophical verdict: \"Assessed through the subjective prism of his unhinged vanity, this wretched creature masquerades as a monarch of the aerial realm; subjected, however, to the empirical scrutiny of operational competence, he stands unmasked as nothing more than a preposterous, flightless jackdaw.\"\n\nBlindly emulating the transcendent achievements of superior entities without possessing their requisite structural competence inevitably transforms aspiring overachievers into pathetic spectacles of universal derision.", "Classic_Original": "An Eagle flew down from a high mountain crag, and carried away a Lamb in his talons. A Jackdaw saw him, and thought that he could do the same. So he flew down upon a Ram with a great whirr, and fastened his claws in the fleece; but when he tried to fly away again, he found he could not move the Ram, and his claws were so entangled in the wool that he could not get away. \n\nThe Shepherd saw what had happened, and ran up and caught the bird. He clipped his wings, and took him home in the evening to his children. \n\n\"What bird is this?\" they cried. \n\n\"Well,\" said the Shepherd, \"if you ask him, he'll tell you he is an Eagle; but I know he is only a Jackdaw.\"\n\nDo not let your vanity lead you to attempt what is beyond your power.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 25, "key": "fox_and_mask", "titleEn": "The Fox and the Mask", "titleJa": "キツネと仮面", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_fox_and_mask.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "One afternoon, a curious fox entered an actor's house. The actor was away, so the fox walked around looking for something interesting.\n\nHe found a large box full of theater props. Inside, there was a beautiful mask. The mask was painted in bright colors, and its face looked very noble and handsome.\n\nThe fox held the mask in his paws. He looked at it carefully from the front. Then, he turned it over and looked at the back. \n\nThe mask was completely empty inside. It had no brain, no eyes, and no tongue.\n\nThe fox shook his head and said, \"What a fine and handsome head! But it is too bad that you have no brains inside.\"\n\nA handsome face is useless if there is no wisdom behind it.", "Grade_3": "A curious fox once slipped through an open doorway into the workshop of a famous actor. Since the master of the house had gone out, the fox began to explore every corner of the room, hoping to discover something tasty to eat.\n\nInstead of food, he came across a chest filled with theatrical costumes and various strange objects. Among them, a tragic actor's mask caught his attention. It was crafted with exceptional skill, featuring a majestic expression and beautifully painted features that resembled the face of a noble hero.\n\nThe fox lifted the magnificent mask with his paws and examined it closely. However, when he turned it over to look inside, he discovered that it was completely hollow. It possessed neither eyes to see, nor a voice to speak, nor any brains to think.\n\nGazing at the empty shell with disappointment, the fox remarked, \"What an imposing and splendid head you have! Yet what a great pity that you lack even a single grain of common sense inside.\"\n\nA handsome appearance has little true value if it lacks intelligence and moral substance.", "Grade_Pre2": "Taking advantage of an unlatched entrance, an inquisitive fox infiltrated the private atelier of a distinguished theatrical performer. Operating under the initial expectation of uncovering edible scraps, the intruder conducted a systematic reconnaissance of the chaotic chamber, inspecting properties and ornate stage attire scattered across the premises.\n\nAmidst this artistic disarray, his gaze was arrested by an extraordinary sculpted artifact resting within an open storage coffer. It was a tragic theater mask, executed with consummate artisanal mastery. The sculpted countenance conveyed regal solemnity, characterized by exquisitely proportioned contours, gilded accents, and an expression of profound philosophical contemplation reminiscent of legendary sovereigns.\n\nFascinated by the apparent dignity embodied in the artifact, the quadruped gingerly elevated the masterpiece between his forepaws to conduct a rigorous inspection. However, upon rotating the object to scrutinize its interior dimension, he was confronted by a stark revelation: the structure comprised nothing more than a superficial, concave shell of dried plaster and pigment. It possessed no sensory faculties, no capacity for articulation, and was entirely devoid of any cerebral apparatus.\n\nReleasing an ironic sigh of intellectual disillusionment, the philosophical fox articulated a profound critique: \"What extraordinary grandeur and nobility your exterior exhibits to the observer! Yet what an immense tragedy that beneath such an imposing facade, there resides not an infinitesimal fragment of intellect or genuine consciousness.\"\n\nSuperficial elegance and elaborate facades remain utterly devoid of authentic merit unless substantiated by internal wisdom and moral integrity.", "Grade_2": "Exploiting an unfastened portal during an interval of human absence, an observant vulpine explorer penetrated the private workshop of a celebrated classical dramatist. Guided primarily by an appetite for nutritional scraps, the animal conducted an exhaustive reconnaissance of the atelier, surveying an eclectic assemblage of stage properties, gilded draperies, and theatrical accessories that littered the creative sanctuary.\n\nDuring this systematic exploration, the animal's cognitive attention was instantaneously captivated by a sculpted artifact resting in an open cedar chest. It was a classical tragic mask—a theatrical persona carved from dense linden wood and embellished with mineral pigments by a master artisan. The sculpted visage projected an aura of transcendent nobility; its chisel-carved brow, harmoniously proportioned symmetry, and dignified, downward-curving lips simulated the profound philosophical gravity of a legendary monarch confronting cosmic adversity.\n\nIntrigued by the compelling illusion of intellectual majesty, the quadruped gingerly lifted the sculpted head between his paws to execute an empirical tactile assessment. However, upon inverting the artifact to interrogate its internal architecture, the investigator encountered an absolute ontological void: the structure constituted nothing beyond an ultra-thin, concave veneer of sculpted wood and lacquered lacquer. It possessed no biological sensory apparatus, was utterly incapable of linguistic articulation, and contained not a single neuron of cerebral matter.\n\nContemplating this radical dichotomy between external aesthetic simulation and internal intellectual vacuum, the vulpine philosopher articulated a scathing pedagogical critique: \"What formidable majesty your countenance projects toward the superficial observer! How lamentable, nevertheless, that beneath such an imposing aesthetic facade, there exists a state of total cognitive vacancy—neither an organ for contemplation nor a pulse of authentic consciousness.\"\n\nThe seductive prestige of superficial ornamentation constitutes a dangerous illusion; outward signifiers of intellectual or social preeminence possess zero substantive value when completely divorced from internal ethical virtue and analytical substance.", "Grade_Pre1": "Infiltrating the private atelier of a prominent Athenian tragic dramatist via an unlatched casement during an interlude of human absence, an inquisitive vulpine predator initiated an exhaustive reconnaissance of the premises. While ostensibly oriented toward the discovery of discarded gastronomic refuse, the animal’s perceptual apparatus was redirected by an eclectic panoply of theatrical paraphernalia—gilded sceptres, embroidered buskins, and polychromatic draperies—that cluttered the creative sanctuary.\n\nAmidst this curated archive of dramatic artifice, the explorer’s gaze was irrevocably arrested by an extraordinary artisanal relic deposited within an open chest of aromatic cypress. It was a tragic theatrical mask—a classical persona sculpted from seasoned cedar and embellished with polychromatic encaustic pigments by a master craftsman. The carved countenance projected an arresting aesthetic of transcendent gravitas: the sculpted brow manifested profound contemplative melancholy, the aristocratic aquiline contour simulated regal authority, and the parted lips evoked the sublime, stoic resignation of an epic protagonist defying relentless cosmic doom.\n\nCaptivated by this hyper-realistic simulacrum of philosophical consciousness, the animal gingerly elevated the artifact between his dexterous forepaws to conduct an unhurried, tactile interrogation of its material properties. However, upon rotating the object to inspect its posterior dimension, the mammalian investigator encountered an absolute ontological nullity: the structural artifact constituted nothing more than an insubstantial, concave perimeter of dried timber and calcified gesso. It was totally devoid of neurological circuitry; it possessed neither visual orbs to process optical stimulation, nor a respiratory apparatus to articulate linguistic meaning, nor an infinitesimal fragment of cerebral tissue to formulate subjective thoughts.\n\nContemplating this profound, irreconcilable discrepancy between an arresting aesthetic exterior and an absolute internal vacuum, the vulpine philosopher formulated an incisive semiotic critique: \"What monumental majesty and philosophical introspection your outward countenance projects toward the superficial observer! How appalling, nevertheless, that beneath such an imposing architectural facade, there resides an ontological wasteland—a profound cognitive vacancy devoid of the slightest flicker of authentic intellect or visceral consciousness.\"\n\nThe fetishization of superficial prestiges constitutes a pervasive cognitive pathology; outward cultural and aesthetic signifiers of intellectual preeminence remain entirely fraudulent and worthless unless substantiated by authentic ethical integrity and rigorous analytical interiority.", "Classic_Original": "A Fox entered the house of an actor and, rummaging through all his properties, came upon a Mask, an admirable imitation of a human head. He placed his paws upon it, and said: \n\n\"What a head is here, and yet it has no brains!\"\n\nOutside show is a poor substitute for inner worth.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 26, "key": "stag_at_pool", "titleEn": "The Stag at the Pool", "titleJa": "鹿と池の影", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_stag_at_pool.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A handsome stag came to a clear pool to drink cool water. As he drank, he saw his reflection in the water.\n\nHe looked at his large, magnificent antlers. \"How beautiful my horns are!\" he said proudly. \"They look like a royal crown.\"\n\nThen, he looked down at his long, thin legs. He felt ashamed. \"My legs are so skinny and ugly,\" he sighed. \"Why are they so weak?\"\n\nSuddenly, a hunter with a pack of hounds came into the meadow. The stag was frightened and began to run.\n\nHis slender legs carried him across the open plain with great speed. He quickly left the dogs far behind.\n\nHowever, he ran into a dense forest. His large antlers got caught in the low branches of the trees. He could not move at all.\n\nAs the hounds ran toward him, the stag cried, \"How foolish I was! The ugly legs saved me, but the beautiful horns destroyed me!\"\n\nUseful things are better than pretty decorations.", "Grade_3": "A graceful stag stepped toward the edge of a crystal-clear spring to quench his thirst. While gazing into the tranquil surface, he noticed his own reflection for the first time.\n\nHe admired his magnificent antlers, which spread out majestically like the branches of an oak tree. Filled with excessive vanity, he praised their extraordinary elegance. However, when he shifted his gaze toward his slender legs, he felt deeply disappointed. \"How wretched and frail my legs appear!\" he grumbled bitterly. \"They are far too thin to match my splendid crown.\"\n\nAt that very instant, the distant baying of hounds echoed through the valley. A skilled hunter had spotted him and immediately launched a pursuit.\n\nInstinctively, the stag bounded across the open plain, leaving his pursuers far behind thanks to the remarkable speed of his agile legs. Yet, as he plunged into a thick forest to seek shelter, his wide antlers became firmly entangled in the tangled boughs of the trees.\n\nStruggling desperately in vain as the hounds rapidly closed in, the stag lamented, \"Alas! How foolish I was to despise the humble legs that could have preserved my life, while taking excessive pride in the ornamental horns that have caused my destruction!\"\n\nWe frequently undervalue what is truly beneficial and praise what ultimately brings about our downfall.", "Grade_Pre2": "Approaching an undisturbed woodland reservoir to satisfy his dehydration, an aristocratic stag paused to contemplate his aquatic mirror image. Mesmerized by his own silhouette, the herbivore indulged in an intensive self-assessment dominated by superficial aesthetic criteria.\n\nHe marveled with profound gratification at his sprawling antlers, which ascended toward the sky in an elaborate architecture of calcified tines reminiscent of an imperial diadem. Nevertheless, this narcissistic reverie deteriorated into acute revulsion when his appraisal shifted downward toward his lower extremities. Observing his elongated, spindly limbs, he registered profound indignation: \"What an appalling biological contradiction! How humiliating that such an awe-inspiring sovereign should be supported by limbs so wretchedly slender, devoid of muscular grandeur, and aesthetically offensive!\"\n\nBefore he could indulge further in self-pity, the thunderous baying of hunting hounds shattered the forest equilibrium. Alerted to the imminent peril, the stag reacted instantaneously. Propelled by the remarkable elasticity and mechanical efficiency of his despised limbs, he accelerated across the open savanna with breathtaking agility, effortlessly outdistancing the equestrian hunters and their canine vanguard.\n\nTragically, seeking refuge within a dense arboreal sanctuary, the fleet-footed quadruped encountered catastrophic misfortune. His expansive, branching antlers became hopelessly snared within the dense canopy of low-hanging branches. Deprived of mobility by the very ornaments he idolized, his frantic lunges served merely to anchor him more securely to the timber.\n\nAs the baying pack converged to tear him apart, the doomed animal articulated a bitter realization: \"What catastrophic delusion blinded my judgment! I despised the utilitarian limbs that granted me salvation, while venerating the decorative appendages that orchestrated my inescapable doom.\"\n\nHumanity habitually denigrates functional utility in favor of ostentatious display, oblivious to the fact that ornamental vanity frequently precipitates ultimate ruin.", "Grade_2": "Arriving at the pristine perimeter of an undisturbed lacustrine basin to alleviate systemic physiological dehydration, a mature male cervid paused to inspect his specular reflection cast upon the unruffled liquid mirror. Captivated by this visual confrontation with his own morphology, the animal embarked upon an uncritical self-appraisal heavily distorted by aesthetic biases rather than ecological considerations.\n\nSurveying his cranial summit, the stag experienced intense narcissistic gratification. His expansive, multi-tined antlers ascended in baroque calcified symmetry, projecting an aura of sovereign majesty that rivaled the ceremonial diadems of ancient potentates. Conversely, when the trajectory of his optical scrutiny descended toward his lower appendages, his self-congratulatory euphoria degenerated into profound resentment. Viewing his elongated, gracile metapodials, he vocalized an indignant grievance against evolutionary design: \"What an egregious physiological incongruity! That an organism endowed with such imperial cranial ornamentation should be obliged to navigate reality upon limbs so wretchedly fragile, bereft of anatomical bulk, and visually contemptible!\"\n\nBefore this irrational self-pity could solidify into fixed doctrine, the acoustic resonance of canine baying violently ruptured the ecological tranquility. Alerted to the presence of an organized hunting expedition, the quadruped initiated an emergency ballistic evasion. Mobilizing the specialized kinetic elasticity and optimized biomechanical architecture of his despised lower limbs, the stag generated explosive acceleration across the savanna, establishing an insurmountable spatial deficit between himself and his equestrian pursuers.\n\nCatastrophically, in a misguided attempt to secure definitive sanctuary within a climax forest canopy, the animal's morphological priorities triggered lethal consequences. Navigating at velocity through dense arboreal thickets, his sprawling, bifurcated antlers became inextricably wedged between the rigid, unyielding boughs of ancient timber. Paralyzed by the very ornamentation he had idolized, every hysterical muscular convulsion served merely to compress the structural trap, neutralizing the biomechanical advantage of his limbs.\n\nAs the predatory pack closed the perimeter to execute his dismemberment, the trapped cervid articulated a devastating philosophical realization: \"What tragic cognitive dissonance dictated my values! I condemned the gracile, utilitarian limbs that alone possessed the capacity to preserve my biological existence, while sanctifying the cumbersome cranial excrescences that systematically engineered my destruction.\"\n\nHuman societies habitually commit identical errors of value attribution, subordinating indispensable functional competence to superficial prestige, oblivious to the reality that ostentatious ornamentation frequently precipitates systemic vulnerability.", "Grade_Pre1": "Approaching the crystalline margin of an undisturbed oligotrophic tarn to remediate acute metabolic dehydration, a magnificent male cervid paused to contemplate his inverted mirror image delineated upon the tranquil aqueous interface. Enamored by this unexpected specular confrontation with his own morphology, the herbivorous aristocrat indulged in an intensive exercise of subjective self-evaluation, allowing superficial aesthetic criteria to completely eclipse evolutionary logic and ecological adaptation.\n\nSurveying the cranial apex of his anatomy, the stag experienced an overwhelming surge of narcissistic ecstasy. His colossal, multi-branched antlers proliferated in baroque calcified architecture, radiating an aura of prehistoric majesty that effortlessly eclipsed the ceremonial insignia of mortal monarchs. In sharp and agonizing contrast, however, when his optical gaze descended toward his locomotory apparatus, this self-congratulatory reverie collapsed into intense somatic revulsion. Contemplating the elongated, hyper-slender architecture of his metapodial limbs, the animal articulated a bitter ontological grievance: \"What a grotesque biological paradox! How humiliating that an organism crowned with such sublime architectural grandeur should be forced to traverse terrestrial reality upon appendages so fragile, lacking all muscular substance, and aesthetically offensive to the aristocratic eye!\"\n\nBefore this irrational episode of self-loathing could undergo cognitive consolidation, the synchronized baying of hunting canines violently shattered the sylvan equilibrium. Discerning the proximate acoustic signature of an elite equestrian hunting detachment, the stag executed an instantaneous transition into ballistic locomotion. Mobilizing the remarkable kinetic elasticity, optimized tendon mechanics, and explosive lever dynamics of his despised lower extremities, the quadruped attained breathtaking velocities across the savanna, effortlessly engineering an insurmountable spatial buffer between himself and his pursuers.\n\nTragically, in a catastrophic bid to seek definitive camouflage within the climax interior of an ancient deciduous forest, the animal’s morphological hubris orchestrated his terminal downfall. Navigating an overgrown woodland corridor at breakneck velocity, his expansive, bifurcated antlers became violently snared within the rigid, unyielding lattice of descending oak branches. Anchored inextricably to the timber by the very ornamentation he had idolatrously venerated, every desperate, uncoordinated convulsion merely compressed the architectural snare, rendering his biomechanically optimized limbs completely impotent.\n\nAs the baying vanguard converged to execute his anatomical dismemberment, the immobilized creature uttered an agonizing philosophical indictment: \"What fatal cognitive dissonance governed my perceptual priorities! I vilified the humble, utilitarian extremities that possessed the exclusive potency to preserve my biological existence, while venerating the cumbersome cranial appendages that actively engineered my inexorable doom.\"\n\nCivilizations consistently reproduce identical fallacies of valuation, subordinating vital functional competence to ostentatious display, oblivious to the immutable principle that ornamental excess inevitably functions as the primary catalyst for catastrophic systemic collapse.", "Classic_Original": "A Stag quenched his thirst at a clear lake, and gazed upon his reflection in the water. He greatly admired the size and variety of his horns, but felt much displeased with the spindly weakness of his legs. \n\nWhile he was still contemplating his form, a Lion sprang upon him. The Stag fled over the plain and outran him, for the strength of stags lies in their legs, but of the lion in his heart. The Stag kept ahead until he reached a dense wood, where his antlers became entangled in the overhanging branches. He could not free himself, and the Lion quickly overtook him. \n\nWhen on the point of death, the Stag cried: \"Woe is me! What an ungrateful wretch I am! Those feet which I despised would have saved me, while the horns on which I prided myself have brought about my ruin.\"\n\nWe often despise what is most useful, and prize that which brings our doom.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 27, "key": "frogs_and_sun", "titleEn": "The Frogs and the Sun", "titleJa": "太陽とカエルたちの結婚", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_frogs_and_sun.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "One summer, news spread across the world that the Sun was going to marry.\n\nAll the animals and people were excited. They planned big parties and celebrated loudly.\n\nHowever, in a quiet pond, a group of frogs gathered together. They were not celebrating at all. Instead, they looked very worried and sad.\n\nAn old toad saw them and asked, \"Why are you so sad? Everyone is happy about the Sun's wedding!\"\n\nA wise frog replied, \"Think about it! Even now, one single Sun dries up our ponds and lakes in the summer. We already have very little water to live in. If the Sun has children, the heat will become unbearable. Every drop of water on earth will disappear, and all of us will die!\"\n\nThe other frogs nodded in fear.\n\nDo not celebrate things that will bring you trouble.", "Grade_3": "One bright summer day, great news echoed across the land: the Sun had decided to get married. Hearing this exciting announcement, humans and animals alike began to celebrate with joyful feasts and lively dances.\n\nHowever, down in the marshes, a community of frogs sat in somber silence, croaking with deep anxiety. Noticing their strange gloom, a curious neighbor asked why they refused to participate in the general rejoicing.\n\nA wise old frog stepped forward and explained their dread. \"Consider how much we already suffer under just one single Sun,\" he said gravely. \"During every hot season, his blazing rays evaporate our shallow pools, forcing us to burrow into the mud simply to survive. If he marries and raises a family of little suns, imagine what will become of our fragile world! Their combined heat will dry up every river, pond, and marsh on earth. We shall all perish from utter drought!\"\n\nHearing this sobering explanation, the other creatures finally realized the hidden peril and ceased their thoughtless cheering.\n\nIt is foolish to rejoice over changes that will merely multiply our masters and intensify our suffering.", "Grade_Pre2": "A monumental proclamation resonated throughout the terrestrial biosphere: the celestial sovereign, the Sun, had declared his intention to enter into holy matrimony. Uncritically assuming that imperial festivities warranted universal jubilation, the majority of terrestrial species succumbed to unrestrained merriment, organizing elaborate banquets and triumphant processions to commemorate the royal wedding.\n\nConversely, within the subterranean dampness of the fenlands, an assembly of indigenous amphibians convened in atmospheric despair. Puzzled by this conspicuous refusal to conform to the prevailing jubilation, an inquisitive bystander challenged their melancholy: \"Why do you maintain this recalcitrant silence while the entirety of creation rejoices over our celestial monarch's nuptials?\"\n\nA venerable anuran patriarch, possessing profound ecological foresight, addressed the assembly with sobering gravity. \"You celebrate in blissful ignorance of catastrophic repercussions,\" the elder declared. \"Even under the unilateral reign of a singular solar entity, our amphibious habitats endure critical degradation. The solar furnace relentlessly desiccates our vernal pools, evaporating moisture reservoirs and compelling our populace to hibernate beneath stagnant silt to evade lethal dehydration.\n\nShould this celestial tyrant reproduce and establish a dynasty of thermal progeny, consider the inevitable ecological devastation! The cumulative thermal radiation generated by multiple solar entities will vaporize every aquatic sanctuary, transforming our fertile wetland ecosystems into arid wastes. Amphibious life will suffer complete, irreversible annihilation.\"\n\nIlluminated by this rigorous geopolitical and ecological analysis, the previously euphoric creatures recognized the peril of autocratic proliferation and abruptly discontinued their premature celebrations.\n\nShortsighted populaces foolishly celebrate the multiplication of governing authorities, blind to the grim reality that institutional proliferation invariably compounds the burden of oppression.", "Grade_2": "A momentous edict emanated from the celestial summit, reverberating across the planetary biosphere: the solar sovereign, whose radiant hegemony governed terrestrial thermodynamics, officially declared his impending matrimony. Conditioned by uncritical sycophancy toward institutional power, the overwhelming majority of biological organisms interpreted this imperial announcement as an unequivocal catalyst for universal celebration. Across terrestrial habitats, diverse species mobilized lavish civic banquets, organized triumphal pageantry, and proclaimed unconditional fealty toward the cosmic autocrat.\n\nStrikingly detached from this mass hysteria, an assembly of indigenous amphibians convened in somber conclave within the subterranean recesses of an ancient fen. Confronted by this obstinate refusal to synchronize with the collective euphoria, a conventional bystander challenged their apparent cynicism: \"What perverse rationale motivates your recalcitrance, while the entirety of the biological commonwealth enthusiastically endorses the dynastic nuptials of our supreme luminary?\"\n\nStepping forward with patriarchal solemnity, a venerable anuran statesman delivered an uncompromising geopolitical and ecological rebuttal. \"Your uncritical jubilation constitutes an appalling manifestation of collective cognitive blindness,\" the elder proclaimed. \"Analyze the thermodynamic reality of our current ecological predicament. Under the unilateral hegemony of a single solar furnace, our vulnerable amphibious ecosystems operate at the absolute precipice of habitability. Even now, seasonal solar radiation desiccates our vernal aquifers, evaporates moisture gradients, and compels our entire populace to seek subterranean dormancy merely to stave off systemic dehydration.\n\nContemplate the apocalyptic ecological consequences should this cosmic potentate successfully reproduce and establish an expansive dynasty of thermal heirs! The compounding atmospheric irradiation generated by multiple solar tyrants will ruthlessly vaporize every remaining wetland sanctuary, reducing the planet's hydrological cycle to absolute thermal arrest. Amphibious biology will experience instantaneous, terminal extinction.\"\n\nConfronted with this indisputable scientific projection, the sycophantic multitude experienced an acute awakening to geopolitical reality. Realizing that celebratory complacency masked imminent ecocide, the animals abruptly suspended their festivities.\n\nSubservient populaces routinely applaud the dynastic proliferation of autocratic rulers, fundamentally oblivious to the systemic reality that the multiplication of oppressive authorities inevitably accelerates the annihilation of the governed.", "Grade_Pre1": "An imperial proclamation of epochal magnitude emanated from the celestial apex, reverberating throughout the terrestrial ecosphere: the solar sovereign, whose radiant hegemony presided over planetary thermodynamics, officially promulgated his intention to enter into imperial matrimony. Psychologically conditioned by systemic sycophancy toward institutional authority, the overwhelming preponderance of the biological commonwealth conceptualized this dynastic event as an absolute mandate for universal jubilation. Throughout every continental biome, diverse populations orchestrated extravagant civic pageantry, conducted triumphal processions, and reaffirmed their uncritical allegiance to the cosmic autocrat.\n\nStrikingly estranged from this collective euphoria, an assembly of indigenous anurans convened in clandestine, somber conclave within the subterranean recesses of an ancient peat fen. Confounded by this conspicuous refusal to synchronize with the public hysteria, an orthodox conformist interrogated their perceived cynicism: \"What pathological perversity compels this recalcitrant inertia, while the entirety of the terrestrial commonwealth enthusiastically ratifies the matrimonial ascension of our sovereign luminary?\"\n\nStepping forward with prophetic solemnity, a venerable amphibious patriarch delivered an uncompromising geopolitical and thermodynamic indictment. \"Your uncritical euphoria constitutes an appalling indictment of collective cognitive myopia,\" the elder articulated with resonant authority. \"Interrogate the thermodynamic parameters of our existing ecological predicament. Under the unilateral hegemony of a solitary solar furnace, our lacustrine and wetland habitats operate at the extreme periphery of biological tolerance. Even under current baseline parameters, seasonal thermal radiation ruthlessly desiccates our vernal wetlands, incinerates microclimatic moisture gradients, and coerces our entire population into subterranean estivation merely to avert lethal somatic desiccation.\n\nContemplate the apocalyptic ecological devastation should this astronomical despot successfully consummate a dynasty and populate the firmament with thermal progeny! The compounding radiative forcing generated by multiple solar entities will vaporize every terrestrial aquifer, boil pelagic reservoirs into atmospheric steam, and reduce the planetary hydrological cycle to complete thermodynamic entropy. Amphibious physiology, utterly dependent upon liquid ambient moisture, will suffer instantaneous and irrevocable extinction.\"\n\nIlluminated by this rigorous, unassailable thermodynamic calculus, the previously intoxicating spell of celebratory conformism instantaneously dissolved. Confronted by the undeniable reality that uncritical public celebration was actively validating the preliminary infrastructure of systemic ecocide, the assembled fauna terminated their festivities in silent dread.\n\nSubservient populaces habitually romanticize the dynastic proliferation of governing oligarchies, catastrophically oblivious to the immutable sociopolitical principle that the multiplication of oppressive authorities exponentially accelerates the systemic extermination of the governed.", "Classic_Original": "One hot summer, the Sun was about to take a wife. All the animals rejoiced at the news, and prepared to celebrate with great feasts. \n\nThe Frogs, however, were not among those who rejoiced. They croaked mournfully in their ponds, and lamented their hard fate. An old Toad, hearing their complaints, asked them why they mourned when all the rest of the world was glad. \n\n\"Alas!\" replied a wise Frog, \"if one Sun alone is able to scorch our pools and dry up the marshes, so that we have scarce room to live, what will become of us if he has children, and there are two or three Suns instead of one? The whole earth will be burnt up, and we shall all perish of thirst!\"\n\nRejoice not at that which will increase your burdens.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 28, "key": "ass_and_salt", "titleEn": "The Ass and the Load of Salt", "titleJa": "ロバと荷物", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_ass_and_salt.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A merchant bought some bags of salt at the seashore and put them on his donkey. They walked home together.\n\nOn their way, they had to cross a shallow river. The donkey slipped on a wet stone and fell into the water.\n\nWhen the donkey stood up, he was very surprised. The salt dissolved in the water, and his load became very light! The donkey was very happy.\n\nThe next day, the merchant bought salt again. When they reached the river, the donkey remembered the easy walk. He fell into the water on purpose. Again, the salt melted, and his bags became light.\n\nThe merchant saw the donkey's trick. He decided to teach him a lesson.\n\nThe next time, the merchant filled the bags with dry sponges. When they came to the river, the foolish donkey fell into the water again.\n\nThis time, the sponges absorbed a lot of water. The load became ten times heavier! The poor donkey could hardly walk at all.\n\nTricks do not work twice.", "Grade_3": "A merchant who dealt in salt loaded several heavy sacks onto his donkey and set out toward the market. On their journey, they arrived at a shallow stream which had to be crossed on foot.\n\nWhile wading through the stream, the donkey accidentally stumbled over a slippery rock and fell into the water. By the time he struggled back to his feet, much of the salt had completely dissolved. Finding his burden remarkably lighter, the donkey trotted home with great satisfaction.\n\nThe following day, when they reached the same stream, the clever beast decided to repeat the experience. He intentionally collapsed into the water. As expected, the salt melted away, allowing him to finish his journey without any difficulty.\n\nRealizing that he had been outsmarted by his animal, the merchant devised a clever plan to teach the donkey a lasting lesson.\n\nOn their next trip, instead of salt, the master packed the sacks with dry sponges. When they reached the middle of the stream, the foolish donkey deliberately dropped to his knees once more.\n\nHowever, the sponges immediately absorbed an enormous amount of water. When the beast attempted to rise, the load had become hopelessly heavy. Crushed beneath the unbearable weight, the donkey barely managed to crawl out of the river.\n\nThose who continually rely on petty tricks will eventually cause their own misfortune.", "Grade_Pre2": "Engaged in the lucrative commerce of unrefined mineral salt, an enterprising merchant laded his pack donkey with substantial burlap sacks and initiated his customary transit toward urban markets. Their standard trade route necessitated traversing a shallow river characterized by rapid currents and algae-encrusted riverbed stones.\n\nWhile negotiating the aquatic ford, the pack animal experienced an inadvertent loss of equilibrium, toppling sideways into the submerged boulders. By the time the drenched quadruped regained a stable footing, rapid chemical dissolution had eliminated the vast majority of the saline cargo. Astonished by the miraculous reduction in gravitational resistance, the donkey concluded the transit with unprecedented buoyancy and ease.\n\nErroneously extrapolating from this isolated phenomenon, the obstinate beast formulated a fallacious hypothesis: immersion in running water served as a universal mechanism for lightening burdens. Consequently, upon returning to the identical ford on subsequent expeditions, the beast executed a premeditated collapse into the stream, triumphantly reducing the merchant's profits while easing his own physical exertion.\n\nPerceiving the fraudulent strategy orchestrating these recurrent accidents, the indignant merchant formulated a sophisticated pedagogical countermeasure. Prior to their subsequent expedition, he substituted the saline contents with porous, dehydrated marine sponges, ensuring the cargo remained deceptive in its initial lightweight state.\n\nUpon arriving at the midstream ford, the complacent donkey enthusiastically enacted his rehearsed stratagem, submerging himself beneath the surface. However, rather than dissolving, the capillary microstructure of the sponges aggressively absorbed colossal volumes of liquid. When the beast attempted to elevate himself, he discovered to his utter horror that his burden had expanded exponentially into a lethal mass. Trapped beneath the saturated cargo, the gasping animal was nearly submerged before barely dragging his exhausted frame onto the opposite embankment.\n\nRelying mechanically upon fraudulent shortcuts inevitably produces catastrophic miscalculations when underlying circumstances undergo a fundamental transformation.", "Grade_2": "Operating within the commercial networks of the ancient Mediterranean littoral, an enterprising merchant specializing in the wholesale distribution of unrefined halite—mineral rock salt—laded his working beast of burden with substantial woven panniers containing the crystalline commodity. The standard logistics corridor connecting the coastal evaporation pans to inland municipal emporiums necessitated the negotiation of a natural fluvial ford characterized by hydraulic turbulence and slippery limestone strata.\n\nWhile traversing this aquatic obstacle, the quadruped suffered an accidental loss of traction, collapsing laterally into the rapid stream. During the temporal interval required for the animal to recover its footing, the thermodynamic properties of the aqueous solvent facilitated the rapid dissolution and dispersion of the highly soluble sodium chloride. Upon regaining an erect posture, the beast experienced an astonishing diminution of downward gravitational torque; concluding the itinerary with minimal metabolic expenditure, the animal erroneously deduced an uncalibrated general law of physics.\n\nEngaging in fundamentally flawed inductive reasoning, the donkey formulated an erroneous conceptual model: that immersion within an aquatic medium functioned as an axiomatic procedure for attenuating mechanical burdens. Consequently, on subsequent commercial transits, the animal deliberately executed rehearsed, fraudulent collapses into the fluvial current, systematically eroding the merchant's profit margins through manufactured cargo loss.\n\nDeciphering the pattern of calculated malingering behind these ostensible mishaps, the aggrieved merchant rejected corporal punishment, resolving instead to engineer a definitive pedagogical intervention. Exploiting the beast's flawed cognitive heuristics, the trader substituted the crystalline cargo with compressed, dehydrated marine sponges—a porous organic matrix displaying negligible baseline mass when dry.\n\nUpon approaching the midstream ford, the self-satisfied donkey initiated his premeditated immersion, anticipating instantaneous physical relief. However, rather than undergoing chemical dissolution, the sponge matrix exhibited rapid capillary absorption, vacuuming immense volumetric quantities of water into its internal cellular voids. When the beast attempted neuromuscular elevation, the compounded mass—now augmented by hundreds of liters of liquid saturation—rendered vertical ascension physically impossible. Pinned beneath this lethal kinetic deadweight, the suffocating quadruped was pushed to the absolute periphery of drowning before barely hauling his traumatized frame onto the littoral bank.\n\nMechanical adherence to behavioral shortcuts based on unexamined empirical precedents guarantees catastrophic operational failure whenever underlying systemic conditions undergo fundamental transformation.", "Grade_Pre1": "Navigating the mercantile trade networks of the Hellenistic Levant, an entrepreneurial merchant engaged in the wholesale procurement and logistics of unrefined mineral halite—crystallized sodium chloride—equipped his domesticated equine beast of burden with heavy wicker panniers charged with the mineral commodity. Their established mercantile trajectory linking coastal evaporation salterns to municipal consumer emporiums necessitated traversing a natural fluvial ford characterized by non-linear hydraulic turbulence, submerged boulders, and slick algae-coated limestone shoals.\n\nDuring the execution of this routine crossing, the quadruped experienced an abrupt catastrophic failure of mechanical traction, collapsing laterally into the churning rapids. In the temporal window necessitated for the animal to re-establish postural equilibrium, the thermodynamic solvent dynamics of the aquatic medium facilitated the rapid molecular dissolution and aqueous dispersion of the crystalline cargo. Upon regaining an erect stance, the animal experienced an astonishing diminution of downward gravitational torque; completing the itinerary with negligible metabolic exertion, the donkey formulated an uncalibrated, deeply fallacious inductive generalization regarding terrestrial mechanics.\n\nOperating under this epistemological distortion, the obstinate beast constructed an axiomatic conceptual heuristic: that immersion within an aqueous fluid functioned as an invariant mechanical protocol for attenuating somatic burdens. Consequently, upon approaching the identical ford during subsequent commercial expeditions, the animal deliberately orchestrated rehearsed, fraudulent collapses into the water, methodically eroding his proprietor’s fiscal profit margins through engineered asset liquidation while illicitly optimizing his own comfort.\n\nDeciphering the calculated pattern of malingering masking these ostensible mishaps, the aggrieved merchant eschewed crude corporal retribution, resolving instead to design an elegant pedagogical trap. Exploiting the animal's cognitive vulnerability and uncritical extrapolation, the merchant substituted the soluble crystalline cargo with dehydrated, compressed marine Porifera—a porous, organic sponge matrix manifesting minimal baseline mass in an unhydrated state.\n\nUpon entering the midstream ford, the complacent donkey executed his practiced plunge, fully anticipating instantaneous somatic relief. What transpired, however, constituted a catastrophic inversion of thermodynamic expectations: rather than dissolving into the solvent, the capillary microstructure of the sponges exhibited hyper-aggressive hygroscopic suction, vacuuming immense volumes of liquid into their cellular cavities. When the beast attempted neuromuscular elevation, the compounded burden—exponentially multiplied by total hydrostatic saturation—rendered vertical ascension structurally impossible. Trapped beneath an immovable mass of kinetic deadweight, the asphyxiating beast was brought to the absolute precipice of lethal submersion before barely hauling his traumatized, trembling frame onto the alluvial embankment.\n\nDogmatic adherence to behavioral heuristics grounded upon unexamined empirical anomalies invariably precipitates catastrophic operational failure when underlying systemic variables undergo radical, unannounced transformation.", "Classic_Original": "A Pedlar was driving an Ass to the seashore to buy salt. On their return, they came to a stream, which they had to cross. The Ass slipped and fell into the middle of the stream, and the salt was melted by the water, so that when the Ass got up again he found his load very much lighter. He was very much pleased with this. \n\nThe next time the Pedlar came to the same stream with a load of salt, the Ass intentionally fell down into the water. Again the salt melted, and he rose with a much lighter burden. \n\nThe Pedlar saw through the trick, and next time loaded him with sponges instead of salt. When they came to the stream, the Ass fell down on purpose once again. But the sponges became soaked with water, and so heavy that the Ass was unable to rise, and was drowned.\n\nThe same trick will not work twice.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 29, "key": "fox_and_woodman", "titleEn": "The Fox and the Woodman", "titleJa": "キツネと木こり", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_fox_and_woodman.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A fox was running through the forest. Some hunters and their dogs were chasing him closely.\n\nThe fox saw a woodman chopping wood outside his hut. \"Please help me!\" cried the fox. \"Hide me from the hunters!\"\n\nThe woodman pointed to his small hut. \"Go inside. You will be safe there,\" he said. The fox quickly ran in and hid in a dark corner.\n\nA few minutes later, the hunters arrived. They asked the woodman, \"Did you see a fox run past here?\"\n\nThe woodman replied loudly with his voice, \"No, I have not seen any fox today!\" \n\nHowever, while he spoke, he pointed his finger toward his hut to show them where the fox was hiding.\n\nLuckily, the hunters did not notice his finger. They quickly rode away.\n\nThe fox came out of the hut and started to walk away silently.\n\nThe woodman shouted angrily, \"Are you leaving without saying thank you?\"\n\nThe fox turned around and answered, \"I would thank you if your hands were as honest as your words!\"\n\nActions show the real truth, not words.", "Grade_3": "A hunted fox, exhausted from fleeing a pack of ferocious hounds, desperately sought refuge in the deep woods. Coming upon a woodman who was busy splitting logs beside his cottage, the fox pleaded for mercy. \"Hide me, kind sir, for the hunters are right behind me!\"\n\nThe woodman offered shelter and directed him into his cabin. The fox immediately hurried inside and concealed himself behind a stack of firewood.\n\nMoments later, the hunters arrived on horseback and questioned the woodcutter. \"Have you happened to see a fox passing this way?\" they inquired.\n\nWith his voice, the woodman answered loudly and clearly, \"No, gentlemen, I have seen no sign of a fox in these parts.\" However, at the very same time, he secretly gestured with his hands and pointed his thumb toward the cabin door to betray the animal's hiding place.\n\nFortunately, the eager hunters failed to notice his subtle hand gestures and galloped off in another direction.\n\nSeeing that the peril had passed, the fox emerged from the cottage and proceeded on his journey without uttering a single word of thanks.\n\nThe woodman rebuked him indignantly, \"How ungrateful you are to depart without thanking the man who preserved your life!\"\n\nThe fox paused and replied calmly, \"If the deeds of your hands had matched the generosity of your words, I would have offered you my deepest gratitude.\"\n\nNever trust individuals whose actions directly contradict their spoken promises.", "Grade_Pre2": "Pushed to the verge of total physical collapse by a relentless pack of mounted huntsmen and tracking canines, a terrified fox sought desperate asylum within a secluded forest clearing. Intercepting an impoverished woodcutter engaged in hewing timber adjacent to his rustic dwelling, the panting fugitive implored his humanitarian intervention: \"Grant me concealment within your sanctuary, for my pursuers are rapidly closing the distance!\"\n\nSimulating benevolent hospitality, the woodman gestured toward his domestic quarters. The fugitive scrambled indoors expeditiously, secreting himself behind an extensive barricade of seasoned logs.\n\nWithin minutes, the equestrian huntsmen arrived, brandishing weapons and interrogating the laborer regarding the fugitive's trajectory. \"Did an exhausted fox traverse this clearing recently?\" the captain demanded.\n\nDisplaying remarkable duplicity, the peasant vocalized a vehement verbal denial: \"Under no circumstances, noble lords! I have witnessed neither track nor shadow of any predator throughout the morning.\" Simultaneously, however, the hypocrite executed subtle somatic gestures, repeatedly gesturing with his index finger and gesturing toward his interior threshold to betray the hidden animal.\n\nIn their haste to sustain the momentum of the pursuit, the impatient riders failed to decipher this covert non-verbal treachery and galloped precipitously down an adjacent ravine.\n\nAscertaining that immediate peril had subsided, the fox emerged from his hiding place and commenced his departure across the meadow without offering the customary courtesies of gratitude.\n\nOutraged by this perceived breach of etiquette, the woodcutter delivered a self-righteous denunciation: \"What despicable ingratitude to abandon your benefactor without acknowledging the individual who preserved your life!\"\n\nHalting at the perimeter of the clearing, the vulpine survivor delivered an incisive indictment: \"Had the conduct of your treacherous fingers corresponded to the apparent nobility of your tongue, I should have celebrated your magnanimity; however, where verbal fidelity is subverted by physical betrayal, silence is the only appropriate response.\"\n\nTrue integrity requires strict harmony between word and deed, for superficial assurances of goodwill are rendered meaningless by covert hostility.", "Grade_2": "Driven to the absolute perimeter of physiological exhaustion by an elite equestrian hunting detachment and specialized tracking hounds, a pursued vulpine fugitive sought emergency extraterritorial asylum within an isolated woodland perimeter. Encountering an impoverished forester engaged in manual timber fabrication beside a rustic cabin, the hyperventilating animal vocalized an urgent plea for humanitarian sanctuary: \"Conceal me within your domestic infrastructure, for my pursuers are rapidly eliminating my margin of evasion!\"\n\nExhibiting simulated benevolence, the laborer designated the interior of his dwelling as a protective enclave. The fugitive scrambled across the threshold, expeditiously secreting his body behind an extensive, structurally stable rampart of cured cordwood.\n\nMoments later, the armed equestrian vanguard descended upon the perimeter, brandishing weapons and initiating an aggressive interrogation regarding the fugitive's spatial trajectory. \"Did an exhausted carnivore traverse this clearing within recent minutes?\" the equestrian officer demanded.\n\nIn this pivotal confrontation, the forester operationalized a masterclass in semiotic duplicity. Verbally, the individual issued an unequivocal, vociferous repudiation: \"Under no circumstances, gentlemen! The surrounding perimeter has remained entirely undisturbed by predatory fauna throughout the day.\" Concurrently, however, the duplicitous agent executed a coordinated sequence of somatic signifiers: deliberately angling his torso, manipulating his ocular gaze, and repeatedly jerking his extended digit toward the entrance of his dwelling to betray the exact coordinates of the concealed animal.\n\nCritically, preoccupied with sustaining the forward kinetic momentum of the pursuit, the impatient huntsmen failed to decode this subtle kinesic treachery, interpreting the verbal utterance as definitive and galloping precipitously down an adjacent ravine.\n\nHaving verified the complete cessation of immediate danger, the fox emerged from the structural enclosure and commenced an unhurried departure across the clearing, intentionally withholding all conventional diplomatic expressions of gratitude.\n\nProfoundly scandalized by this apparent breach of moral reciprocity, the woodman vocalized an indignant denunciation: \"What contemptible ethical depravity to abandon your benefactor without offering formal acknowledgment to the very agent who preserved your existence!\"\n\nPausing at the boundary of the forest canopy, the vulpine analyst articulated an unanswerable philosophical verdict: \"Had the physical execution of your treacherous digits harmonized with the ostensible nobility of your spoken rhetoric, I should have consecrated your moral rectitude; however, where overt verbal benevolence is deliberately subverted by covert somatic sabotage, ethical protocol dictates that silence constitutes the only dignified response.\"\n\nAuthentic ethical integrity necessitates strict coherence between linguistic proclamation and empirical execution; verbal assurances of goodwill are completely invalidated when subverted by treacherous non-verbal conduct.", "Grade_Pre1": "Pushed to the precipitous boundary of cardiopulmonary collapse by a relentless detachment of mounted huntsmen and synchronized scent hounds, an exhausted vulpine fugitive sought urgent extraterritorial asylum within a remote clearing. Intercepting a solitary rustic forester occupied in splitting oak cordwood adjacent to his primitive hovel, the hyperventilating predator articulated an agonized plea for emergency sanctuary: \"Grant me immediate asylum within your domestic enclosure, for the canine vanguard has completely eliminated my perimeter of evasion!\"\n\nAffecting an attitude of philanthropic hospitality, the peasant gestured toward the portal of his cabin. Scrambling across the threshold with desperate agility, the fugitive secreted his trembling frame behind an expansive, structurally dense rampart of seasoned firewood.\n\nWithin minutes, the equestrian vanguard thundered into the clearing, their mounts lathered with foam and their weapons primed for kinetic intervention. The hunt master subjected the peasant to immediate interrogative pressure: \"Declare at once whether an exhausted vulpine specimen traversed this clearing during the preceding moments!\"\n\nIn this decisive crucible of interspecies ethics, the forester executed a textbook manifestation of performative duplicity. Verbally, the peasant vocalized an emphatic, unequivocal repudiation: \"Under no circumstances, noble lords! This precinct has witnessed zero predatory transit throughout the entirety of the morning.\" Simultaneously, however, the treacherous host deployed an elaborate choreography of covert somatic signifiers: subtly realigning his postural axis, directing his ocular gaze toward the doorway, and repeatedly manipulating his extended thumb in a surreptitious trajectory to pinpoint the fugitive's exact coordinates.\n\nFortuitously for the concealed animal, the huntsmen were entirely consumed by the imperative of maintaining operational momentum. Incapable of decoding this sophisticated layer of kinesic treason, the horsemen accepted the vocalized disclaimer as unproblematic empirical truth, spurring their mounts precipitously down a descending ravine.\n\nHaving rigorously established the complete cessation of proximate peril, the fox emerged from his wooden redoubt and initiated a deliberate, measured traversal across the meadow, pointedly omitting all conventional courtesies of verbal acknowledgment.\n\nScandalized by this apparent violation of basic reciprocal etiquette, the peasant delivered a self-righteous ethical indictment: \"What unconscionable moral depravity to abandon your sanctuary without offering a single syllable of gratitude to the benefactor who preserved your biological existence!\"\n\nHalting at the perimeter of the arboreal canopy, the vulpine philosopher delivered an intellectually devastating counter-critique: \"Had the treacherous kinetic manifestations of your digits maintained fidelity with the apparent nobility of your vocal proclamations, I should have consecrated your philanthropic virtue; however, in a moral arena where overt rhetorical benevolence is systematically subverted by covert somatic treachery, ethical rigor dictates that absolute silence represents the sole legitimate and dignified response.\"\n\nAuthentic moral integrity demands rigorous intersubjective coherence between linguistic discourse and physical action; verbal proclamations of benevolence become utterly void of ethical legitimacy the precise instant they are betrayed by treacherous empirical conduct.", "Classic_Original": "A Fox, hard pressed by the Hounds, came across a Woodcutter, and begged him to hide him. The Woodcutter told him to go into his cottage. Shortly afterwards the Hounds and the Huntsmen arrived, and the Huntsmen asked the Woodcutter if he had seen the Fox. \n\n\"I have not seen him,\" said the Woodcutter aloud; but at the same time he pointed with his finger to the place where the Fox was hiding. The Huntsmen, however, did not understand the gesture, and went off in haste. \n\nThe Fox, when he saw them gone, came out without saying a word to the Woodcutter. The man reproached him, saying: \"Is this the way you thank me for saving your life?\" \n\nThe Fox replied: \"If your fingers had agreed with your tongue, I should have given you thanks; but your deeds contradicted your speech.\"\n\nActions speak louder than words.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}, {"chapter": 30, "key": "wolf_and_lamb", "titleEn": "The Wolf and the Lamb", "titleJa": "オオカミと子羊", "referenceImage": "images/vol1_wolf_and_lamb.png", "texts": {"Grade_4": "A small lamb was drinking water at a quiet stream. \n\nA hungry wolf walked to the stream. He saw the gentle lamb and wanted to eat her. However, he wanted an excuse to attack her.\n\nThe wolf walked upstream and shouted angrily, \"Why are you making my drinking water dirty?\"\n\nThe poor lamb looked up and said gently, \"Sir, the water flows from you down to me. I cannot make your water dirty.\"\n\nThe wolf had nothing to say to that, so he tried another excuse. \"Last year, you said terrible things about me!\"\n\nThe lamb replied, \"Sir, I was only born this spring. I was not even alive last year!\"\n\nThe wolf became furious. \"If it was not you, it must be your father!\" he roared.\n\nWith that shout, the wolf jumped on the helpless lamb and ate her.\n\nA wicked person will always find an excuse to do harm.", "Grade_3": "A little lamb was peacefully quenching its thirst beside a clear brook. Further upstream, a ravenous wolf emerged from the forest in search of prey. Desiring to devour the tender animal, yet wishing to justify his cruelty with a plausible excuse, the wolf approached with a fierce scowl.\n\n\"How dare you muddy the clean water that I am trying to drink?\" the wolf snarled menacingly.\n\nThe frightened lamb replied in a meek tone, \"Excuse me, noble sir, but the current flows downward from your position to mine. It is completely impossible for me to disturb the water upstream.\"\n\nFinding his first accusation easily disproved by logic, the wolf quickly invented another complaint. \"Last year, you insulted my character with slanderous words!\"\n\n\"That cannot be true,\" pleaded the lamb, trembling with fear, \"for I was not even born last year.\"\n\nRealizing that reason could not defeat truth, the tyrant dropped all pretenses of fairness. \"If it was not you, then it was certainly your father!\" roared the wolf. Without waiting for any reply, he seized the defenseless creature and devoured it instantly.\n\nTyrants will always devise excuses for cruelty, and innocence is no protection against brutal force.", "Grade_Pre2": "A vulnerable lamb was drinking peacefully along the lower embankment of an alpine rivulet, savoring the uncontaminated current. Concurrently, a predatory wolf emerged from the coniferous periphery upstream, acutely motivated by hunger. Harboring an immediate intention to butcher the herbivore, the predator nevertheless experienced a perverse psychological impulse: he sought to construct a veneer of legalistic legitimacy to rationalise unprovoked violence.\n\nInitiating hostilities with calculated indignation, the carnivore bellowed: \"How dare you contaminate my potable water by churning up riparian sediment with your insolent hooves?\"\n\nPerceiving the elementary hydrodynamics of the stream, the trembling lamb submitted an unassailable logical defense: \"Revered sir, simple observation demonstrates that the liquid current descends gravitationally from your elevated position toward my subordinate station; consequently, physical laws render it impossible for my actions to corrupt the upstream reservoir.\"\n\nDismayed to discover his initial indictment demolished by scientific reality, the despot instantly formulated an alternative grievance: \"Even if that is conceded, an identical period last autumn witnessed you disseminating malicious fabrications against my lineage!\"\n\nMounting a desperate factual rebuttal, the terrified juvenile stammered: \"That accusation is chronologically impossible, noble master, for my existence commenced merely six months ago; I had not yet been conceived during the timeframe you specify.\"\n\nConfronted with the utter futility of debating an innocent adversary whose rational arguments consistently exposed his bad faith, the tyrant discarded the theatrical pretense of procedural justice. \"If you yourself were not culpable, then your progenitor undeniably committed the offense, which justifies the identical retribution!\" the carnivore snarled. Terminating the discourse through unmitigated physical savagery, he sprang across the shallows and annihilated the defenseless victim.\n\nAuthoritarian tyrants will perpetually manufacture spurious pretexts to validate oppression, proving that rational argument provides no shield against unbridled brutality.", "Grade_2": "An innocent juvenile ovine was peacefully ingesting hydration along the subordinate riparian margin of a crystalline alpine stream. Concurrently, an apex apex carnivore—a mature wolf experiencing acute metabolic deprivation—emerged from the adjacent boreal timberline. Harboring an immediate predatory imperative to dismember the defenseless herbivore, the aggressor nevertheless manifested a psychological pathology common to authoritarian despots: an obsessive compulsion to drape unprovoked lethal violence in the procedural drapery of pseudo-legal justification.\n\nCommencing hostilities under simulated moral indignation, the predator bellowed across the current: \"By what intolerable audacity do you contaminate my potable hydration by aggressively churning up sedimentary particulate with your insolent hooves?\"\n\nObserving the elementary hydrological mechanics of the stream, the terrified lamb articulated an intellectually unassailable empirical defense: \"Honorable sovereign, empirical observation demonstrates that fluid dynamics compel the stream to descend gravitationally from your elevated riparian position toward my downstream station; consequently, Newtonian physics renders it structurally impossible for my subordinate activity to compromise your upstream water quality.\"\n\nHumiliated to discover his initial prosecutorial indictment instantaneously pulverized by elementary physics, the tyrant executed an immediate rhetorical shift, manufacturing an alternative fabricated grievance: \"Even if that hydrological reality is conceded, reliable intelligence confirms that precisely one calendar year ago, you orchestrated a malicious defamation campaign calculated to subvert my ancestral dignity!\"\n\nMounting a desperate chronological rebuttal, the trembling victim stammered: \"That accusation collapses under biological impossibility, noble master; my physical birth occurred merely six months ago, meaning that during the temporal window you allege, I had not yet entered physical existence.\"\n\nConfronted with the ultimate exhaustion of rhetorical expedients against an adversary whose factual innocence methodically stripped away his theatrical pretense of fairness, the despot unmasked his raw totalitarian impulse. Discarding all procedural jurisprudence, the carnivore snarled: \"If you yourself were biologically incapable of the offense, then your patriarchal progenitor undeniably executed the treachery, which ethically legitimizes your surrogate extermination!\" Terminating intellectual engagement through instantaneous kinetic savagery, the predator bounded across the shallows and pulverized the defenseless victim.\n\nAuthoritarian systems perpetually manufacture spurious legalistic pretexts to legitimize predatory violence; when absolute power collides with absolute truth, empirical logic constitutes zero defense against unmitigated institutional brutality.", "Grade_Pre1": "Drinking peacefully along the subordinate riparian embankment of an unpolluted alpine brook, an innocent juvenile ovine sought metabolic hydration from the crystalline current. Simultaneously, an apex canid carnivore—a mature timber wolf enduring acute caloric starvation—materialized from the adjacent coniferous timberline. While animated by an unyielding biological imperative to eviscerate the herbivore, the predator exhibited a perverse psychological syndrome quintessential to totalitarian despots: an intractable psychological compulsion to sanitize unprovoked, unilateral violence behind a facade of pseudo-jurisprudential legitimacy.\n\nInitiating hostilities with fabricated moral outrage, the carnivore vocalized a thunderous denunciation: \"By what intolerable insolence do you presume to contaminate my potable water by churning up alluvial sediments with your contemptible hooves?\"\n\nPerceiving the elementary hydrological dynamics of the riparian corridor, the terrified lamb articulated an intellectually unassailable defense grounded upon rigorous empirical observation: \"Revered master, elementary fluid mechanics demonstrate that the liquid gradient descends gravitationally from your elevated upstream position toward my subordinate downstream station. Consequently, the invariant laws of classical physics render it structural and operational nonsense to claim that my downstream activities could compromise your upstream reservoir.\"\n\nInfuriated to discover his initial prosecutorial indictment instantaneously pulverized by empirical science, the autocrat executed an instantaneous rhetorical pivot, improvising an alternative fabricated indictment: \"Even if that hydrological reality is conceded, historical intelligence confirms that precisely one calendar year ago, you disseminated malicious, defamatory fabrications designed to subvert my ancestral lineage!\"\n\nMounting a desperate chronological and biological rebuttal, the trembling victim articulated an absolute factual alibi: \"That indictment collapses beneath ontological impossibility, noble lord; my biological birth transpired merely six months prior to this encounter, definitively establishing that during the temporal interval you cite, I had not yet crossed the threshold into physical existence.\"\n\nConfronted with the utter collapse of his judicial pretense before an adversary whose transparent innocence systematically dismantled his theatrical affectations of justice, the tyrant unmasked the raw, undisguised brutality of authoritarian power. Discarding all procedural jurisprudence, the predator snarled: \"If you were chronologically disqualified from committing the transgression, then your patriarchal progenitor undeniably executed the treachery—a genealogical guilt that ethically legitimizes your surrogate extermination!\" Terminating all communicative discourse through instantaneous physical savagery, the carnivore vaulted across the alluvial shallows and pulverized the defenseless organism.\n\nAuthoritarian regimes perpetually fabricate spurious juridical pretexts to rationalize systemic oppression; when despotic hegemony collides with objective empirical truth, rational argumentation functions as a tragically impotent defense against unrestrained institutional violence.", "Classic_Original": "Once upon a time a Wolf was lapping at a spring on a hillside, when, looking up, what should he see but a Lamb just beginning to drink a little lower down. \n\n\"There's my supper,\" thought he, \"if only I can find some excuse to seize it.\" \n\nThen he called out to the Lamb: \"How dare you muddle the water from which I am drinking?\" \n\n\"Nay, master, nay,\" said the Lamb; \"if the water be muddy up there, I cannot be the cause of it, for it runs down from you to me.\" \n\n\"Well, then,\" said the Wolf, \"why did you insult me this time last year?\" \n\n\"Can't be,\" said the Lamb; \"I was not even born then.\" \n\n\"Well,\" snarled the Wolf, \"if it wasn't you, it was your father, and that's all the same to me.\" \n\nAnd without further words, he fell upon the poor Lamb and tore him to pieces.\n\nAny excuse will serve a tyrant.", "vocab": "", "moral": ""}}];
